{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639524751,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_K3GLNzEYRBJVxWweCGSY8502","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/CLAUDE.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/CLAUDE.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # [Project Name]\n2: \n3: <!--\n4: This is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\n5: manigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode (`mg --profile\n6: claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile opencode-go`) against the same\n7: project. Your docs/ directory is\n8: mounted at /workspace/.claude for Claude Code and /workspace/.opencode for\n9: OpenCode, and the same global agents are available under @name either way —\n10: custom project agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools too, written in\n11: the built-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...). To make a\n12: custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a `permission:` frontmatter block\n13: (see the manigot README's agent section).\n14: Keep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n15: -->\n16: \n17: Brief description of what this project does and who it's for.\n18: \n19: ## Stack\n20: - Backend:\n21: - Frontend:\n22: - Database:\n23: - Key packages:\n24: \n25: ## Architecture\n26: Describe the structure here — what lives where, what the key concepts are.\n27: The more specific you are about YOUR architecture, the less Claude guesses.\n28: \n29: ## Commands\n30: - `[test command]` — run tests\n31: - `[build command]` — build\n32: - `[dev command]` — start dev server\n33: \n34: ## Hard rules\n35: - NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n36: - NEVER run database migrations without showing them first\n37: - NEVER install packages without asking\n38: - NEVER touch [whatever is sensitive in this project] without flagging it\n39: - When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n40: - Do not refactor