{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639547237,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_xqEJgu8ffwklcgBNcPMg0400","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md","limit":40},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Assessment: funnel icon usage\n2: \n3: id: drama\n4: status: open\n5: date: 2026-08-16\n6: \n7: ## Summary\n8: \n9: The `funnel` icon (`@lucide/svelte/icons/funnel`) is used in **7 places** across the codebase. Exactly **one** of them is a semantically correct use of a funnel — the library filter button in `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`. The remaining **6** are all mobile navigation/drawer toggles, where the funnel icon is inappropriate: users reading a funnel expect \"filter this list\", but the button actually opens a navigation drawer/menu. This assessment recommends replacing every non-filter usage with a `menu` (hamburger) icon, which the codebase already ships as `HamburgerButton` (used by settings).\n10: \n11: ## 1. Where the funnel icon is used (full audit)\n12: \n13: ### 1.1 Direct `IconFunnel` renders (visible funnel icons)\n14: \n15: | # | File | Line(s) | Context | Kind |\n16: |---|------|---------|---------|------|\n17: | 1 | `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte` | 2, 15 | Floating circular button (`absolute`, `lg:hidden` = mobile-only), renders `<IconFunnel class=\"text-c-neutral-1\" />`. This is the icon *source* for every `FunnelButton` consumer. | Icon source for mobile toggles |\n18: | 2 | `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | 2, 60 | `<IconFunnel />` inside the libraries filter button; clicking opens the filter dropdown (genres, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe/plant filters, clear filters). | **True filter action** ✅ |\n19: \n20: ### 1.2 `FunnelButton` consumers (all mobile navigation toggles)\n21: \n22: | # | File | Line | Usage | Kind |\n23: |---|------|------|-------|------|\n24: | 3 | `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` | 31 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} top={3} />` — reveals the hidden feed list drawer on mobile (display block/none). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n25: | 4 | `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` | 34 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the address-book navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n26: | 5 | `src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` | 64 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} top={6} />` — opens the full-screen mobile todo navigation drawer (workspaces, categories, priority, status, effort, due, tags). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n27: | 6 | `src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` | 141 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the hidden time-tracking navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n28: | 7 | `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` | 44 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} />` — opens the full-screen mobile notes/categories navigation drawer. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n29: \n30: ### 1.3 Hamburger precedent (correct pattern already in the codebase)\n31: \n32: - `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/HamburgerButton.svelte` — byte-for-byte identical to `FunnelButton` except it renders `IconMenu` (`@lucide/svelte/icons/menu`) instead of `IconFunnel`.\n33: - `src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte` (lines 4, 24) — the settings mobile drawer already uses `HamburgerButton`. This is the exact scenario the other mobile drawers are in, done right.\n34: \n35: ### 1.4 Dead code: unused `IconFunnel` imports\n36: \n37: These files import `IconFunnel` but never render it (leftover from an earlier version that rendered the icon directly):\n38: \n39: - `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` — line 3\n40: - `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` — line 11\n\n(Showing lines 1-40 of 101. Use offset=41 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Assessment: funnel icon usage\n\nid: drama\nstatus: open\ndate: 2026-08-16\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `funnel` icon (`@lucide/svelte/icons/funnel`) is used in **7 places** across the codebase. Exactly **one** of them is a semantically correct use of a funnel — the library filter button in `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`. The remaining **6** are all mobile navigation/drawer toggles, where the funnel icon is inappropriate: users reading a funnel expect \"filter this list\", but the button actually opens a navigation drawer/menu. This assessment recommends replacing every non-filter usage with a `menu` (hamburger) icon, which the codebase already ships as `HamburgerButton` (used by settings).\n\n## 1. Where the funnel icon is used (full audit)\n\n### 1.1 Direct `IconFunnel` renders (visible funnel icons)\n\n| # | File | Line(s) | Context | Kind |\n|---|------|---------|---------|------|\n| 1 | `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte` | 2, 15 | Floating circular button (`absolute`, `lg:hidden` = mobile-only), renders `<IconFunnel class=\"text-c-neutral-1\" />`. This is the icon *source* for every `FunnelButton` consumer. | Icon source for mobile toggles |\n| 2 | `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | 2, 60 | `<IconFunnel />` inside the libraries filter button; clicking opens the filter dropdown (genres, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe/plant filters, clear filters). | **True filter action** ✅ |\n\n### 1.2 `FunnelButton` consumers (all mobile navigation toggles)","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md","text":"# Assessment: funnel icon usage\n\nid: drama\nstatus: open\ndate: 2026-08-16\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `funnel` icon (`@lucide/svelte/icons/funnel`) is used in **7 places** across the codebase. Exactly **one** of them is a semantically correct use of a funnel — the library filter button in `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`. The remaining **6** are all mobile navigation/drawer toggles, where the funnel icon is inappropriate: users reading a funnel expect \"filter this list\", but the button actually opens a navigation drawer/menu. This assessment recommends replacing every non-filter usage with a `menu` (hamburger) icon, which the codebase already ships as `HamburgerButton` (used by settings).\n\n## 1. Where the funnel icon is used (full audit)\n\n### 1.1 Direct `IconFunnel` renders (visible funnel icons)\n\n| # | File | Line(s) | Context | Kind |\n|---|------|---------|---------|------|\n| 1 | `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte` | 2, 15 | Floating circular button (`absolute`, `lg:hidden` = mobile-only), renders `<IconFunnel class=\"text-c-neutral-1\" />`. This is the icon *source* for every `FunnelButton` consumer. | Icon source for mobile toggles |\n| 2 | `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | 2, 60 | `<IconFunnel />` inside the libraries filter button; clicking opens the filter dropdown (genres, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe/plant filters, clear filters). | **True filter action** ✅ |\n\n### 1.2 `FunnelButton` consumers (all mobile navigation toggles)\n\n| # | File | Line | Usage | Kind |\n|---|------|------|-------|------|\n| 3 | `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` | 31 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} top={3} />` — reveals the hidden feed list drawer on mobile (display block/none). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 4 | `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` | 34 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the address-book navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 5 | `src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` | 64 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} top={6} />` — opens the full-screen mobile todo navigation drawer (workspaces, categories, priority, status, effort, due, tags). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 6 | `src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` | 141 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the hidden time-tracking navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 7 | `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` | 44 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} />` — opens the full-screen mobile notes/categories navigation drawer. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n\n### 1.3 Hamburger precedent (correct pattern already in the codebase)\n\n- `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/HamburgerButton.svelte` — byte-for-byte identical to `FunnelButton` except it renders `IconMenu` (`@lucide/svelte/icons/menu`) instead of `IconFunnel`.\n- `src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte` (lines 4, 24) — the settings mobile drawer already uses `HamburgerButton`. This is the exact scenario the other mobile drawers are in, done right.\n\n### 1.4 Dead code: unused `IconFunnel` imports\n\nThese files import `IconFunnel` but never render it (leftover from an earlier version that rendered the icon directly):\n\n- `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` — line 3\n- `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` — line 11","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":40,"totalLines":101,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md","time":{"start":1791639547187,"end":1791639547202}},"id":"prt_12609ecae001torygpvZCmVYSd","sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","messageID":"msg_12609e4610011Gnr7vGOlAytEp"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639547902,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_00_M31a2drbb50ruKaGvAGA3650","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"policy|best practice|convention|guideline","path":"/workspace/docs","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 16 matches\n/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/verdict.md:\n  Line 1: # Verdict: svelte best practices\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/tasks.md:\n  Line 1: # Tasks: svelte best practices\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/implementation.md:\n  Line 1: # Implementation: svelte best practices\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/brief.md:\n  Line 1: # Brief: svelte best practices\n\n  Line 11: Can you analyze our app repository and try to gather a policy set HOW we build stuff? Most of the app I've developed myself in a way that makes sense and adheres to best practices, is easy to read and easy to work with. When I let AI do stuff, it's sometimes okay, but sometimes meh. So I'd like to build a policy set of how to do things inside of solyto app, e.g. easy-to-read, specific state services, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested short-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on $derived, etc. Write it to docs/*.md.\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/client_skyrim-theme-transparency/implementation.md:\n  Line 35: `nav-mobile-container` convention):\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/client_skyrim-theme-transparency/tasks.md:\n  Line 38: the existing `nav-mobile-container` convention) to the three mobile-only drawer navigations.\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md:\n  Line 635: ### 5.6 Heading/spacing conventions\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/implementation.md:\n  Line 65:   convention. Move it if a top-level path was intended.\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/tasks.md:\n  Line 51: TASK-5: Audit visual and interaction consistency, and compare the feature's look-and-feel against sibling features and the shared UI kit: use of shared `forms/` controls vs. hand-rolled raw inputs (e.g. `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` duration and date inputs and `TimerWidget`'s description input vs. `TextInput`; `StatisticsView` date inputs), heading/spacing conventions, hover-only affordances (`group-hover` edit/delete in the nav) and touch/Mobile usability, color handling (hardcoded hex fallbacks `#1dbda5`, `#888`, `#9ca3af` across components), accessibility concerns (double-click-to-rename category, hover-revealed controls, icon-only buttons, color contrast of category chips), and i18n (unused keys such as `add_category`, `edit_category`, `color`, `duration_minutes`, `category`, `this_month`, and the unused `pomodoro_tip` feature-tip; verify all four locales stay in sync). This is the \"visually confusing and inconsistent\" part of the brief.\n\n  Line 63: - **Deliverable location:** the brief says \"the docs/ folder in the workspace\". There is no established top-level `docs/assessments/` convention; the closest precedent (`docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md`) places `assessment.md` inside the job directory. TASK-6 uses that location. If the author wanted a different top-level path (e.g. `docs/time-tracking-assessment.md`), that is a one-line change to TASK-6 — flag it in the implementation notes rather than guessing silently.\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/highlight_rename-category/verdict.md:\n  Line 13: notes: `updateCategory: API_URL + '/todos/categories/%d'` added to the `todos` section of `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts` (line 52), between `createCategory` and `deleteCategory`. Matches the brief's `PUT /api/v1/todos/categories/{category}`; `%d` matches the numeric-id convention of the sibling `deleteCategory` route and is correctly substituted by `ApiService.update` (`src/lib/services/ApiService.ts:61-70`, PUT + `%d` → `id.toString()`).\n\n  Line 36: All four tasks are implemented as specified and are consistent with the codebase's established patterns (KeyManager priorities, loadingIndicator, DeleteButton styling, i18n key handling, route/type conventions). Nothing found requires changes before merge. The TASK-5 note about not re-running npm checks here is an environment limitation, not a defect; the developer's verification claims are plausible and nothing in the diff contradicts them. Minor observations listed under TASK-4 (no error feedback, stale embedded todo titles, no try/finally around the loading indicator) are pre-existing house patterns and explicitly out of scope for this job.\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/lot_search-bar-overlays-buttons-in-libraries/verdict.md:\n  Line 22: ordering (`pointer-events-*` first) matches the dominant convention in the\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md:\n  Line 65: **Recommended replacement icon: `menu` (hamburger)** — via the existing `HamburgerButton` component, which is API-compatible with `FunnelButton` (`onclick`, `top`, `left` props) and already the convention for settings.\n\n  Line 69: - `align-justify` / `panel-left-open` — plausible menu glyphs, but `menu`/hamburger is the established convention in this app (settings) and the least surprising to users.\n","metadata":{"matches":16,"truncated":false},"title":"policy|best practice|convention|guideline","time":{"start":1791639547029,"end":1791639547895}},"id":"prt_12609ebf7001EyTnsaLxKPymuA","sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","messageID":"msg_12609e4610011Gnr7vGOlAytEp"}}
