r icon vs. deprecate in favor of `HamburgerButton`), and note the unused `IconFunnel` imports left behind in FeedNavigation.svelte, ContactNavigation.svelte, TodoNavigationMobile.svelte and TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte.\n18:      files: same list as TASK-1\n19:      depends: TASK-1\n20:      risk: medium — requires design judgment on icon semantics; the only clearly-correct funnel usage today is libraries/filters/Filter.svelte\n21: \n22: TASK-3: Verify that all proposed replacement icons exist in the pinned lucide version (`@lucide/svelte` 0.544.0) and record any that do not, so the assessment only recommends available icons.\n23:      files: package.json (version pin), node_modules/@lucide/svelte (icon availability check; no code changes)\n24:      depends: TASK-2\n25:      risk: low — verification only; note that node_modules is not installed in the worktree, so icon names must be confirmed against the lucide 0.544.0 icon set (e.g. via the published package listing) if present\n26: \n27: TASK-4: Write `assessment.md` documenting: where the funnel icon is used (with file references), where it makes sense (libraries filter button), where it does not (all mobile navigation/menu toggles), and the recommended replacement per location (with icon names). Do NOT change any source files — this job only produces the assessment document.\n28:      files: docs/jobs/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md\n29:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3\n30:      risk: low — documentation-only deliverable\n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: funnel icon assessment\n\nid: drama\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-08-16\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Audit and catalog every funnel icon usage in the codebase (direct `IconFunnel` renders, the `FunnelButton` component, and every component that consumes `FunnelButton`), recording file path, usage context, and whether the render is a filter action, a navigation/menu toggle, or decorative.\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte; src/lib/components/ui/buttons/HamburgerButton.svelte (precedent to note); src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte; src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte; src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte (hamburger precedent)\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — read-only grep audit, no behavior change\n\nTASK-2: Classify each funnel usage by semantic intent (true filter vs. mobile navigation drawer/menu toggle) and decide, per usage, whether the funnel icon is appropriate or should be replaced — with the concrete replacement icon (e.g. `menu`/hamburger via existing `HamburgerButton`, `list-filter`, `sliders-horizontal`) and the rationale. Include the recommendation for the `FunnelButton` component itself (repoint to hamburger icon vs. deprecate in favor of `HamburgerButton`), and note the unused `IconFunnel` imports left behind in FeedNavigation.svelte, ContactNavigation.svelte, TodoNavigationMobile.svelte and TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte.\n     files: same list as TASK-1\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — requires design judgment on icon semantics; the only clearly-correct funnel usage today is libraries/filters/Filter.svelte","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: funnel icon assessment\n\nid: drama\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-08-16\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Audit and catalog every funnel icon usage in the codebase (direct `IconFunnel` renders, the `FunnelButton` component, and every component that consumes `FunnelButton`), recording file path, usage context, and whether the render is a filter action, a navigation/menu toggle, or decorative.\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte; src/lib/components/ui/buttons/HamburgerButton.svelte (precedent to note); src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte; src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte; src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte (hamburger precedent)\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — read-only grep audit, no behavior change\n\nTASK-2: Classify each funnel usage by semantic intent (true filter vs. mobile navigation drawer/menu toggle) and decide, per usage, whether the funnel icon is appropriate or should be replaced — with the concrete replacement icon (e.g. `menu`/hamburger via existing `HamburgerButton`, `list-filter`, `sliders-horizontal`) and the rationale. Include the recommendation for the `FunnelButton` component itself (repoint to hamburger icon vs. deprecate in favor of `HamburgerButton`), and note the unused `IconFunnel` imports left behind in FeedNavigation.svelte, ContactNavigation.svelte, TodoNavigationMobile.svelte and TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte.\n     files: same list as TASK-1\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — requires design judgment on icon semantics; the only clearly-correct funnel usage today is libraries/filters/Filter.svelte\n\nTASK-3: Verify that all proposed replacement icons exist in the pinned lucide version (`@lucide/svelte` 0.544.0) and record any that do not, so the assessment only recommends available icons.\n     files: package.json (version pin), node_modules/@lucide/svelte (icon availability check; no code changes)\n     depends: TASK-2\n     risk: low — verification only; note that node_modules is not installed in the worktree, so icon names must be confirmed against the lucide 0.544.0 icon set (e.g. via the published package listing) if present\n\nTASK-4: Write `assessment.md` documenting: where the funnel icon is used (with file references), where it makes sense (libraries filter button), where it does not (all mobile navigation/menu toggles), and the recommended replacement per location (with icon names). Do NOT change any source files — this job only produces the assessment document.\n     files: docs/jobs/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3\n     risk: low — documentation-only deliverable","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":30,"totalLines":30,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791639573819,"end":1791639573951}},"id":"prt_1260a54dd001v4S6dEHQaI5114","sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","messageID":"msg_12609f0d5001TWQ6jEgOk0mtAL"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639574017,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_JZHpCoSDnacr45AhO3v84986","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: assessment: time tracking\n2: \n3: id: whom\n4: analyst: deepseek-flash\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Context\n10: \n11: The brief asks for a **thorough assessment** of the Time Tracking feature —\n12: what's good, what's bad, functionally and visually — written to the `docs/`\n13: folder. Following the precedent of the archived `drama_funnel-icon-assessment`\n14: job (the only other assessment job in this repo), the deliverable is a single\n15: document at `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md` (the job\n16: directory lives under `docs/`, which satisfies \"the docs/ folder in the\n17: workspace\"). This is an **assessment-only job: no source files are changed.**\n18: \n19: This repo is frontend-only; there is no backend to read. The authoritative\n20: contract for the data model is `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` plus\n21: `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts` (a `TimeTrackingProject` owns a many-to-many set\n22: of `TimeTrackingCategory`s; a `TimeTrackingEntry` belongs to exactly one\n23: project).\n24: \n25: The assessment must be evidence-based — every claim backed by file/line\n26: references — and must cover both **functional/IA** and **visual/consistency**\n27: angles, and must call out what already works well, not only problems.\n28: \n29: ## Task breakdown\n30: \n31: TASK-1: Audit the navigation and information architecture of Time Tracking: how `/time-tracking`, the `dashboard`/`entries` tabs, the per-project route `/time-tracking/[id]`, and the desktop/mobile navigation are structured, and how (or whether) view state is reflected in the URL (the active tab lives in the store's `$state`, both \"Dashboard\" and \"Entries\" nav links resolve to the same `urls.timeTracking` href and only mutate `activeTab`, so deep-linking/back-forward/reload do not restore the view). Document the project list/category-management affordances living inside the nav sidebar, the mobile drawer open/close mechanism (`style.display` toggle), and where each create/edit action is reachable. Compare against the navigation patterns used by other features (e.g. `todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte`, `notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, `calendar` views) to judge consistency.\n32:      files: src/routes/time-tracking/+layout.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/config/navigation.ts; src/lib/config/urls.ts\n33:      depends: none\n34:      risk: low — read-only structural audit; criteria are concrete (URL-driven vs state-driven navigation)\n35: \n36: TASK-2: Audit the data model and domain semantics against the brief's complaint that \"the data model doesn't feel intuitive (the way you add projects, categories, entries, etc.)\". Assess: global categories vs project-owned categories and the many-to-many `category_ids` linkage; entries requiring a `project_id` (no project-less/description-only entries, yet the UI has an `uncategorized` fallback path); recomputation of durations in components (`projectDurations`, `totalDuration`, breakdowns) despite the API exposing `project.total_duration` and `TimeTrackingStatistics`; the `has_exact_times` flag and the `date_range`/backdating semantics in `buildTimestamps()` (duration-only entries are anchored to *today's current wall-clock time*, so a past `date` cannot be honoured); how category colors are used (per-category color reused as the project's color in charts and breakdowns); and what the model makes easy vs. awkward for the user. Treat `types/time_tracking.ts` and `apiRoutes.ts` as the contract (no backend in this repo).\n37:      files: src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts; src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts; src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts\n38:      depends: none\n39:      risk: medium — the core of the brief's complaint; requires judgement on model intuitiveness, not just enumeration\n40: \n41: TASK-3: Audit the create/edit/manage flows and CRUD interactions for friction and inconsistency: `ProjectCreate` (create + edit via one modal), `EntryCreate`, and `EntryEdit` (which duplicates ~90% of `EntryCreate` and instead of `EntryCreate`), inline category add/rename (double-click, non-discoverable) and inline color picking in the nav, delete affordances (project delete confirms on the detail page via `ConfirmationModal` but is immediate/unconfirmed in the nav sidebar; category delete is immediate; entry delete is immediate), and where editing is and is not available (entries are editable from the Entries list but not from the dashboard \"recent entries\" or the project-detail page, whose `Entry` only shows delete). Note validation gaps (e.g. save silently no-ops when duration is 0 / no project) and the default-to-first-project behaviour in `TimerWidget`/`EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit`.\n42:      files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/ProjectCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/GroupedEntries.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n43:      depends: TASK-2\n44:      risk: low — concrete, file-by-file flow walkthrough\n45: \n46: TASK-4: Audit the timer, dashboard, and statistics surfaces: the start/stop timer (`TimerWidget`, `ActiveTimer`), the client-only `PomodoroWidget` (a fourth timer concept that is not persisted and does not create or link to a time entry — inconsistent with the feature's purpose), the `DashboardView` composition (Timer, Pomodoro, Today, This-Week widgets plus recent entries plus full statistics all stacked on one page), `TimeBreakdownWidget`'s project grouping (uses first category color, falls back to hardcoded `#9ca3af`), `StatisticsView` (embedded in the dashboard rather than its own tab/route; category filter filters *projects* by their categories; raw `<input type=\"date\">` with bespoke styling), and the dashboard-shell `TimeTrackingWidget` (duplicates the week-breakdown grouping logic from `DashboardView`). Assess whether timer state is honest (single active timer derived from `entries.find(stopped_at === null)`) and whether the dashboard answers the questions a user actually has.\n47:      files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimerWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/ActiveTimer.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/PomodoroWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeBreakdownWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget.svelte\n48:      depends: none\n49:      risk: low — read-only behavioural audit of self-contained widgets\n50: \n51: TASK-5: Audit visual and interaction consistency, and compare the feature's look-and-feel against sibling features and the shared UI kit: use of shared `forms/` controls vs. hand-rolled raw inputs (e.g. `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` duration and date inputs and `TimerWidget`'s description input vs. `TextInput`; `StatisticsView` date inputs), heading/spacing conventions, hover-only affordances (`group-hover` edit/delete in the nav) and touch/Mobile usability, color handling (hardcoded hex fallbacks `#1dbda5`, `#888`, `#9ca3af` across components), accessibility concerns (double-click-to-rename category, hover-revealed controls, icon-only buttons, color contrast of category chips), and i18n (unused keys such as `add_category`, `edit_category`, `color`, `duration_minutes`, `category`, `this_month`, and the unused `pomodoro_tip` feature-tip; verify all four locales stay in sync). This is the \"visually confusing and inconsistent\" part of the brief.\n52:      files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/i18n/en.ts; src/lib/i18n/de.ts; src/lib/i18n/es.ts; src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n53:      depends: none\n54:      risk: medium — design/consistency judgement; findings must stay evidence-based (cite component + line) rather than subjective\n55: \n56: TASK-6: Write `assessment.md` in the job directory, synthesising TASK-1–5 into a single, coherent, evidence-based report: an executive summary with the headline verdict on what's good and what's broken; sections for information architecture/navigation, data model, CRUD/edit flows, timer/dashboard/statistics, and visual/consistency + accessibility/i18n; per issue, the concrete file/line reference and a suggested direction (not code); and a prioritised list of recommended follow-up changes (ranked, with effort/impact noted) so a future implementation job can pick them up. Explicitly state that no source files were changed (assessment-only), consistent with the brief and the `drama` precedent. Re-read the final document once for factual accuracy against the code before finishing.\n57:      files: docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md\n58:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n59:      risk: low — documentation-only deliverable\n60: \n61: ## Notes / open questions\n62: \n63: - **Deliverable location:** the brief says \"the docs/ folder in the workspace\". There is no established top-level `docs/assessments/` convention; the closest precedent (`docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md`) places `assessment.md` inside the job directory. TASK-6 uses that location. If the author wanted a different top-level path (e.g. `docs/time-tracking-assessment.md`), that is a one-line change to TASK-6 — flag it in the implementation notes rather than guessing silently.\n64: - **No source changes.** Per the brief this is an assessment, not a refactor; implementations of any recommendation are out of scope and should become separate jobs.\n65: - **No render report / screenshots exist for this job** (checked `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/screenshots/`), so the visual claims must be grounded in the component/template source, not in rendered screenshots.\n\n(End of file - total 65 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: assessment: time tracking\n\nid: whom\nanalyst: deepseek-flash\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe brief asks for a **thorough assessment** of the Time Tracking feature —\nwhat's good, what's bad, functionally and visually — written to the `docs/`\nfolder. Following the precedent of the archived `drama_funnel-icon-assessment`\njob (the only other assessment job in this repo), the deliverable is a single\ndocument at `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md` (the job\ndirectory lives under `docs/`, which satisfies \"the docs/ folder in the\nworkspace\"). This is an **assessment-only job: no source files are changed.**\n\nThis repo is frontend-only; there is no backend to read. The authoritative\ncontract for the data model is `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` plus","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/whom_assessment-time-tracking/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: assessment: time tracking\n\nid: whom\nanalyst: deepseek-flash\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe brief asks for a **thorough assessment** of the Time Tracking feature —\nwhat's good, what's bad, functionally and visually — written to the `docs/`\nfolder. Following the precedent of the archived `drama_funnel-icon-assessment`\njob (the only other assessment job in this repo), the deliverable is a single\ndocument at `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md` (the job\ndirectory lives under `docs/`, which satisfies \"the docs/ folder in the\nworkspace\"). This is an **assessment-only job: no source files are changed.**\n\nThis repo is frontend-only; there is no backend to read. The authoritative\ncontract for the data model is `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` plus\n`src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts` (a `TimeTrackingProject` owns a many-to-many set\nof `TimeTrackingCategory`s; a `TimeTrackingEntry` belongs to exactly one\nproject).\n\nThe assessment must be evidence-based — every claim backed by file/line\nreferences — and must cover both **functional/IA** and **visual/consistency**\nangles, and must call out what already works well, not only problems.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Audit the navigation and information architecture of Time Tracking: how `/time-tracking`, the `dashboard`/`entries` tabs, the per-project route `/time-tracking/[id]`, and the desktop/mobile navigation are structured, and how (or whether) view state is reflected in the URL (the active tab lives in the store's `$state`, both \"Dashboard\" and \"Entries\" nav links resolve to the same `urls.timeTracking` href and only mutate `activeTab`, so deep-linking/back-forward/reload do not restore the view). Document the project list/category-management affordances living inside the nav sidebar, the mobile drawer open/close mechanism (`style.display` toggle), and where each create/edit action is reachable. Compare against the navigation patterns used by other features (e.g. `todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte`, `notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, `calendar` views) to judge consistency.\n     files: src/routes/time-tracking/+layout.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/config/navigation.ts; src/lib/config/urls.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — read-only structural audit; criteria are concrete (URL-driven vs state-driven navigation)\n\nTASK-2: Audit the data model and domain semantics against the brief's complaint that \"the data model doesn't feel intuitive (the way you add projects, categories, entries, etc.)\". Assess: global categories vs project-owned categories and the many-to-many `category_ids` linkage; entries requiring a `project_id` (no project-less/description-only entries, yet the UI has an `uncategorized` fallback path); recomputation of durations in components (`projectDurations`, `totalDuration`, breakdowns) despite the API exposing `project.total_duration` and `TimeTrackingStatistics`; the `has_exact_times` flag and the `date_range`/backdating semantics in `buildTimestamps()` (duration-only entries are anchored to *today's current wall-clock time*, so a past `date` cannot be honoured); how category colors are used (per-category color reused as the project's color in charts and breakdowns); and what the model makes easy vs. awkward for the user. Treat `types/time_tracking.ts` and `apiRoutes.ts` as the contract (no backend in this repo).\n     files: src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts; src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts; src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — the core of the brief's complaint; requires judgement on model intuitiveness, not just enumeration\n\nTASK-3: Audit the create/edit/manage flows and CRUD interactions for friction and inconsistency: `ProjectCreate` (create + edit via one modal), `EntryCreate`, and `EntryEdit` (which duplicates ~90% of `EntryCreate` and instead of `EntryCreate`), inline category add/rename (double-click, non-discoverable) and inline color picking in the nav, delete affordances (project delete confirms on the detail page via `ConfirmationModal` but is immediate/unconfirmed in the nav sidebar; category delete is immediate; entry delete is immediate), and where editing is and is not available (entries are editable from the Entries list but not from the dashboard \"recent entries\" or the project-detail page, whose `Entry` only shows delete). Note validation gaps (e.g. save silently no-ops when duration is 0 / no project) and the default-to-first-project behaviour in `TimerWidget`/`EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit`.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/ProjectCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/GroupedEntries.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/routes/time-tracking/[id]/+page.svelte\n     depends: TASK-2\n     risk: low — concrete, file-by-file flow walkthrough\n\nTASK-4: Audit the timer, dashboard, and statistics surfaces: the start/stop timer (`TimerWidget`, `ActiveTimer`), the client-only `PomodoroWidget` (a fourth timer concept that is not persisted and does not create or link to a time entry — inconsistent with the feature's purpose), the `DashboardView` composition (Timer, Pomodoro, Today, This-Week widgets plus recent entries plus full statistics all stacked on one page), `TimeBreakdownWidget`'s project grouping (uses first category color, falls back to hardcoded `#9ca3af`), `StatisticsView` (embedded in the dashboard rather than its own tab/route; category filter filters *projects* by their categories; raw `<input type=\"date\">` with bespoke styling), and the dashboard-shell `TimeTrackingWidget` (duplicates the week-breakdown grouping logic from `DashboardView`). Assess whether timer state is honest (single active timer derived from `entries.find(stopped_at === null)`) and whether the dashboard answers the questions a user actually has.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimerWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/ActiveTimer.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/PomodoroWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeBreakdownWidget.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/components/dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget.svelte\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — read-only behavioural audit of self-contained widgets\n\nTASK-5: Audit visual and interaction consistency, and compare the feature's look-and-feel against sibling features and the shared UI kit: use of shared `forms/` controls vs. hand-rolled raw inputs (e.g. `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` duration and date inputs and `TimerWidget`'s description input vs. `TextInput`; `StatisticsView` date inputs), heading/spacing conventions, hover-only affordances (`group-hover` edit/delete in the nav) and touch/Mobile usability, color handling (hardcoded hex fallbacks `#1dbda5`, `#888`, `#9ca3af` across components), accessibility concerns (double-click-to-rename category, hover-revealed controls, icon-only buttons, color contrast of category chips), and i18n (unused keys such as `add_category`, `edit_category`, `color`, `duration_minutes`, `category`, `this_month`, and the unused `pomodoro_tip` feature-tip; verify all four locales stay in sync). This is the \"visually confusing and inconsistent\" part of the brief.\n     files: src/lib/components/time-tracking/DashboardView.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryCreate.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/EntryEdit.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/Entry.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte; src/lib/components/time-tracking/StatisticsView.svelte; src/lib/i18n/en.ts; src/lib/i18n/de.ts; src/lib/i18n/es.ts; src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — design/consistency judgement; findings must stay evidence-based (cite component + line) rather than subjective\n\nTASK-6: Write `assessment.md` in the job directory, synthesising TASK-1–5 into a single, coherent, evidence-based report: an executive summary with the headline verdict on what's good and what's broken; sections for information architecture/navigation, data model, CRUD/edit flows, timer/dashboard/statistics, and visual/consistency + accessibility/i18n; per issue, the concrete file/line reference and a suggested direction (not code); and a prioritised list of recommended follow-up changes (ranked, with effort/impact noted) so a future implementation job can pick them up. Explicitly state that no source files were changed (assessment-only), consistent with the brief and the `drama` precedent. Re-read the final document once for factual accuracy against the code before finishing.\n     files: docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n     risk: low — documentation-only deliverable\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- **Deliverable location:** the brief says \"the docs/ folder in the workspace\". There is no established top-level `docs/assessments/` convention; the closest precedent (`docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md`) places `assessment.md` inside the job directory. TASK-6 uses that location. If the author wanted a different top-level path (e.g. `docs/time-tracking-assessment.md`), that is a one-line change to TASK-6 — flag it in the implementation notes rather than guessing silently.\n- **No source changes.** Per the brief this is an assessment, not a refactor; implementations of any recommendation are out of scope and should become separate jobs.\n- **No render report / screenshots exist for this job** (checked `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/screenshots/`), so the visual claims must be grounded in the component/template source, not in rendered screenshots.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":65,"totalLines":65,