{"type":"text","timestamp":1791639630613,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","part":{"id":"prt_1260b2a71001AxrSvxq0rX5Cho","messageID":"msg_1260b2244001GG9TWcmNTzvn3S","sessionID":"ses_ed9f6a1a9ffeKSNlfjObVylAL2","type":"text","text":"I've written the task list to `docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/tasks.md`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe brief asks for a **policy set of how code is built in solyto** (readable, DRY, small functions, lean components, no nested short-ifs, disciplined `$derived`, specific state services), written to `docs/*.md`. I read the brief, an existing precedent job (`whom_assessment-time-tracking`), and the real code (`Todos.svelte.ts`, `Clipboard.svelte.ts`, `Viewpoint.svelte.ts`, `+layout.svelte`, `Title.svelte`, `AddButton.svelte`, `Counter.svelte`, plus `TESTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `eslint.config.js`, `.prettierrc`, `package.json`) so the policy tasks are grounded in actual idioms rather than generic Svelte advice.\n\n**Deliverable:** a small, focused set of top-level docs in `docs/` (not one monolith):\n- `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` — entry point + general in-file principles\n- `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — the `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer\n- `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the component/routes UI layer\n- `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — services, helpers, config, types, i18n, data flow\n\n**Tasks (6):**\n- **TASK-1** `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` (general principles + index) — no deps\n- **TASK-2** `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — depends on TASK-1\n- **TASK-3** `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — depends on TASK-1\n- **TASK-4** `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — depends on TASK-1\n- **TASK-5** short \"Coding policies\" pointer in `docs/AGENTS.md` (flagged judgment call) — depends on TASK-1–4\n- **TASK-6** consistency/accuracy pass — depends on TASK-2–5\n\nAll are low risk (documentation-only; explicit \"no `src/` changes\"). Two things I flagged rather than guessed: the **doc layout** (split into four files is my analyst decision under the brief's \"policy set … `docs/*.md`\", trivially mergeable to one) and the **AGENTS.md pointer** (a small extension the author can drop). I also noted that `docs/TESTING.md` should be referenced, not duplicated.\n\nOne caveat: this environment had no shell, so I could not run `git branch --show-current` to independently verify the branch. `brief.md` specifies `feature/cut_svelte-best-practices` and the mounted worktree is assumed to be on the job branch per the pipeline's guarantee — noted in the file. I did not need a human decision, so no `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` was required.","time":{"start":1791639628401,"end":1791639630598}}}
