 with defaults that preserve zero-arg construction** (`auth = getAuth()`, `apiService = auth.apiService`, `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()`) — contrast the preferred injectable style (`Todos`, `Clipboard` after the TESTING.md refactor) with the older field-initializer style and codify the preferred one; the `load()` + `loaded` flag convention; the **CRUD method pattern** (call `ApiService`, `if (res) await this.load()`, return boolean) and an explicit note that its repetitiveness is intentional, not something to \"DRY up\" with a generic helper; delegate pure logic to `services/` (e.g. `Todos` → `TodoFilterService`/`TodoSortingService`/`TodoGroupingService`/`TodoRelevanceService`); persistence via `LocalStorageService` with a `static readonly LS_*_KEY` (cite `Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`); use of `page` from `$app/state` and `browser` from `$app/environment` (guards!), plus lifecycle/`destroy()` cleanup (cite `Viewpoint`); stores may read other stores/translation (cite `QuickAdd`); read-only view state via getters (cite `Viewpoint`); what **not** to do (no markup/UI, no hardcoded API URLs, no inline `fetch` where `ApiService` exists, keep methods small). Cross-link `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` and `docs/DATA_LAYER.md`.\n     files: docs/STATE_SERVICES.md\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — documentation only; source is well understood from TASK files and the codebase.\n\nTASK-3: Write `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the policy for Svelte components (`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` `.svelte` files), grounded in real examples.\n     content: components are **lean** — read context stores once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">` (`const todos = getTodos();`) and delegate logic to the store/service; type props with `$props<{...}>()`; Svelte 5 syntax (event attributes like `onclick`, snippets, `{@render children?.()}`) — no Svelte 4 `on:click`/`createEventDispatcher`/`export let`; keep markup declarative and **extract non-trivial conditions into functions or boolean