 const;","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":348,"totalLines":348,"truncated":false}},"title":"src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts","time":{"start":1791639652859,"end":1791639652938}},"id":"prt_1260b88ec001MjxFJM24pbKpaF","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","messageID":"msg_1260b81cb001HYXJcdTcZE91pH"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791639653051,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"id":"prt_1260b8aad001tKxcrmoxAr03Lm","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"","messageID":"msg_1260b81cb001HYXJcdTcZE91pH","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":32621,"input":4047,"output":121,"reasoning":37,"cache":{"write":0,"read":28416}},"cost":0.000787098}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791639654521,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"id":"prt_1260b9073001SNNaJ0LS24BdB9","messageID":"msg_1260b8ab800177P3AEAgHH6DKl","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639655584,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_vaA0F0lKLOQFnoXC2AIP3609","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/TESTING.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/TESTING.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Test coverage plan\n2: \n3: How to build the best possible automated test coverage for the solyto frontend.\n4: \n5: Status of this document: proposal. Nothing here is implemented yet. The phases\n6: at the bottom describe the order of work; every phase that requires new\n7: dev-dependencies needs explicit approval before `npm install` (dependencies are\n8: pinned, `engine-strict=true`).\n9: \n10: ---\n11: \n12: ## 0. Implementation status\n13: \n14: Most of the plan below is now implemented. Current state (run `npm test`):\n15: \n16: - **678 tests** (53 files) across 3 Vitest projects: `unit` (node), `stores`\n17:   (node + store-mock setup), `components` (jsdom).\n18: - Coverage: `src/lib` at **~22.8% statements / ~29.2% functions / ~22.2%\n19:   lines** (up from 8.7% / 12.4%), against the whole of `src/lib` including\n20:   the 357 untested components and 37 stores. The remaining uncovered lines\n21:   cluster in the documented out-of-scope list (§8) — heavy/skip components\n22:   (echarts, TipTap, DnD, WebAuthn, electronAPI, …) and the boilerplate CRUD\n23:   stores — which is the intended \"complete enough\" state.\n24: - New devDeps (pinned): `@vitest/coverage-v8`, `jsdom`, `@testing-library/svelte`,\n25:   `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/dom`.\n26: - `vitest.config.ts` now uses `sveltekit()` + three projects; `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts`\n27:   registers module mocks (ApiService/Auth/LocalStorageService/`$app/state`) for the\n28:   `stores` project only, so service-boundary tests keep the real implementations.\n29: - `Todos` and `Finances` state classes received a constructor-injection refactor\n30:   (auth/apiService/localStorage), defaulting to current behaviour. Other stores\n31:   are tested without source changes via the store mocks.\n32: - Component tests run in jsdom with `resolve.conditions: ['browser']` (needed so\n33:   `svelte` resolves to the client build, not SSR) and an `Element.prototype.animate`\n34:   stub in `tests/setup/component.ts` for Svelte transitions.\n35: \n36: ### Covered so far\n37: \n38: - **Pure logic (Phase 1):** `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`,\n39:   `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, `TodoFilterService` gaps\n40:   (`filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'`), `CheckInHelper`,\n41:   `CheckInSummaryHelper`, `ColorHelper`, `FormatHelper`, `NameHelper`, full\n42:   `DateHelper` gap coverage, `NumberHelper.europeanFormat`, all `MusicTheory/*`,\n43:   `themes.ts`, `confetti.ts`.\n44: - **Service boundary (Phase 2):** `ApiService` (fetch seam — headers, `%s`/`%d`\n45:   replacement, method/body semantics, error paths), `LocalStorageService`,\n46:   `NavHelper`, `platform.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n47: - **Stores (Phase 3):** `Todos`, `Finances`, `Tags`, `UserManagement`,\n48:   `TimeTracking`, `LoadingIndicator`, `CookieConsent`, `UiNotifications`,\n49:   `Calendars` (42-day grid, per-date lookups, month/week/day navigation,\n50:   view-state persistence), `Auth` (login/register/refresh/passkey,\n51:   load-from-localStorage, `isAdmin`, `shouldRefresh` threshold, public-profile\n52:   cache — in `tests/unit/auth/` because the stores project's storeMocks\n53:   replaces the Auth module), `Notes` (newest/updated/favorites, category\n54:   lookup/titles, collapsed persistence, `selectNote`, url-active check,\n55:   create guards), all 8 library stores' **filtering** (search,\n56:   genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags,\n57:   view-pref persistence, LinkLibrary category counts), `CheckInData`\n58:   (month navigation with year wrap, `isCurrentMonth`, date-derived\n59:   `selectedDate`, scored-trackers persistence, settings merge).\n60: - **Auth-token workflow regression:** `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`\n61:   pins the token snapshot semantics — `new Todos()`/`new Finances()` capture\n62:   `auth.getToken()` into their `ApiService` at construction (and send it as a\n63:   Bearer header), guarding the store-construction ordering workflow described\n64:   in §0's Docker note's sibling docs.\n65: - **Components (Phase 4a):** forms (`Checkbox`, `TextInput`, `Toggle`, `Select`),\n66:   ui primitives (`Heading`, `Badge`, `CloseButton`, `DeleteButton`, `AddButton`,\n67:   `ViewSwitcher`), `todos/Counter`, and logic leaves (`AverageNumber`, `Rating`,\n68:   `StatisticWidget`).\n69: - **Context harness (§4.3):** `tests/components/helpers/context.ts` +\n70:   `ContextHarness.svelte` seed `setTranslation`, `setKeyManager`, `setTodos`,\n71:   `setAuth`, `setLoadingIndicator`, `setUiNotifications`, `setViewPoint`,\n72:   `setCookieConsent` before rendering — unlocks the context-coupled component\n73:   tests below. `tests/setup/component.ts` additionally stubs\n74:   `Element.prototype.animate` (completing `onfinish`), `matchMedia` and the\n75:   `$env/dynamic/public` virtual module.\n76: - **Components (Phase 4b/4c):** dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`,\n77:   `ScoredTodosWidget`, `EventsTodayWidget`, `UpcomingEventsWidget`,\n78:   `NewestNotesWidget`, `NewestLinksWidget`, `BookReleasesWidget`,\n79:   `MovieReleasesWidget`, `MusicReleasesWidget`, `QuoteWidget`), logic-bearing\n80:   leaves (`forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`, `forms/Slider`,\n81:   `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon` + `check-in/overview/CheckInIcon`,\n82:   `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`,\n83:   `libraries/shared/CoverImage`), and translation-only components\n84:   (  `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`,\n85:   `ui/CookieBanner`, `NavLegalEntry`, `PopupConfirmationModal`,\n86:   `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `ImportButton` + 8 provider variants:\n87:   Goodreads/Hardcover/Bgg/Steam/Deezer/Discogs/Imdb/Chefkoch).\n88: - **Secondary stores (TASK-11):** `Feeds` (loadMore pagination/recursion,\n89:   filter, library flags, subscribe duplicates), `Contacts` (`contactsAZ`\n90:   grouping/sorting/hidden books, search, photo batching), `Navigation`\n91:   (usage tracking, `promoteMobileItem` least-used swap), `QuickAdd`\n92:   (detect/auto-confirm/error branches, `isUrl`), `UserNotifications`\n93:   (unread, mark-all-read, polling with fake timers), `WelcomeTour` (step\n94:   building, navigation), `Theme` (load/apply/persist, dark-mode listener,\n95:   `patchAnimate` — with document/window/Element stubs), `PwaInstall`\n96:   (capture/install flow, iOS detection).\n97: \n98: ### Not yet covered\n99: \n100: The refined next-steps roadmap (§8, Priority 1–3 and the execution order) is\n101: now implemented: state stores with real business logic (including the\n102: secondary stores `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `Navigation`, `QuickAdd`,\n103: `UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme`, `PwaInstall`), the context\n104: harness, dashboard widgets, logic-bearing leaves and the translation-only\n105: components. What remains untested is deliberately out of scope (see §8): the\n106: heavy/skip component list (§4d — echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD,\n107: svelte-gestures, WebAuthn, electronAPI, clipboard API, canvas), render-only\n108: components, and the remaining boilerplate CRUD store wrappers (`Clipboard`,\n109: `DevRequests`, `Friends`, `LibraryNavigation`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`,\n110: `Weather`). E2E (Phase 5) is deliberately out of scope for now — see §8.\n111: \n112: ### Docker decision\n113: \n114: The frontend does **not** get an API-style test image. The backend's one-shot\n115: `test` container exists because PHP needs `pcov` and only ever runs in Docker;\n116: the frontend test suite is 100% in-process (mocked fetch), so a test container\n117: would add orchestration with zero isolation — and the compose bind-mount of\n118: `../app/:/app` means a test container runs the host's `node_modules` anyway.\n119: Frontend tests run on the host via Vitest. Docker only enters at the future\n120: integration/E2E layer, which needs the full stack up (api/nginx at `:8000`).\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 1. Current state\n125: \n126: - Vitest 4.1.8 with `environment: 'node'`, `env: { TZ: 'UTC' }`, `$lib` alias,\n127:   `include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts']`.\n128: - 74 passing tests in 4 files, all **pure functions**:\n129:     - `tests/helpers/DateHelper.test.ts`, `tests/helpers/NumberHelper.test.ts`\n130:     - `tests/services/TodoFilterService.test.ts`, `tests/services/TodoSortingService.test.ts`\n131: - No component tests, no state-store tests, no E2E tests. `@testing-library/svelte`,\n132:   `jsdom`/`happy-dom`, Playwright, and coverage tooling are not installed.\n133: \n134: ### Two blockers that gate everything (empirically verified)\n135: \n136: 1. **`.svelte.ts` files cannot be imported in the current Vitest config.**\n137:    Importing any `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` throws `ReferenceError: $state is\n138: not defined`, because the Svelte compiler plugin is not active in Vitest.\n139:    Verified with a throwaway test against `LoadingIndicator.svelte.ts`.\n140: 2. **`$app/*` and `$env/*` modules are unresolvable** (no SvelteKit aliases),\n141:    unless each test `vi.mock`s them. `$env/dynamic/public` is imported at\n142:    module load by `src/lib/config/platform.ts`, so it blocks everything\n143:    transitively (e.g. `apiRoutes.ts`).\n144: \n145: Verified working recipe: adding `@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte` to the Vitest\n146: config compiles runes in `.svelte.ts`, and `vi.mock`ing `$app/state`,\n147: `$app/environment`, `$env/dynamic/public`, `$lib/state/Auth.svelte`,\n148: `$lib/services/ApiService`, and `$lib/services/LocalStorageService` lets the\n149: state classes be instantiated and tested in node. (Confirmed: `new Todos()`\n150: works under that recipe.)\n151: \n152: ### Architecture facts that shape the strategy\n153: \n154: - **Pure client-side-rendered SPA.** There are zero `load` functions, no\n155:   `+server.ts`, no `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts`, no `hooks.server.ts`, no\n156:   `*.server.*` files anywhere in `src/routes`. All data is fetched in\n157:   `onMount` handlers that call `.load()` on state stores.\n158: - **Data flow:** component → state store (`src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`) →\n159:   `ApiService` (`src/lib/services/ApiService.ts`) → REST API at\n160:   `${getApiUrl()}/api/v1` (`http://localhost:8000` in dev). `ApiService` is a\n161:   single fetch choke point — one seam to stub for the entire app.\n162: - **Stores are Svelte-context singletons:** 37 runes classes, created in\n163:   `src/routes/+layout.svelte` via `setX()`, read back via `getX()`.\n164:     - 29 of 37 call `getAuth()` at **class-field initialisation** (so even\n165:       `new X()` fails without a mocked Auth module or injected auth).\n166:     - 28 construct `new ApiService(...)` internally; 12 construct\n167:       `new LocalStorageService()`; 8 construct `new LibraryFilterService()`.\n168:     - 5 use `page` from `$app/state` (CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation,\n169:       Notes, Todos); 3 use `browser` from `$app/environment`.\n170:     - `QuickAdd` additionally reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()`.\n171: - **No DI anywhere:** stores build their own services in the constructor.\n172:   Field initializers run _before_ the constructor body, so adding constructor\n173:   parameters alone is not enough — the initializer must move into the\n174:   constructor (see §4).\n175: - **Service worker** (`src/service-worker.ts`) precaches the app shell and\n176:   uses stale-while-revalidate, but explicitly skips `/api` GETs. It does not\n177:   affect API mocking; it can serve stale shell during E2E runs and should be\n178:   blocked/cleared there.\n179: - The only type modules with runtime values are `src/lib/types/check_in.ts`\n180:   and `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts`; all other type files are erased at compile\n181:   time.\n182: \n183: ---\n184: \n185: ## 2. Strategy: a four-layer test pyramid\n186: \n187: The most coverage per effort, in order:\n188: \n189: ```\n190:                ┌─────────────┐\n191:                │  E2E (later)│  Playwright, mocked API — a few happy paths\n192:                └─────────────┘\n193:             ┌─────────────────────┐\n194:             │ Component (jsdom)   │  @testing-library/svelte — pure leaves,\n195:             │  + integration      │  then context-harnessed feature tests\n196:             └─────────────────────┘\n197:          ┌────────────────────────────┐\n198:          │  Unit: state stores        │  node + module mocks (+ small DI refactor)\n199:          └────────────────────────────┘\n200:       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐\n201:       │  Unit: pure logic (helpers,       │  node — biggest cheap win\n202:       │  services, config, ApiService)    │\n203:       └───────────────────────────────────┘\n204: ```\n205: \n206: Layer 1 and the pure part of layer 2 require **no new dependencies** (except a\n207: coverage reporter). Layers 2–4 require the infrastructure changes in §3.\n208: \n209: ---\n210: \n211: ## 3. Required infrastructure changes (enable first)\n212: \n213: ### 3.1 Fix the Vitest config (`vitest.config.ts`)\n214: \n215: Add the Svelte compiler plugin so `.svelte.ts` and `.svelte` files compile:\n216: \n217: ```ts\n218: import { sveltekit } from '@sveltejs/kit/vite';\n219: import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';\n220: \n221: export default defineConfig({\n222: \tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n223: \tresolve: { alias: { $lib: resolve('./src/lib') } },\n224: \ttest: {\n225: \t\tinclude: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'],\n226: \t\tenvironment: 'node',\n227: \t\tenv: { TZ: 'UTC' }\n228: \t}\n229: });\n230: ```\n231: \n232: - `sveltekit()` is the documented SvelteKit approach: it activates the Svelte\n233:   plugin (fixes `$state` in `.svelte.ts`) **and** makes `$app/*`/`$env/*`\n234:   resolvable, so most tests won't need to mock those.\n235: - Alternative if `sveltekit()` proves problematic in Vitest: use\n236:   `svelte({ compilerOptions: { runes: true } })` and `vi.mock` each `$app/*`\n237:   / `$env/*` module per test (verified working).\n238: - `$app/environment`'s `browser` flag may report `false` under node/jsdom\n239:   depending on the SvelteKit version — tests that need `browser === true`\n240:   (e.g. `LocalStorageService`) should force it:\n241:   `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true, dev: true }))`.\n242: \n243: ### 3.2 Add a jsdom project for component tests\n244: \n245: Vitest 4 supports `projects`. Add a second project so the existing node tests\n246: stay untouched:\n247: \n248: ```ts\n249: test: {\n250: \tprojects: [\n251: \t\t{ test: { include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'], environment: 'node' } },\n252: \t\t{\n253: \t\t\tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n254: \t\t\ttest: {\n255: \t\t\t\tinclude: ['tests/components/**/*.test.ts'],\n256: \t\t\t\tenvironment: 'jsdom',\n257: \t\t\t\tsetupFiles: ['tests/setup/component.ts']\n258: \t\t\t}\n259: \t\t}\n260: \t];\n261: }\n262: ```\n263: \n264: Component tests live under `tests/components/` and run in jsdom.\n265: \n266: ### 3.3 New dev-dependencies (all require approval before install)\n267: \n268: | Package                       | Purpose                                  | Version notes         |\n269: | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n270: | `@vitest/coverage-v8`         | `--coverage` reporting to drive the plan | match vitest 4.x      |\n271: | `jsdom`                       | DOM for component tests                  | latest                |\n272: | `@testing-library/svelte`     | render Svelte 5 components               | v5+ supports Svelte 5 |\n273: | `@testing-library/jest-dom`   | DOM matchers (`toBeInTheDocument`, ...)  | v6                    |\n274: | `@testing-library/user-event` | realistic clicks/typing                  | v14                   |\n275: | _(later)_ `@playwright/test`  | E2E layer                                | optional, phase 5     |\n276: \n277: ### 3.4 Test support code (`tests/` layout)\n278: \n279: ```\n280: tests/\n281:   setup/component.ts        # jest-dom import, localStorage/global stubs, cleanup\n282:   helpers/\n283:     factories.ts            # todo(), category(), tag(), checkIn() builders\n284:     context.ts              # renderWithContext(component, { stores }) — see §4.3\n285:     fetchMock.ts            # mockFetch(routes) + ApiService fake\n286:     localStorageMock.ts     # in-memory localStorage\n287:   unit/                     # node env: helpers, services, config, stores\n288:   components/               # jsdom env: component tests\n289: ```\n290: \n291: ---\n292: \n293: ## 4. Making the state layer testable (small refactor, big payoff)\n294: \n295: The stores hold most of the app's real logic (`Todos.useFilters`,\n296: `Todos.groupByStatus`, `Finances.getWealthSum`, library search/filter, ...) and\n297: are currently untestable because services are constructed internally and `auth`\n298: is a context read at field-init. The minimal, mechanical refactor:\n299: \n300: ```ts\n301: // before — field initializer runs before the constructor body\n302: export class Todos {\n303: \tauth = getAuth();\n304: \tapiService: ApiService;\n305: \tlocalStorage = new LocalStorageService();\n306: \tconstructor() {\n307: \t\tthis.apiService = new ApiService(this.auth.getToken());\n308: \t}\n309: }\n310: \n311: // after — everything injectable, defaults preserve current behaviour\n312: export class Todos {\n313: \tauth: Auth;\n314: \tapiService: ApiService;\n315: \tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n316: \tconstructor(\n317: \t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n318: \t\tapiService: ApiService = new ApiService(auth.getToken()),\n319: \t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n320: \t) {\n321: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n322: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n323: \t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n324: \t}\n325: }\n326: ```\n327: \n328: This applies to:\n329: \n330: - **28 stores** constructing `ApiService`: pass it in (Auth, Todos, Notes,\n331:   Calendars, Finances, Feeds, all 8 libraries, Contacts, CheckInData,\n332:   Clipboard, DevRequests, Friends, Shortcuts, Statistics, Tags, TimeTracking,\n333:   UserManagement, UserNotifications, Weather, Navigation, QuickAdd).\n334: - **12 stores** constructing `LocalStorageService` (incl. Auth, Theme,\n335:   CookieConsent).\n336: - **8 library stores** constructing `LibraryFilterService`.\n337: - **QuickAdd**: inject `ts`/`notifications` as well.\n338: - **Stores using `page` from `$app/state`**: keep reading `page` for now and\n339:   `vi.mock('$app/state')` in tests; or inject a `getPathname`/`page` for the\n340:   cleanest seams (only 5 stores; the constructor only reads path params, not a\n341:   live value).\n342: \n343: Scope guard: this refactor is mechanical and does not change behaviour. Do it\n344: only as far as tests need it (one store at a time), not as a bulk rewrite.\n345: \n346: ### 4.1 Standard unit-test recipe for a store\n347: \n348: ```ts\n349: vi.mock('$app/state', () => ({ page: { url: new URL('http://localhost/todos') } }));\n350: vi.mock('$lib/state/Auth.svelte', () => ({\n351:   getAuth: () => ({ getToken: () => 'test-token', /* …used methods */ })\n352: }));\n353: vi.mock('$lib/services/ApiService', () => ({\n354:   default: class FakeApi {\n355:     list = vi.fn(); get = vi.fn(); create = vi.fn();\n356:     update = vi.fn(); delete = vi.fn(); post = vi.fn(); put = vi.fn();\n357:   }\n358: }));\n359: \n360: const api = new (await import('$lib/services/ApiService')).default();\n361: const store = new Todos(/* mocked auth */, api as any, /* fake storage */);\n362: \n363: // test pure logic: set store.todos, call useFilters(), assert store.filteredTodos\n364: // test CRUD: api.list.mockResolvedValue({ data: [...] }); await store.load();\n365: ```\n366: \n367: Mock only the methods a given test exercises; `ApiService` methods return\n368: `null` by default (safe no-ops) unless stubbed.\n369: \n370: ### 4.2 Priority stores to test first (highest logic density)\n371: \n372: | Store                                                                                                                         | What to cover                                                                                                                                                                         |\n373: | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n374: | `Todos.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `useFilters` (backlog/hide-it/category/tag/auto-generated visibility), `groupByStatus`, `checkUrlForFilter`, `quickCreate` recurrence-ignore logic, `toggleSortByScore`, `loadHideIt` |\n375: | `Finances.svelte.ts`                                                                                                          | `getWealthSum`, `getBudgetTotal`, `getBudgetIncomeTotal`, `getBudgetExpenseTotal`, `getActivePage`, `loadIncome` income/expense split                                                 |\n376: | `Auth.svelte.ts`                                                                                                              | token refresh flow, `isAdmin`, login/register request bodies, persistence keys                                                                                                        |\n377: | `Calendars.svelte.ts`                                                                                                         | `loadMonth` date math, `getEventsForDate`, view state (skip the 3 direct `fetch` methods or stub global fetch)                                                                        |\n378: | Library stores (BookLibrary, MusicLibrary, MovieLibrary, GameLibrary, PlantLibrary, QuoteLibrary, RecipeLibrary, LinkLibrary) | search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, per-type `*View` prefs from localStorage                                                               |\n379: | `Notes.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                             |\n380: | `CheckInData.svelte.ts`, `TimeTracking.svelte.ts`, `UserManagement.svelte.ts`, `Tags.svelte.ts`                               | pure helpers (`formatDuration`, `filterUsers`, `sort`)                                                                                                                                |\n381: \n382: ### 4.3 Component test harness (context wrapper)\n383: \n384: Because components pull stores via `getX()`, provide a render helper that\n385: seeds context before rendering:\n386: \n387: ```ts\n388: import { render } from '@testing-library/svelte';\n389: \n390: export function renderWithContext(Component, props, stores = {}) {\n391: \t// wrapper component:\n392: \t//   setTranslation(mockTs); setKeyManager(mock); setTodos(mockTodos);\n393: \t//   setAuth(mockAuth); setLoadingIndicator(mock); setUiNotifications(mock);\n394: \t//   <Component {...props} />\n395: \t// store mocks = real store instances with apiService stubbed, or `vi.mock`ed modules\n396: }\n397: ```\n398: \n399: Build the wrapper once with the six most common stores (`Translation`,\n400: `KeyManager`, `Todos`, `Auth`, `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`) —\n401: unlocks ~250 context-coupled components.\n402: \n403: ---\n404: \n405: ## 5. Coverage roadmap (layered, in order)\n406: \n407: ### Phase 1 — Complete pure-logic unit tests (node, no new deps) ✅ high ROI\n408: \n409: Finish the untested pure modules. Current gaps:\n410: \n411: **Services**\n412: \n413: - `TodoGroupingService` — `groupByStatus` (untested, pure).\n414: - `TodoRelevanceService` — `getScoredTodos` (pure, uses `daysSince`; use fake timers/fixed date).\n415: - `LibraryFilterService` — `search`, `byRating`, `byGenre`, `byGenreAndRating`, `byType`, `byLocation`, `byUnidentified`, `byWishlist`, `byLent` (pure, type-only imports).\n416: - `WealthStatisticsService` — `getGraphValues` (pure; `SvelteDate` + `getUrlFormat`; fix the \"current date\" with fake timers).\n417: - `TodoFilterService` gaps — `filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'` case.\n418: \n419: **Helpers**\n420: \n421: - `CheckInHelper` — `getMeanValue`, `getTotalMeanValue`.\n422: - `CheckInSummaryHelper` — `buildDaySummary`, `buildPeriodSummary`, `getDayLabel`.\n423: - `ColorHelper` — `lightenColor`.\n424: - `FormatHelper` — `nl2br`, `markdownToHtml` (uses `marked`, node-safe).\n425: - `NameHelper` — `getInitials`.\n426: - `MusicTheoryHelper` + all 4 `MusicTheory/*` modules (ChordGenerator, NoteOperations, ScaleGenerator, TheoryConstants) — large pure surface, snapshot the constants.\n427: - `DateHelper` gaps (~14 functions): `formatDateWithWeekday`, `formatFloatingDate`, `getUrlFormat`, `getDaysInMonth`, `getLast30Days`, `getNextXDays`, `isDateThisWeek`, `isDateLast7Days`, `getCurrentTimestamp`, `getCurrentYearMonthString`, `getISODateInfo`, `getCalendarMonth`, `getCalendarWeek`, `dateFromTimestamp`.\n428: - `NumberHelper` gap — `europeanFormat`.\n429: \n430: **Config / effects**\n431: \n432: - `themes.ts` — pure data.\n433: - `effects/confetti.ts` — `createConfettiOptions` merges options (type-only import, pure).\n434: \n435: ### Phase 2 — Service boundary tests (node, tiny mocks)\n436: \n437: - `ApiService` — stub `globalThis.fetch` (`vi.stubGlobal`): assert `list/get/create/delete/update/post/put/postFormData/uploadFile` send the right method, URL (`%s`/`%d` replacement), headers (Bearer token present/absent, Content-Type for bodies), and return semantics on `ok`/error. This is the single most valuable test target — it is the only network seam.\n438: - `LocalStorageService` — `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true }))` + in-memory `localStorage` stub; assert get/set/getJson/getNumber/getBool/destroy round-trips and JSON parse-failure → null.\n439: - `NavHelper` — `vi.mock('$app/state')`; cover `getPageSlug`, `getPageFeature`, `showNavbar`, `isDashboard`, `isAdminRoute`, `isAuthRoute`, `isSetupRoute`.\n440: - `platform.ts` / `urls.ts` / `features.ts` / `navigation.ts` / `apiRoutes.ts` — `vi.mock('$env/dynamic/public')` + `$app/*` + `localStorage`; assert `getApiUrl` resolution order (env → hostname map → fallback), custom-API URL persistence, `PLATFORM`/`IS_NATIVE` flags. Use `vi.resetModules()` + fresh `$env` mocks for isolation.\n441: \n442: ### Phase 3 — State stores (node + module mocks, after §4 refactor)\n443: \n444: Apply the §4.1 recipe. Full inventory by group (37 files):\n445: \n446: | Group            | Stores                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Extra mocks needed                                                                                                                             |\n447: | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n448: | Root             | `Auth`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$env/dynamic/public`, ApiService, LocalStorageService                                                                                         |\n449: | No-auth (8)      | `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `PwaInstall`, `Viewpoint`, `CookieConsent`, `Theme`, `LibraryNavigation`                                                                                                                                                                                                           | `LoadingIndicator` testable as-is; `WelcomeTour`/`LibraryNavigation` need `urls`/`$app/state` mocks; `Theme` DOM methods need jsdom or adapter |\n450: | Auth+CRUD (21)   | `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `Finances`, `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `BookLibrary`, `MusicLibrary`, `MovieLibrary`, `GameLibrary`, `PlantLibrary`, `QuoteLibrary`, `RecipeLibrary`, `LinkLibrary`, `Clipboard`, `DevRequests`, `Friends`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`, `Tags`, `TimeTracking`, `UserManagement`, `UserNotifications`, `Weather` | Auth + ApiService (+ LocalStorageService for the 12 that use it)                                                                               |\n451: | `page` users (5) | CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation, Notes, Todos                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$app/state`                                                                                                                                   |\n452: | Special          | `QuickAdd` (3 contexts), `Navigation` (`$env/dynamic/public` + `auth.user.settings`), `Translation` (`browser` + `navigator.language`)                                                                                                                                                                                                   | per-file                                                                                                                                       |\n453: \n454: ### Phase 4 — Component tests (jsdom, after §3.2/§3.3)\n455: \n456: **4a. Pure/presentational leaves (~70, low effort).** No context, no `$app`:\n457: \n458: - `forms/` (11): Checkbox, DateInput, DateTimeInput, NumberInput, TextInput, Select, Slider, Toggle, SvelteDateInput, InputAutocomplete, InlineAutocomplete.\n459: - `ui/buttons/` (17): AcceptButton, AddButton, CloseButton, CloudButton, DeleteButton, EditButton, FunnelButton, HamburgerButton, IconButton, ImportButton, InlineDeleteButton, InlineEditButton, InlineExpandButton, RefreshButton, SaveButton, StarButton, TextButton.\n460: - `ui/icons/` (12), `ui/menus/` (2: MenuIcon, RightClickMenu), `ui/` primitives (~18): Badge, Card, Divider, File, Flag, Heading, SubHeading, ModalFormRow, Tabs, ViewSwitcher, NavEntry, NavEntryIcon, MovableHoverBox, HelpTooltip, LoadingLogo, StaggeredLogo, QuickSelectOverlay, PopupContentModal, BottomSheetModal, SlidingSideBar.\n461: - Feature leaves: `todos/Counter`, `check-in/` (DailyCheckInIcon, CheckInIcon, AverageNumber), `libraries/shared/` (Rating, CoverImage, MissingCover, GenreFlexList, ExternalSearchLink, BookRelease), `tags/TagFlexList`, `dev-requests/Author`, `guitar/GuitarTheoryNavigation`, `admin/StatisticWidget`, `notes/AddFolderButton`/`AddNoteButton`/`editor/ToolbarDivider`, `settings/SettingsSection` + SettingsNavigation*, `dashboard/widgets/*` (the props-driven ones: DueTodosWidget, ScoredTodosWidget, EventsTodayWidget, UpcomingEventsWidget, NewestNotesWidget, NewestLinksWidget, BookReleasesWidget, MovieReleasesWidget, MusicReleasesWidget, QuoteWidget).\n462: \n463: **4b. Translation-only components (~20).** Presentational but call `getTranslation()`; become trivial once the §4.3 harness exists: the `*ImportButton`/`*Button` icons, `NoTodos`, `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`, `ui/CookieBanner`, `PopupConfirmationModal`, `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `NavLegalEntry`.\n464: \n465: **4c. KeyManager + domain integration.** With `setKeyManager()`/`setTodos()`/`setAuth()`/`setLoadingIndicator()`/`setUiNotifications()`/`setViewPoint()` in the harness:\n466: \n467: - Todos feature: `views/{CardView,ListView,OverviewView}`, `props/*` (Category, DueDate, Effort, Flags, Link, Priority, Progress, Recurrence, Status, Subtasks, Tags, Title), `actions/{TodoCreate,TodoDelete,HideIt,SortByScore}`, `TodoNavigation*`, `ListAndAdd`.\n468: - Calendars: `views/{day,week,month,list}/*`, `NavigationEntry`, `MobileCalendarHeader`.\n469: - Dashboard: `YourDay`, `QuickGlance`, plus context widgets.\n470: - Libraries: shared `Entries/Header/Search/ShelfView/SpineView/CreateModal/DetailModal`.\n471: - Feeds, time-tracking, notes, check-in, settings, finances as capacity allows.\n472: \n473: **4d. Heavy/skip (~15 components).** Do not attempt in jsdom without heavy stubbing — exclude from automated coverage or stub their leaf dependencies:\n474: `charts/*` (echarts), `notes/editor/*` (TipTap/ProseMirror), `todos/views/KanbanView` (svelte-dnd-action), `ui/Notifications` (svelte-gestures), `settings/SecuritySettings` (simplewebauthn), `forms/{DatePicker,MultiSelect}` (datepicker/svelte-multiselect), `settings/{TagEdit,LocalizationSettings}`, `contacts/AddressBook*` (color picker, tzdb), dompurify/marked-rich components, `desktop/TitleBar` + `settings/UpdateChecker` (electronAPI), `clipboard/ClipboardList` (clipboard API), `tour/WelcomeTour`, `quick-add/QuickAddModal`. `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas) is likewise skipped or reduced to pure resize-math.\n475: \n476: ### Phase 5 — E2E (optional, later)\n477: \n478: If desired, Playwright against the real dev server with API responses mocked at\n479: `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/**` (or via a stub server). High-value flows:\n480: auth (email/password + WebAuthn virtual authenticator), todos CRUD, calendar\n481: month navigation, a library search. Must block/clear the service-worker cache\n482: (`serviceWorkers: 'block'` or `caches.delete()`) for deterministic runs.\n483: \n484: ---\n485: \n486: ## 6. Expected coverage & measurement\n487: \n488: - Use `@vitest/coverage-v8` with `npm run test:coverage`.\n489: - Treat coverage as a **signal, not a target**: after the §8 roadmap, the\n490:   remaining uncovered code should be the explicit out-of-scope list — third-party\n491:   wrappers, canvas/DOM-heavy leaves, and render-only components.\n492: - Keep the out-of-scope paths excluded (`exclude` in the coverage config) so\n493:   the number stays honest and comparable over time.\n494: - Re-measure after each priority and watch _where_ the uncovered lines are,\n495:   not the headline percentage. The number will stay modest while the 357\n496:   components and 37 stores exist, because most of them are intentionally not\n497:   tested (see §8).\n498: \n499: ## 7. Risks & caveats\n500: \n501: - **SvelteKit `$app/state` `page` object** in tests is a static mock; code that\n502:   reacts to `page` changes won't be exercised at unit level (fine — component\n503:   tests cover rendering paths).\n504: - **Run/effect timing:** stores use `setTimeout`/`tick`/`setInterval`\n505:   (`quickCreate`, `recentlyCreated`, `UserNotifications`, `Calendars`,\n506:   `Notes`). Use `vi.useFakeTimers()` and `flushSync`/`await tick()`.\n507: - **`SvelteDate` ignores `vi.setSystemTime`:** `svelte/reactivity`'s `SvelteDate`\n508:   captures the native `Date` at module load (in both the client and server\n509:   builds), so the fake-timer clock never reaches `new SvelteDate()` — it always\n510:   returns the real current time. Tests that exercise store code reading \"now\"\n511:   via `SvelteDate` (`Calendars` constructor/`goToToday`, `CheckInData`\n512:   initialisation/`isCurrentMonth`) must therefore assert against the real\n513:   `new Date()` on real timers, never against a hardcoded date — a hardcoded\n514:   \"today\" only passes on the day it was written.\n515: - **jsdom gaps:** `matchMedia`, `ResizeObserver`, `IntersectionObserver`,\n516:   `navigator.clipboard`, canvas 2D context need small stubs in\n517:   `tests/setup/component.ts`.\n518: - **i18n invariant:** when adding/verifying UI strings in component tests,\n519:   keep all four locales (`en/de/es/fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it.\n520: - **Pinned deps:** all additions must be pinned and installed only with\n521:   approval (AGENTS.md hard rule).\n522: - **Do not over-test third-party wrappers:** ECharts/TipTap/DnD behavior is the\n523:   library's responsibility; assert our props/logic, not their internals.\n524: \n525: ## 8. Next steps — where to invest next (current roadmap)\n526: \n527: Guiding rule: **test what has logic or a contract worth pinning; nothing else.**\n528: The 8.7% figure is low because the denominator is the whole of `src/lib` (357\n529: components, 37 stores), most of which is boilerplate or third-party wrappers.\n530: Raise it by testing the real logic — not by chasing a number.\n531: \n532: ### Priority 1 — State stores with real business logic (highest value)\n533: \n534: | Store                  | What is genuinely testable                                                                                                                                                                         |\n535: | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n536: | `Calendars`            | `loadMonth` (42-day grid math), `getEventsForDate`, month/week/day navigation, view state                                                                                                          |\n537: | `Auth`                 | login/register/refresh/passkey flows, load-from-localStorage, token-expiry branch, `isAdmin` — the security surface; the token-capture recipe is proven in `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts` |\n538: | `Notes`                | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                                          |\n539: | Library stores (all 8) | the **non-CRUD** parts: search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, view-pref persistence                                                                       |\n540: | `CheckInData`          | month navigation, date-derived `selectedDate`, scoring                                                                                                                                             |\n541: \n542: Do **not** test the ~20 boilerplate CRUD wrappers (`createX`/`updateX`/`deleteX`\n543: = call the API + reload). Prove the pattern once per store, then move on.\n544: \n545: ### Priority 2 — Presentational components _with logic_\n546: \n547: Most of the ~70 \"pure\" leaves (icons, logos, dividers) are render-only and not\n548: worth tests. Real value is in:\n549: \n550: - Keyboard/selection logic: `forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`,\n551:   `forms/Slider`.\n552: - State-driven leaves: `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon`/`CheckInIcon`,\n553:   `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`, `libraries/shared/CoverImage`.\n554: - Props-driven dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`, `ScoredTodosWidget`,\n555:   `UpcomingEventsWidget`, …) — data + handlers come in as props, making them the\n556:   cleanest integration targets in the app.\n557: - Translation-only components (~20 `*ImportButton`s, `NoTodos`, password\n558:   indicators) — only after Priority 3's harness exists.\n559: \n560: ### Priority 3 — Context harness (enabling investment)\n561: \n562: One `renderWithContext` helper that seeds `setTranslation()`, `setKeyManager()`,\n563: `setTodos()`, `setAuth()`, `setLoadingIndicator()`, `setUiNotifications()`,\n564: `setViewPoint()` before rendering (pattern in §4.3). This unlocks the ~250\n565: context-coupled components (todos views/props/actions, calendar views, dashboard)\n566: and the translation-only leaves. Without it, the mock boilerplate per component\n567: test is not worth the effort.\n568: \n569: ### Explicitly out of scope\n570: \n571: - Heavy/skip list (§4d): echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD (`KanbanView`),\n572:   svelte-gestures (`ui/Notifications`), WebAuthn (`SecuritySettings`),\n573:   `DatePicker`/`MultiSelect`, dompurify/marked-rich components, electronAPI\n574:   (`TitleBar`/`UpdateChecker`), clipboard API (`ClipboardList`).\n575: - `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas + `Image`).\n576: - Icons, logos, and other render-only components.\n577: - Third-party behavior — assert our props/logic, not ECharts/ProseMirror internals.\n578: - E2E/Playwright for now — a client-side SPA with a mocked API at the unit level\n579:   is already covered by store + component tests; E2E adds infrastructure for\n580:   marginal value.\n581: \n582: ### Execution order\n583: \n584: 1. [x] `Calendars` + `Auth` store tests (biggest logic; recipe proven) — TASK-1/TASK-2.\n585: 2. [x] `Notes` + library-store filtering tests — TASK-3/TASK-4 (+ `CheckInData`, TASK-5).\n586: 3. [x] §4.3 context harness — TASK-6.\n587: 4. [x] Dashboard widgets + logic-bearing leaves — TASK-7/TASK-8.\n588: 5. [x] Translation-only components — TASK-9.\n589: 6. [x] Re-run `npm run test:coverage` and inspect the remaining uncovered lines —\n590:    they cluster in the \"explicitly out of scope\" list above (plus the secondary\n591:    stores named in §0). The suite is \"complete enough\" rather than \"maximised\",\n592:    which is the goal.\n593: 7. [x] Optional follow-up: secondary stores with real non-CRUD logic — `Feeds`,\n594:    `Contacts`, `Navigation` (+ `PUBLIC_DISABLE_DEV_REQUESTS` env branch),\n595:    `QuickAdd`, `UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme` (DOM-stubbed),\n596:    `PwaInstall`. All landed in `tests/unit/stores/` and brought `lib/state`\n597:    statement coverage to ~56%.\n\n(End of file - total 597 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Test coverage plan\n\nHow to build the best possible automated test coverage for the solyto frontend.\n\nStatus of this document: proposal. Nothing here is implemented yet. The phases\nat the bottom describe the order of work; every phase that requires new\ndev-dependencies needs explicit approval before `npm install` (dependencies are\npinned, `engine-strict=true`).\n\n---\n\n## 0. Implementation status\n\nMost of the plan below is now implemented. Current state (run `npm test`):\n\n- **678 tests** (53 files) across 3 Vitest projects: `unit` (node), `stores`\n  (node + store-mock setup), `components` (jsdom).\n- Coverage: `src/lib` at **~22.8% statements / ~29.2% functions / ~22.2%\n  lines** (up from 8.7% / 12.4%), against the whole of `src/lib` including\n  the 357 untested components and 37 stores. The remaining uncovered lines","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/TESTING.md","text":"# Test coverage plan\n\nHow to build the best possible automated test coverage for the solyto frontend.\n\nStatus of this document: proposal. Nothing here is implemented yet. The phases\nat the bottom describe the order of work; every phase that requires new\ndev-dependencies needs explicit approval before `npm install` (dependencies are\npinned, `engine-strict=true`).\n\n---\n\n## 0. Implementation status\n\nMost of the plan below is now implemented. Current state (run `npm test`):\n\n- **678 tests** (53 files) across 3 Vitest projects: `unit` (node), `stores`\n  (node + store-mock setup), `components` (jsdom).\n- Coverage: `src/lib` at **~22.8% statements / ~29.2% functions / ~22.2%\n  lines** (up from 8.7% / 12.4%), against the whole of `src/lib` including\n  the 357 untested components and 37 stores. The remaining uncovered lines\n  cluster in the documented out-of-scope list (§8) — heavy/skip components\n  (echarts, TipTap, DnD, WebAuthn, electronAPI, …) and the boilerplate CRUD\n  stores — which is the intended \"complete enough\" state.\n- New devDeps (pinned): `@vitest/coverage-v8`, `jsdom`, `@testing-library/svelte`,\n  `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/dom`.\n- `vitest.config.ts` now uses `sveltekit()` + three projects; `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts`\n  registers module mocks (ApiService/Auth/LocalStorageService/`$app/state`) for the\n  `stores` project only, so service-boundary tests keep the real implementations.\n- `Todos` and `Finances` state classes received a constructor-injection refactor\n  (auth/apiService/localStorage), defaulting to current behaviour. Other stores\n  are tested without source changes via the store mocks.\n- Component tests run in jsdom with `resolve.conditions: ['browser']` (needed so\n  `svelte` resolves to the client build, not SSR) and an `Element.prototype.animate`\n  stub in `tests/setup/component.ts` for Svelte transitions.\n\n### Covered so far\n\n- **Pure logic (Phase 1):** `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`,\n  `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, `TodoFilterService` gaps\n  (`filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'`), `CheckInHelper`,\n  `CheckInSummaryHelper`, `ColorHelper`, `FormatHelper`, `NameHelper`, full\n  `DateHelper` gap coverage, `NumberHelper.europeanFormat`, all `MusicTheory/*`,\n  `themes.ts`, `confetti.ts`.\n- **Service boundary (Phase 2):** `ApiService` (fetch seam — headers, `%s`/`%d`\n  replacement, method/body semantics, error paths), `LocalStorageService`,\n  `NavHelper`, `platform.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- **Stores (Phase 3):** `Todos`, `Finances`, `Tags`, `UserManagement`,\n  `TimeTracking`, `LoadingIndicator`, `CookieConsent`, `UiNotifications`,\n  `Calendars` (42-day grid, per-date lookups, month/week/day navigation,\n  view-state persistence), `Auth` (login/register/refresh/passkey,\n  load-from-localStorage, `isAdmin`, `shouldRefresh` threshold, public-profile\n  cache — in `tests/unit/auth/` because the stores project's storeMocks\n  replaces the Auth module), `Notes` (newest/updated/favorites, category\n  lookup/titles, collapsed persistence, `selectNote`, url-active check,\n  create guards), all 8 library stores' **filtering** (search,\n  genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags,\n  view-pref persistence, LinkLibrary category counts), `CheckInData`\n  (month navigation with year wrap, `isCurrentMonth`, date-derived\n  `selectedDate`, scored-trackers persistence, settings merge).\n- **Auth-token workflow regression:** `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`\n  pins the token snapshot semantics — `new Todos()`/`new Finances()` capture\n  `auth.getToken()` into their `ApiService` at construction (and send it as a\n  Bearer header), guarding the store-construction ordering workflow described\n  in §0's Docker note's sibling docs.\n- **Components (Phase 4a):** forms (`Checkbox`, `TextInput`, `Toggle`, `Select`),\n  ui primitives (`Heading`, `Badge`, `CloseButton`, `DeleteButton`, `AddButton`,\n  `ViewSwitcher`), `todos/Counter`, and logic leaves (`AverageNumber`, `Rating`,\n  `StatisticWidget`).\n- **Context harness (§4.3):** `tests/components/helpers/context.ts` +\n  `ContextHarness.svelte` seed `setTranslation`, `setKeyManager`, `setTodos`,\n  `setAuth`, `setLoadingIndicator`, `setUiNotifications`, `setViewPoint`,\n  `setCookieConsent` before rendering — unlocks the context-coupled component\n  tests below. `tests/setup/component.ts` additionally stubs\n  `Element.prototype.animate` (completing `onfinish`), `matchMedia` and the\n  `$env/dynamic/public` virtual module.\n- **Components (Phase 4b/4c):** dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`,\n  `ScoredTodosWidget`, `EventsTodayWidget`, `UpcomingEventsWidget`,\n  `NewestNotesWidget`, `NewestLinksWidget`, `BookReleasesWidget`,\n  `MovieReleasesWidget`, `MusicReleasesWidget`, `QuoteWidget`), logic-bearing\n  leaves (`forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`, `forms/Slider`,\n  `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon` + `check-in/overview/CheckInIcon`,\n  `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`,\n  `libraries/shared/CoverImage`), and translation-only components\n  (  `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`,\n  `ui/CookieBanner`, `NavLegalEntry`, `PopupConfirmationModal`,\n  `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `ImportButton` + 8 provider variants:\n  Goodreads/Hardcover/Bgg/Steam/Deezer/Discogs/Imdb/Chefkoch).\n- **Secondary stores (TASK-11):** `Feeds` (loadMore pagination/recursion,\n  filter, library flags, subscribe duplicates), `Contacts` (`contactsAZ`\n  grouping/sorting/hidden books, search, photo batching), `Navigation`\n  (usage tracking, `promoteMobileItem` least-used swap), `QuickAdd`\n  (detect/auto-confirm/error branches, `isUrl`), `UserNotifications`\n  (unread, mark-all-read, polling with fake timers), `WelcomeTour` (step\n  building, navigation), `Theme` (load/apply/persist, dark-mode listener,\n  `patchAnimate` — with document/window/Element stubs), `PwaInstall`\n  (capture/install flow, iOS detection).\n\n### Not yet covered\n\nThe refined next-steps roadmap (§8, Priority 1–3 and the execution order) is\nnow implemented: state stores with real business logic (including the\nsecondary stores `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `Navigation`, `QuickAdd`,\n`UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme`, `PwaInstall`), the context\nharness, dashboard widgets, logic-bearing leaves and the translation-only\ncomponents. What remains untested is deliberately out of scope (see §8): the\nheavy/skip component list (§4d — echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD,\nsvelte-gestures, WebAuthn, electronAPI, clipboard API, canvas), render-only\ncomponents, and the remaining boilerplate CRUD store wrappers (`Clipboard`,\n`DevRequests`, `Friends`, `LibraryNavigation`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`,\n`Weather`). E2E (Phase 5) is deliberately out of scope for now — see §8.\n\n### Docker decision\n\nThe frontend does **not** get an API-style test image. The backend's one-shot\n`test` container exists because PHP needs `pcov` and only ever runs in Docker;\nthe frontend test suite is 100% in-process (mocked fetch), so a test container\nwould add orchestration with zero isolation — and the compose bind-mount of\n`../app/:/app` means a test container runs the host's `node_modules` anyway.\nFrontend tests run on the host via Vitest. Docker only enters at the future\nintegration/E2E layer, which needs the full stack up (api/nginx at `:8000`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Current state\n\n- Vitest 4.1.8 with `environment: 'node'`, `env: { TZ: 'UTC' }`, `$lib` alias,\n  `include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts']`.\n- 74 passing tests in 4 files, all **pure functions**:\n    - `tests/helpers/DateHelper.test.ts`, `tests/helpers/NumberHelper.test.ts`\n    - `tests/services/TodoFilterService.test.ts`, `tests/services/TodoSortingService.test.ts`\n- No component tests, no state-store tests, no E2E tests. `@testing-library/svelte`,\n  `jsdom`/`happy-dom`, Playwright, and coverage tooling are not installed.\n\n### Two blockers that gate everything (empirically verified)\n\n1. **`.svelte.ts` files cannot be imported in the current Vitest config.**\n   Importing any `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` throws `ReferenceError: $state is\nnot defined`, because the Svelte compiler plugin is not active in Vitest.\n   Verified with a throwaway test against `LoadingIndicator.svelte.ts`.\n2. **`$app/*` and `$env/*` modules are unresolvable** (no SvelteKit aliases),\n   unless each test `vi.mock`s them. `$env/dynamic/public` is imported at\n   module load by `src/lib/config/platform.ts`, so it blocks everything\n   transitively (e.g. `apiRoutes.ts`).\n\nVerified working recipe: adding `@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte` to the Vitest\nconfig compiles runes in `.svelte.ts`, and `vi.mock`ing `$app/state`,\n`$app/environment`, `$env/dynamic/public`, `$lib/state/Auth.svelte`,\n`$lib/services/ApiService`, and `$lib/services/LocalStorageService` lets the\nstate classes be instantiated and tested in node. (Confirmed: `new Todos()`\nworks under that recipe.)\n\n### Architecture facts that shape the strategy\n\n- **Pure client-side-rendered SPA.** There are zero `load` functions, no\n  `+server.ts`, no `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts`, no `hooks.server.ts`, no\n  `*.server.*` files anywhere in `src/routes`. All data is fetched in\n  `onMount` handlers that call `.load()` on state stores.\n- **Data flow:** component → state store (`src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`) →\n  `ApiService` (`src/lib/services/ApiService.ts`) → REST API at\n  `${getApiUrl()}/api/v1` (`http://localhost:8000` in dev). `ApiService` is a\n  single fetch choke point — one seam to stub for the entire app.\n- **Stores are Svelte-context singletons:** 37 runes classes, created in\n  `src/routes/+layout.svelte` via `setX()`, read back via `getX()`.\n    - 29 of 37 call `getAuth()` at **class-field initialisation** (so even\n      `new X()` fails without a mocked Auth module or injected auth).\n    - 28 construct `new ApiService(...)` internally; 12 construct\n      `new LocalStorageService()`; 8 construct `new LibraryFilterService()`.\n    - 5 use `page` from `$app/state` (CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation,\n      Notes, Todos); 3 use `browser` from `$app/environment`.\n    - `QuickAdd` additionally reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()`.\n- **No DI anywhere:** stores build their own services in the constructor.\n  Field initializers run _before_ the constructor body, so adding constructor\n  parameters alone is not enough — the initializer must move into the\n  constructor (see §4).\n- **Service worker** (`src/service-worker.ts`) precaches the app shell and\n  uses stale-while-revalidate, but explicitly skips `/api` GETs. It does not\n  affect API mocking; it can serve stale shell during E2E runs and should be\n  blocked/cleared there.\n- The only type modules with runtime values are `src/lib/types/check_in.ts`\n  and `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts`; all other type files are erased at compile\n  time.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Strategy: a four-layer test pyramid\n\nThe most coverage per effort, in order:\n\n```\n               ┌─────────────┐\n               │  E2E (later)│  Playwright, mocked API — a few happy paths\n               └─────────────┘\n            ┌─────────────────────┐\n            │ Component (jsdom)   │  @testing-library/svelte — pure leaves,\n            │  + integration      │  then context-harnessed feature tests\n            └─────────────────────┘\n         ┌────────────────────────────┐\n         │  Unit: state stores        │  node + module mocks (+ small DI refactor)\n         └────────────────────────────┘\n      ┌───────────────────────────────────┐\n      │  Unit: pure logic (helpers,       │  node — biggest cheap win\n      │  services, config, ApiService)    │\n      └───────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nLayer 1 and the pure part of layer 2 require **no new dependencies** (except a\ncoverage reporter). Layers 2–4 require the infrastructure changes in §3.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Required infrastructure changes (enable first)\n\n### 3.1 Fix the Vitest config (`vitest.config.ts`)\n\nAdd the Svelte compiler plugin so `.svelte.ts` and `.svelte` files compile:\n\n```ts\nimport { sveltekit } from '@sveltejs/kit/vite';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n\tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n\tresolve: { alias: { $lib: resolve('./src/lib') } },\n\ttest: {\n\t\tinclude: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'],\n\t\tenvironment: 'node',\n\t\tenv: { TZ: 'UTC' }\n\t}\n});\n```\n\n- `sveltekit()` is the documented SvelteKit approach: it activates the Svelte\n  plugin (fixes `$state` in `.svelte.ts`) **and** makes `$app/*`/`$env/*`\n  resolvable, so most tests won't need to mock those.\n- Alternative if `sveltekit()` proves problematic in Vitest: use\n  `svelte({ compilerOptions: { runes: true } })` and `vi.mock` each `$app/*`\n  / `$env/*` module per test (verified working).\n- `$app/environment`'s `browser` flag may report `false` under node/jsdom\n  depending on the SvelteKit version — tests that need `browser === true`\n  (e.g. `LocalStorageService`) should force it:\n  `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true, dev: true }))`.\n\n### 3.2 Add a jsdom project for component tests\n\nVitest 4 supports `projects`. Add a second project so the existing node tests\nstay untouched:\n\n```ts\ntest: {\n\tprojects: [\n\t\t{ test: { include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'], environment: 'node' } },\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n\t\t\ttest: {\n\t\t\t\tinclude: ['tests/components/**/*.test.ts'],\n\t\t\t\tenvironment: 'jsdom',\n\t\t\t\tsetupFiles: ['tests/setup/component.ts']\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t];\n}\n```\n\nComponent tests live under `tests/components/` and run in jsdom.\n\n### 3.3 New dev-dependencies (all require approval before install)\n\n| Package                       | Purpose                                  | Version notes         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `@vitest/coverage-v8`         | `--coverage` reporting to drive the plan | match vitest 4.x      |\n| `jsdom`                       | DOM for component tests                  | latest                |\n| `@testing-library/svelte`     | render Svelte 5 components               | v5+ supports Svelte 5 |\n| `@testing-library/jest-dom`   | DOM matchers (`toBeInTheDocument`, ...)  | v6                    |\n| `@testing-library/user-event` | realistic clicks/typing                  | v14                   |\n| _(later)_ `@playwright/test`  | E2E layer                                | optional, phase 5     |\n\n### 3.4 Test support code (`tests/` layout)\n\n```\ntests/\n  setup/component.ts        # jest-dom import, localStorage/global stubs, cleanup\n  helpers/\n    factories.ts            # todo(), category(), tag(), checkIn() builders\n    context.ts              # renderWithContext(component, { stores }) — see §4.3\n    fetchMock.ts            # mockFetch(routes) + ApiService fake\n    localStorageMock.ts     # in-memory localStorage\n  unit/                     # node env: helpers, services, config, stores\n  components/               # jsdom env: component tests\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Making the state layer testable (small refactor, big payoff)\n\nThe stores hold most of the app's real logic (`Todos.useFilters`,\n`Todos.groupByStatus`, `Finances.getWealthSum`, library search/filter, ...) and\nare currently untestable because services are constructed internally and `auth`\nis a context read at field-init. The minimal, mechanical refactor:\n\n```ts\n// before — field initializer runs before the constructor body\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth = getAuth();\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage = new LocalStorageService();\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tthis.apiService = new ApiService(this.auth.getToken());\n\t}\n}\n\n// after — everything injectable, defaults preserve current behaviour\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n\tconstructor(\n\t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n\t\tapiService: ApiService = new ApiService(auth.getToken()),\n\t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n\t) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis applies to:\n\n- **28 stores** constructing `ApiService`: pass it in (Auth, Todos, Notes,\n  Calendars, Finances, Feeds, all 8 libraries, Contacts, CheckInData,\n  Clipboard, DevRequests, Friends, Shortcuts, Statistics, Tags, TimeTracking,\n  UserManagement, UserNotifications, Weather, Navigation, QuickAdd).\n- **12 stores** constructing `LocalStorageService` (incl. Auth, Theme,\n  CookieConsent).\n- **8 library stores** constructing `LibraryFilterService`.\n- **QuickAdd**: inject `ts`/`notifications` as well.\n- **Stores using `page` from `$app/state`**: keep reading `page` for now and\n  `vi.mock('$app/state')` in tests; or inject a `getPathname`/`page` for the\n  cleanest seams (only 5 stores; the constructor only reads path params, not a\n  live value).\n\nScope guard: this refactor is mechanical and does not change behaviour. Do it\nonly as far as tests need it (one store at a time), not as a bulk rewrite.\n\n### 4.1 Standard unit-test recipe for a store\n\n```ts\nvi.mock('$app/state', () => ({ page: { url: new URL('http://localhost/todos') } }));\nvi.mock('$lib/state/Auth.svelte', () => ({\n  getAuth: () => ({ getToken: () => 'test-token', /* …used methods */ })\n}));\nvi.mock('$lib/services/ApiService', () => ({\n  default: class FakeApi {\n    list = vi.fn(); get = vi.fn(); create = vi.fn();\n    update = vi.fn(); delete = vi.fn(); post = vi.fn(); put = vi.fn();\n  }\n}));\n\nconst api = new (await import('$lib/services/ApiService')).default();\nconst store = new Todos(/* mocked auth */, api as any, /* fake storage */);\n\n// test pure logic: set store.todos, call useFilters(), assert store.filteredTodos\n// test CRUD: api.list.mockResolvedValue({ data: [...] }); await store.load();\n```\n\nMock only the methods a given test exercises; `ApiService` methods return\n`null` by default (safe no-ops) unless stubbed.\n\n### 4.2 Priority stores to test first (highest logic density)\n\n| Store                                                                                                                         | What to cover                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Todos.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `useFilters` (backlog/hide-it/category/tag/auto-generated visibility), `groupByStatus`, `checkUrlForFilter`, `quickCreate` recurrence-ignore logic, `toggleSortByScore`, `loadHideIt` |\n| `Finances.svelte.ts`                                                                                                          | `getWealthSum`, `getBudgetTotal`, `getBudgetIncomeTotal`, `getBudgetExpenseTotal`, `getActivePage`, `loadIncome` income/expense split                                                 |\n| `Auth.svelte.ts`                                                                                                              | token refresh flow, `isAdmin`, login/register request bodies, persistence keys                                                                                                        |\n| `Calendars.svelte.ts`                                                                                                         | `loadMonth` date math, `getEventsForDate`, view state (skip the 3 direct `fetch` methods or stub global fetch)                                                                        |\n| Library stores (BookLibrary, MusicLibrary, MovieLibrary, GameLibrary, PlantLibrary, QuoteLibrary, RecipeLibrary, LinkLibrary) | search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, per-type `*View` prefs from localStorage                                                               |\n| `Notes.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                             |\n| `CheckInData.svelte.ts`, `TimeTracking.svelte.ts`, `UserManagement.svelte.ts`, `Tags.svelte.ts`                               | pure helpers (`formatDuration`, `filterUsers`, `sort`)                                                                                                                                |\n\n### 4.3 Component test harness (context wrapper)\n\nBecause components pull stores via `getX()`, provide a render helper that\nseeds context before rendering:\n\n```ts\nimport { render } from '@testing-library/svelte';\n\nexport function renderWithContext(Component, props, stores = {}) {\n\t// wrapper component:\n\t//   setTranslation(mockTs); setKeyManager(mock); setTodos(mockTodos);\n\t//   setAuth(mockAuth); setLoadingIndicator(mock); setUiNotifications(mock);\n\t//   <Component {...props} />\n\t// store mocks = real store instances with apiService stubbed, or `vi.mock`ed modules\n}\n```\n\nBuild the wrapper once with the six most common stores (`Translation`,\n`KeyManager`, `Todos`, `Auth`, `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`) —\nunlocks ~250 context-coupled components.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Coverage roadmap (layered, in order)\n\n### Phase 1 — Complete pure-logic unit tests (node, no new deps) ✅ high ROI\n\nFinish the untested pure modules. Current gaps:\n\n**Services**\n\n- `TodoGroupingService` — `groupByStatus` (untested, pure).\n- `TodoRelevanceService` — `getScoredTodos` (pure, uses `daysSince`; use fake timers/fixed date).\n- `LibraryFilterService` — `search`, `byRating`, `byGenre`, `byGenreAndRating`, `byType`, `byLocation`, `byUnidentified`, `byWishlist`, `byLent` (pure, type-only imports).\n- `WealthStatisticsService` — `getGraphValues` (pure; `SvelteDate` + `getUrlFormat`; fix the \"current date\" with fake timers).\n- `TodoFilterService` gaps — `filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'` case.\n\n**Helpers**\n\n- `CheckInHelper` — `getMeanValue`, `getTotalMeanValue`.\n- `CheckInSummaryHelper` — `buildDaySummary`, `buildPeriodSummary`, `getDayLabel`.\n- `ColorHelper` — `lightenColor`.\n- `FormatHelper` — `nl2br`, `markdownToHtml` (uses `marked`, node-safe).\n- `NameHelper` — `getInitials`.\n- `MusicTheoryHelper` + all 4 `MusicTheory/*` modules (ChordGenerator, NoteOperations, ScaleGenerator, TheoryConstants) — large pure surface, snapshot the constants.\n- `DateHelper` gaps (~14 functions): `formatDateWithWeekday`, `formatFloatingDate`, `getUrlFormat`, `getDaysInMonth`, `getLast30Days`, `getNextXDays`, `isDateThisWeek`, `isDateLast7Days`, `getCurrentTimestamp`, `getCurrentYearMonthString`, `getISODateInfo`, `getCalendarMonth`, `getCalendarWeek`, `dateFromTimestamp`.\n- `NumberHelper` gap — `europeanFormat`.\n\n**Config / effects**\n\n- `themes.ts` — pure data.\n- `effects/confetti.ts` — `createConfettiOptions` merges options (type-only import, pure).\n\n### Phase 2 — Service boundary tests (node, tiny mocks)\n\n- `ApiService` — stub `globalThis.fetch` (`vi.stubGlobal`): assert `list/get/create/delete/update/post/put/postFormData/uploadFile` send the right method, URL (`%s`/`%d` replacement), headers (Bearer token present/absent, Content-Type for bodies), and return semantics on `ok`/error. This is the single most valuable test target — it is the only network seam.\n- `LocalStorageService` — `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true }))` + in-memory `localStorage` stub; assert get/set/getJson/getNumber/getBool/destroy round-trips and JSON parse-failure → null.\n- `NavHelper` — `vi.mock('$app/state')`; cover `getPageSlug`, `getPageFeature`, `showNavbar`, `isDashboard`, `isAdminRoute`, `isAuthRoute`, `isSetupRoute`.\n- `platform.ts` / `urls.ts` / `features.ts` / `navigation.ts` / `apiRoutes.ts` — `vi.mock('$env/dynamic/public')` + `$app/*` + `localStorage`; assert `getApiUrl` resolution order (env → hostname map → fallback), custom-API URL persistence, `PLATFORM`/`IS_NATIVE` flags. Use `vi.resetModules()` + fresh `$env` mocks for isolation.\n\n### Phase 3 — State stores (node + module mocks, after §4 refactor)\n\nApply the §4.1 recipe. Full inventory by group (37 files):\n\n| Group            | Stores                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Extra mocks needed                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Root             | `Auth`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$env/dynamic/public`, ApiService, LocalStorageService                                                                                         |\n| No-auth (8)      | `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `PwaInstall`, `Viewpoint`, `CookieConsent`, `Theme`, `LibraryNavigation`                                                                                                                                                                                                           | `LoadingIndicator` testable as-is; `WelcomeTour`/`LibraryNavigation` need `urls`/`$app/state` mocks; `Theme` DOM methods need jsdom or adapter |\n| Auth+CRUD (21)   | `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `Finances`, `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `BookLibrary`, `MusicLibrary`, `MovieLibrary`, `GameLibrary`, `PlantLibrary`, `QuoteLibrary`, `RecipeLibrary`, `LinkLibrary`, `Clipboard`, `DevRequests`, `Friends`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`, `Tags`, `TimeTracking`, `UserManagement`, `UserNotifications`, `Weather` | Auth + ApiService (+ LocalStorageService for the 12 that use it)                                                                               |\n| `page` users (5) | CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation, Notes, Todos                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$app/state`                                                                                                                                   |\n| Special          | `QuickAdd` (3 contexts), `Navigation` (`$env/dynamic/public` + `auth.user.settings`), `Translation` (`browser` + `navigator.language`)                                                                                                                                                                                                   | per-file                                                                                                                                       |\n\n### Phase 4 — Component tests (jsdom, after §3.2/§3.3)\n\n**4a. Pure/presentational leaves (~70, low effort).** No context, no `$app`:\n\n- `forms/` (11): Checkbox, DateInput, DateTimeInput, NumberInput, TextInput, Select, Slider, Toggle, SvelteDateInput, InputAutocomplete, InlineAutocomplete.\n- `ui/buttons/` (17): AcceptButton, AddButton, CloseButton, CloudButton, DeleteButton, EditButton, FunnelButton, HamburgerButton, IconButton, ImportButton, InlineDeleteButton, InlineEditButton, InlineExpandButton, RefreshButton, SaveButton, StarButton, TextButton.\n- `ui/icons/` (12), `ui/menus/` (2: MenuIcon, RightClickMenu), `ui/` primitives (~18): Badge, Card, Divider, File, Flag, Heading, SubHeading, ModalFormRow, Tabs, ViewSwitcher, NavEntry, NavEntryIcon, MovableHoverBox, HelpTooltip, LoadingLogo, StaggeredLogo, QuickSelectOverlay, PopupContentModal, BottomSheetModal, SlidingSideBar.\n- Feature leaves: `todos/Counter`, `check-in/` (DailyCheckInIcon, CheckInIcon, AverageNumber), `libraries/shared/` (Rating, CoverImage, MissingCover, GenreFlexList, ExternalSearchLink, BookRelease), `tags/TagFlexList`, `dev-requests/Author`, `guitar/GuitarTheoryNavigation`, `admin/StatisticWidget`, `notes/AddFolderButton`/`AddNoteButton`/`editor/ToolbarDivider`, `settings/SettingsSection` + SettingsNavigation*, `dashboard/widgets/*` (the props-driven ones: DueTodosWidget, ScoredTodosWidget, EventsTodayWidget, UpcomingEventsWidget, NewestNotesWidget, NewestLinksWidget, BookReleasesWidget, MovieReleasesWidget, MusicReleasesWidget, QuoteWidget).\n\n**4b. Translation-only components (~20).** Presentational but call `getTranslation()`; become trivial once the §4.3 harness exists: the `*ImportButton`/`*Button` icons, `NoTodos`, `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`, `ui/CookieBanner`, `PopupConfirmationModal`, `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `NavLegalEntry`.\n\n**4c. KeyManager + domain integration.** With `setKeyManager()`/`setTodos()`/`setAuth()`/`setLoadingIndicator()`/`setUiNotifications()`/`setViewPoint()` in the harness:\n\n- Todos feature: `views/{CardView,ListView,OverviewView}`, `props/*` (Category, DueDate, Effort, Flags, Link, Priority, Progress, Recurrence, Status, Subtasks, Tags, Title), `actions/{TodoCreate,TodoDelete,HideIt,SortByScore}`, `TodoNavigation*`, `ListAndAdd`.\n- Calendars: `views/{day,week,month,list}/*`, `NavigationEntry`, `MobileCalendarHeader`.\n- Dashboard: `YourDay`, `QuickGlance`, plus context widgets.\n- Libraries: shared `Entries/Header/Search/ShelfView/SpineView/CreateModal/DetailModal`.\n- Feeds, time-tracking, notes, check-in, settings, finances as capacity allows.\n\n**4d. Heavy/skip (~15 components).** Do not attempt in jsdom without heavy stubbing — exclude from automated coverage or stub their leaf dependencies:\n`charts/*` (echarts), `notes/editor/*` (TipTap/ProseMirror), `todos/views/KanbanView` (svelte-dnd-action), `ui/Notifications` (svelte-gestures), `settings/SecuritySettings` (simplewebauthn), `forms/{DatePicker,MultiSelect}` (datepicker/svelte-multiselect), `settings/{TagEdit,LocalizationSettings}`, `contacts/AddressBook*` (color picker, tzdb), dompurify/marked-rich components, `desktop/TitleBar` + `settings/UpdateChecker` (electronAPI), `clipboard/ClipboardList` (clipboard API), `tour/WelcomeTour`, `quick-add/QuickAddModal`. `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas) is likewise skipped or reduced to pure resize-math.\n\n### Phase 5 — E2E (optional, later)\n\nIf desired, Playwright against the real dev server with API responses mocked at\n`http://localhost:8000/api/v1/**` (or via a stub server). High-value flows:\nauth (email/password + WebAuthn virtual authenticator), todos CRUD, calendar\nmonth navigation, a library search. Must block/clear the service-worker cache\n(`serviceWorkers: 'block'` or `caches.delete()`) for deterministic runs.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Expected coverage & measurement\n\n- Use `@vitest/coverage-v8` with `npm run test:coverage`.\n- Treat coverage as a **signal, not a target**: after the §8 roadmap, the\n  remaining uncovered code should be the explicit out-of-scope list — third-party\n  wrappers, canvas/DOM-heavy leaves, and render-only components.\n- Keep the out-of-scope paths excluded (`exclude` in the coverage config) so\n  the number stays honest and comparable over time.\n- Re-measure after each priority and watch _where_ the uncovered lines are,\n  not the headline percentage. The number will stay modest while the 357\n  components and 37 stores exist, because most of them are intentionally not\n  tested (see §8).\n\n## 7. Risks & caveats\n\n- **SvelteKit `$app/state` `page` object** in tests is a static mock; code that\n  reacts to `page` changes won't be exercised at unit level (fine — component\n  tests cover rendering paths).\n- **Run/effect timing:** stores use `setTimeout`/`tick`/`setInterval`\n  (`quickCreate`, `recentlyCreated`, `UserNotifications`, `Calendars`,\n  `Notes`). Use `vi.useFakeTimers()` and `flushSync`/`await tick()`.\n- **`SvelteDate` ignores `vi.setSystemTime`:** `svelte/reactivity`'s `SvelteDate`\n  captures the native `Date` at module load (in both the client and server\n  builds), so the fake-timer clock never reaches `new SvelteDate()` — it always\n  returns the real current time. Tests that exercise store code reading \"now\"\n  via `SvelteDate` (`Calendars` constructor/`goToToday`, `CheckInData`\n  initialisation/`isCurrentMonth`) must therefore assert against the real\n  `new Date()` on real timers, never against a hardcoded date — a hardcoded\n  \"today\" only passes on the day it was written.\n- **jsdom gaps:** `matchMedia`, `ResizeObserver`, `IntersectionObserver`,\n  `navigator.clipboard`, canvas 2D context need small stubs in\n  `tests/setup/component.ts`.\n- **i18n invariant:** when adding/verifying UI strings in component tests,\n  keep all four locales (`en/de/es/fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it.\n- **Pinned deps:** all additions must be pinned and installed only with\n  approval (AGENTS.md hard rule).\n- **Do not over-test third-party wrappers:** ECharts/TipTap/DnD behavior is the\n  library's responsibility; assert our props/logic, not their internals.\n\n## 8. Next steps — where to invest next (current roadmap)\n\nGuiding rule: **test what has logic or a contract worth pinning; nothing else.**\nThe 8.7% figure is low because the denominator is the whole of `src/lib` (357\ncomponents, 37 stores), most of which is boilerplate or third-party wrappers.\nRaise it by testing the real logic — not by chasing a number.\n\n### Priority 1 — State stores with real business logic (highest value)\n\n| Store                  | What is genuinely testable                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Calendars`            | `loadMonth` (42-day grid math), `getEventsForDate`, month/week/day navigation, view state                                                                                                          |\n| `Auth`                 | login/register/refresh/passkey flows, load-from-localStorage, token-expiry branch, `isAdmin` — the security surface; the token-capture recipe is proven in `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts` |\n| `Notes`                | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                                          |\n| Library stores (all 8) | the **non-CRUD** parts: search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, view-pref persistence                                                                       |\n| `CheckInData`          | month navigation, date-derived `selectedDate`, scoring                                                                                                                                             |\n\nDo **not** test the ~20 boilerplate CRUD wrappers (`createX`/`updateX`/`deleteX`\n= call the API + reload). Prove the pattern once per store, then move on.\n\n### Priority 2 — Presentational components _with logic_\n\nMost of the ~70 \"pure\" leaves (icons, logos, dividers) are render-only and not\nworth tests. Real value is in:\n\n- Keyboard/selection logic: `forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`,\n  `forms/Slider`.\n- State-driven leaves: `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon`/`CheckInIcon`,\n  `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`, `libraries/shared/CoverImage`.\n- Props-driven dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`, `ScoredTodosWidget`,\n  `UpcomingEventsWidget`, …) — data + handlers come in as props, making them the\n  cleanest integration targets in the app.\n- Translation-only components (~20 `*ImportButton`s, `NoTodos`, password\n  indicators) — only after Priority 3's harness exists.\n\n### Priority 3 — Context harness (enabling investment)\n\nOne `renderWithContext` helper that seeds `setTranslation()`, `setKeyManager()`,\n`setTodos()`, `setAuth()`, `setLoadingIndicator()`, `setUiNotifications()`,\n`setViewPoint()` before rendering (pattern in §4.3). This unlocks the ~250\ncontext-coupled components (todos views/props/actions, calendar views, dashboard)\nand the translation-only leaves. Without it, the mock boilerplate per component\ntest is not worth the effort.\n\n### Explicitly out of scope\n\n- Heavy/skip list (§4d): echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD (`KanbanView`),\n  svelte-gestures (`ui/Notifications`), WebAuthn (`SecuritySettings`),\n  `DatePicker`/`MultiSelect`, dompurify/marked-rich components, electronAPI\n  (`TitleBar`/`UpdateChecker`), clipboard API (`ClipboardList`).\n- `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas + `Image`).\n- Icons, logos, and other render-only components.\n- Third-party behavior — assert our props/logic, not ECharts/ProseMirror internals.\n- E2E/Playwright for now — a client-side SPA with a mocked API at the unit level\n  is already covered by store + component tests; E2E adds infrastructure for\n  marginal value.\n\n### Execution order\n\n1. [x] `Calendars` + `Auth` store tests (biggest logic; recipe proven) — TASK-1/TASK-2.\n2. [x] `Notes` + library-store filtering tests — TASK-3/TASK-4 (+ `CheckInData`, TASK-5).\n3. [x] §4.3 context harness — TASK-6.\n4. [x] Dashboard widgets + logic-bearing leaves — TASK-7/TASK-8.\n5. [x] Translation-only components — TASK-9.\n6. [x] Re-run `npm run test:coverage` and inspect the remaining uncovered lines —\n   they cluster in the \"explicitly out of scope\" list above (plus the secondary\n   stores named in §0). The suite is \"complete enough\" rather than \"maximised\",\n   which is the goal.\n7. [x] Optional follow-up: secondary stores with real non-CRUD logic — `Feeds`,\n   `Contacts`, `Navigation` (+ `PUBLIC_DISABLE_DEV_REQUESTS` env branch),\n   `QuickAdd`, `UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme` (DOM-stubbed),\n   `PwaInstall`. All landed in `tests/unit/stores/` and brought `lib/state`\n   statement coverage to ~56%.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":597,"totalLines":597,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/TESTING.md","time":{"start":1791639655364,"end":1791639655557}},"id":"prt_1260b9317001dx9O1qf6bUmqW6","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","messageID":"msg_1260b8ab800177P3AEAgHH6DKl"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639655642,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_x86eVDiw57YRkgw3QHlj5078","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/src/lib/config/platform.ts"},"output":"<path>/workspace/src/lib/config/platform.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import { env } from '$env/dynamic/public';\n2: import { browser, dev } from '$app/environment';\n3: import type { Platform } from '$lib/types/platform';\n4: import LocalStorageService from '$lib/services/LocalStorageService';\n5: \n6: const LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY = 'custom_api_url';\n7: export const PLATFORM: Platform = (() => {\n8: \tif (env.PUBLIC_DESKTOP) return 'desktop';\n9: \tif (env.PUBLIC_MOBILE) return 'mobile';\n10: \treturn 'web';\n11: })();\n12: \n13: export const IS_DESKTOP = PLATFORM === 'desktop';\n14: export const IS_MOBILE = PLATFORM === 'mobile';\n15: export const IS_WEB = PLATFORM === 'web';\n16: export const IS_NATIVE = !IS_WEB;\n17: \n18: export function getApiUrl(): string {\n19: \treturn PLATFORM === 'web' ? getPwaApiUrl() : getCustomApiUrl();\n20: }\n21: \n22: export function getPwaApiUrl(): string {\n23: \tif (dev) return 'http://localhost:8000';\n24: \tif (env.PUBLIC_API_URL) return env.PUBLIC_API_URL;\n25: \tif (!browser) return 'https://api.solyto.app';\n26: \n27: \tconst domainMap: Record<string, string> = {\n28: \t\t'app.solyto.de': 'https://api.solyto.de',\n29: \t\t'my.solyto.app': 'https://api.solyto.app'\n30: \t};\n31: \n32: \treturn domainMap[window.location.hostname] || 'https://api.solyto.app';\n33: }\n34: \n35: export function getCustomApiUrl(): string {\n36: \tconst ls = new LocalStorageService();\n37: \treturn ls.get(LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY) || getPwaApiUrl();\n38: }\n39: \n40: export function setCustomApiUrl(url: string) {\n41: \tconst ls = new LocalStorageService();\n42: \tls.set(LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY, url);\n43: }\n44: \n45: export function dropCustomApiUrl() {\n46: \tconst ls = new LocalStorageService();\n47: \tls.destroy(LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY);\n48: }\n\n(End of file - total 48 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import { env } from '$env/dynamic/public';\nimport { browser, dev } from '$app/environment';\nimport type { Platform } from '$lib/types/platform';\nimport LocalStorageService from '$lib/services/LocalStorageService';\n\nconst LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY = 'custom_api_url';\nexport const PLATFORM: Platform = (() => {\n\tif (env.PUBLIC_DESKTOP) return 'desktop';\n\tif (env.PUBLIC_MOBILE) return 'mobile';\n\treturn 'web';\n})();\n\nexport const IS_DESKTOP = PLATFORM === 'desktop';\nexport const IS_MOBILE = PLATFORM === 'mobile';\nexport const IS_WEB = PLATFORM === 'web';\nexport const IS_NATIVE = !IS_WEB;\n\nexport function getApiUrl(): string {\n\treturn PLATFORM === 'web' ? getPwaApiUrl() : getCustomApiUrl();\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/src/lib/config/platform.ts","text":"import { env } from '$env/dynamic/public';\nimport { browser, dev } from '$app/environment';\nimport type { Platform } from '$lib/types/platform';\nimport LocalStorageService from '$lib/services/LocalStorageService';\n\nconst LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY = 'custom_api_url';\nexport const PLATFORM: Platform = (() => {\n\tif (env.PUBLIC_DESKTOP) return 'desktop';\n\tif (env.PUBLIC_MOBILE) return 'mobile';\n\treturn 'web';\n})();\n\nexport const IS_DESKTOP = PLATFORM === 'desktop';\nexport const IS_MOBILE = PLATFORM === 'mobile';\nexport const IS_WEB = PLATFORM === 'web';\nexport const IS_NATIVE = !IS_WEB;\n\nexport function getApiUrl(): string {\n\treturn PLATFORM === 'web' ? getPwaApiUrl() : getCustomApiUrl();\n}\n\nexport function getPwaApiUrl(): string {\n\tif (dev) return 'http://localhost:8000';\n\tif (env.PUBLIC_API_URL) return env.PUBLIC_API_URL;\n\tif (!browser) return 'https://api.solyto.app';\n\n\tconst domainMap: Record<string, string> = {\n\t\t'app.solyto.de': 'https://api.solyto.de',\n\t\t'my.solyto.app': 'https://api.solyto.app'\n\t};\n\n\treturn domainMap[window.location.hostname] || 'https://api.solyto.app';\n}\n\nexport function getCustomApiUrl(): string {\n\tconst ls = new LocalStorageService();\n\treturn ls.get(LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY) || getPwaApiUrl();\n}\n\nexport function setCustomApiUrl(url: string) {\n\tconst ls = new LocalStorageService();\n\tls.set(LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY, url);\n}\n\nexport function dropCustomApiUrl() {\n\tconst ls = new LocalStorageService();\n\tls.destroy(LS_CUSTOM_API_URL_KEY);\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":48,"totalLines":48,"truncated":false}},"title":"src/lib/config/platform.ts","time":{"start":1791639655449,"end":1791639655637}},"id":"prt_1260b93fe0012gTmR0DttGAcVE","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","messageID":"msg_1260b8ab800177P3AEAgHH6DKl"}}
