{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639971741,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_c00aefb72fa64b27ba22c62e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","limit":22,"offset":48},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n48: - `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n49: - `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n50: - Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n51: \n52: ## Commands\n53: - `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n54: - `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n55: - `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n56: - `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n57: - `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n58: - `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n59: - `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n60: - `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n61: \n62: ## Hard rules\n63: - NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n64: - NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n65: - NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n66: - NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n67: - When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n68: - When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n69: - Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n\n(Showing lines 48-69 of 70. Use offset=70 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","text":"- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task","lineStart":48,"lineEnd":69,"totalLines":70,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1791639971727,"end":1791639971735}},"id":"prt_126106685001iIQUgYj12lD0B8","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","messag