{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640064712,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_3e594850727b4fd6a9ac92d4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # State services\n2: \n3: Policy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\n4: Svelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\n5: talk to the API. Read [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\n6: document applies those general rules to this layer.\n7: \n8: ## One class per domain, one file per domain\n9: \n10: - One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n11:   in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n12: - `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n13:   compile.\n14: - The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n15:   the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n16:   `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n17: - No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n18:   components and `i18n/`).\n19: \n20: ## The context-singleton pattern\n21: \n22: Every store is a Svelte context singleton. The file exports a private `Symbol`\n23: key plus a `setX()` / `getX()` pair — the only sanctioned shape:\n24: \n25: ```ts\n26: const CLIPBOARD_KEY = Symbol('SOLYTO_CLIPBOARD');\n27: \n28: export function setClipboard(): Clipboard {\n29: \treturn setContext(CLIPBOARD_KEY, new Clipboard());\n30: }\n31: \n32: export function getClipboard(): Clipboard {\n33: \treturn getContext<Clipboard>(CLIPBOARD_KEY);\n34: }\n35: ```\n36: \n37: - `setX()` is called **once**, during component initialisation, and returns the\n38:   new instance.\n39: - `getX()` is called by any component below that needs the store. It never\n40:   constructs — a missing provider is a programming error, not a case to handle.\n41: - App-wide stores (`Auth`, `Translation`, `Viewpoint`, `KeyManager`,\n42:   `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `Navigation`, `CookieConsent`,\n43:   `PwaInstall`, `WelcomeTour`, `QuickAdd`) are created in\n44:   `src/routes/+layout.svelte`.\n45: - Feature stores are created in the feature's route layout — e.g.\n46:   `setTodos()`/`setTags()` in `src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n47:   `setClipboard()` in `src/routes/clipboard/+layout.svelte`,\n48:   `setBookLibrary()` in `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`. This keeps\n49:   a feature's store alive only while its routes are mounted.\n50: \n51: ## Reactive state as `$state` class fields\n52: \n53: - Declare each piece of reactive state as a public `$state` field with an\n54:   explicit type:\n55: \n56:   ```ts\n57:   loaded = $state<boolean>(false);\n58:   todos = $state<Todo[]>([]);\n59:   activeWorkspace = $state<TodoWorkspace | null>(null);\n60:   view = $state<'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' | 'card'>('list');\n61:   ```\n62: \n63: - Initialise to the empty/neutral value so the store is valid before `load()`\n64:   runs.\n65: - Mutate the field directly (`this.todos = res.data as Todo[]`); do not wrap it\n66:   in setters, stores or extra indirection. Svelte's runes propagate the change.\n67: - Internal-only state may be `private` (see `Viewpoint._state`), but reach for\n68:   that only when you also want to expose a stable read-only surface (next\n69:   section).\n70: \n71: ## Member ordering\n72: \n73: Keep the same order in every store, top to bottom. `Todos` is the reference:\n74: \n75: 1. `static readonly` constants (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`).\n76: 2. `$state` fields.\n77: 3. Collaborators/dependencies declared as typed fields (`auth`, `apiService`,\n78:    `localStorage`, injected services) and any private helpers.\n79: 4. The constructor.\n80: 5. Public methods.\n81: 6. `private` methods last.\n82: \n83: The `Symbol` key and `setX()`/`getX()` functions live **below** the class, at\n84: the bottom of the file.\n85: \n86: ## Constructor dependency injection (preferred)\n87: \n88: The preferred shape injects collaborators through constructor parameters whose\n89: defaults preserve zero-argument construction. `Todos` and `Finances` are the\n90: reference:\n91: \n92: ```ts\n93: export class Todos {\n94: \tauth: Auth;\n95: \tapiService: ApiService;\n96: \tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n97: \n98: \tconstructor(\n99: \t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n100: \t\tapiService: ApiService = auth.apiService,\n101: \t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n102: \t) {\n103: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n104: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n105: \t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n106: \t}\n107: }\n108: ```\n109: \n110: ```ts\n111: export class Finances {\n112: \tauth: Auth;\n113: \tapiService: ApiService;\n114: \n115: \tconstructor(auth: Auth = getAuth(), apiService: ApiService = auth.apiService) {\n116: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n117: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n118: \t\t// …\n119: \t}\n120: }\n121: ```\n122: \n123: Why it matters:\n124: \n125: - `new Todos()` still works everywhere (the defaults do the context lookup), so\n126:   the change is invisible to callers.\n127: - Tests can pass mocks (`new Todos(mockAuth, mockApi, mockStorage)`) without\n128:   module-level `vi.mock` gymnastics — this is the refactor `docs/TESTING.md` §4\n129:   describes, and it is what made the store tests possible.\n130: - The defaults are the single place that knows how to build the real\n131:   collaborators.\n132: \n133: The **older style** some stores still use declares dependencies as\n134: field initialisers, which run before the constructor body:\n135: \n136: ```ts\n137: // older — not the target style\n138: export class Clipboard {\n139: \tauth = getAuth();\n140: \tapiService: ApiService;\n141: \n142: \tconstructor() {\n143: \t\tthis.apiService = this.auth.apiService;\n144: \t}\n145: }\n146: ```\n147: \n148: This works, but it cannot be overridden by a constructor argument and forces\n149: tests to mock the `Auth` module. When you touch a store, prefer migrating it to\n150: the injectable shape; do not do it as a bulk rewrite.\n151: \n152: The shared API client is `auth.apiService` — `Auth` owns one `ApiService`\n153: instance and keeps its token current (`updateAuthToken`). Stores default to it;\n154: do not construct a second `ApiService` with a hand-copied token.\n155: \n156: ## The `load()` + `loaded` convention\n157: \n158: Every domain store exposes an async `load(): Promise<void>` that fetches its\n159: data and populates the `$state` fields, and a boolean `loaded` field set to\n160: `true` on the first successful load. Components/layouts call `load()` in\n161: `onMount` and use `loaded` to avoid rendering empty state.\n162: \n163: ```ts\n164: async load(): Promise<void> {\n165: \tconst res = await this.apiService.list(apiRoutes.todos.list);\n166: \n167: \tif (res) {\n168: \t\tthis.loaded = true;\n169: \t\tthis.todos = res.data as Todo[];\n170: \t\tthis.filteredTodos = this.todos;\n171: \t\t// …\n172: \t}\n173: \n174: \t// … derived steps, then parallel sub-loads\n175: }\n176: ```\n177: \n178: - One `if (res)` block does the assignment; failure simply leaves the previous\n179:   state in place (see error semantics in [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)).\n180: - Sub-loads use their own `loadX()` methods and may run in parallel via\n181:   `Promise.all`.\n182: - `load()` re-derives everything that depends on the freshly-loaded data, so a\n183:   store is never left half-updated.\n184: \n185: ## The CRUD method pattern\n186: \n187: Every create/update/delete method follows the same shape: call `ApiService`\n188: with a route from `apiRoutes`, reload on success, return a boolean.\n189: \n190: ```ts\n191: async delete(todo: Todo): Promise<boolean> {\n192: \tconst ok = await this.apiService.delete(apiRoutes.todos.delete, todo.id);\n193: \tif (ok) await this.load();\n194: \treturn ok;\n195: }\n196: ```\n197: \n198: ```ts\n199: async addTag(todo: Todo, tagId: number): Promise<boolean> {\n200: \tconst tagIds = todo.tags.map((t) => t.id);\n201: \tconst request: UpdateTodoRequest = { tags: tagIds.concat([tagId]) };\n202: \tconst res = await this.apiService.update(apiRoutes.todos.update, todo.id, request);\n203: \tif (res) await this.load();\n204: \treturn res;\n205: }\n206: ```\n207: \n208: - Build a typed request object first (`const request: UpdateTodoRequest = {…}`),\n209:   then pass it to `ApiService`.\n210: - Return `true`/`false` (or the raw `res`/`ok`) so the calling component can\n211:   react. Mutating methods that need a created entity return it (or `null`).\n212: - **This repetitiveness is intentional.** It is not something to \"DRY up\" behind\n213:   a generic `crud(endpoint, method, id)` helper — each method is a greppable,\n214:   independently-readable contract with its own request type, and the\n215:   boilerplate CRUD wrappers are explicitly excluded from test coverage\n216:   (`docs/TESTING.md` §8). Copy the nearest method; do not abstract it.\n217: \n218: ## Delegate pure logic to `services/`\n219: \n220: A store is glue: it holds state and sequences API/pure calls. Filtering,\n221: sorting, grouping and scoring are pure and live in `src/lib/services/`:\n222: \n223: - `Todos` delegates to `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`,\n224:   `TodoGroupingService` and `TodoRelevanceService` — e.g.\n225:   `this.filteredTodos = this.filterService.filter(filter, this.filteredTodos)`.\n226: - The service instances are held as fields (`filterService = new TodoFilterService()`)\n227:   and called from the store's methods.\n228: - Library stores hold a `LibraryFilterService`; `Finances` uses\n229:   `WealthStatisticsService`.\n230: \n231: If you are about to write a non-trivial `filter`/`map`/`reduce` chain inside a\n232: store method, stop: it probably belongs in a `*Service.ts` where it can be unit\n233: tested without any Svelte context. See [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md).\n234: \n235: ## Persistence\n236: \n237: The only client-side persistence is `LocalStorageService`, injected into the\n238: store. Storage keys are class constants named `LS_*`:\n239: \n240: ```ts\n241: export class Todos {\n242: \tstatic readonly LS_HIDE_IT_KEY: string = 'todos_hideit';\n243: \t// …\n244: }\n245: ```\n246: \n247: ```ts\n248: this.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n249: ```\n250: \n251: - Always go through `LocalStorageService` — it guards `browser` internally, so\n252:   callers do not have to.\n253: - Keys are `snake_case` strings (`'todos_hideit'`, `'custom_api_url'`).\n254: - Restore persisted state in the constructor, and re-read it in `load()` when a\n255:   value could have changed while the initial load was in flight (see\n256:   `Todos.loadHideIt()`). Auth tokens are the one exception handled by `Auth`\n257:   itself.\n258: \n259: ## Browser and route imports — guard them\n260: \n261: - `browser` from `$app/environment` guards anything that touches `window`,\n262:   `document` or `localStorage`. `LocalStorageService` does this internally; a\n263:   store that touches the DOM directly must do the same. `Viewpoint` guards its\n264:   entire initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n265: - `page` from `$app/state` is read for route information (e.g.\n266:   `page.url.searchParams` in `Todos.checkUrlForFilter()`). Read it; do not\n267:   subscribe to navigation inside the store.\n268: - If a store registers listeners or timers, clean them up in an explicit\n269:   `destroy()` method and call it from the owner component's `onDestroy`.\n270:   `Viewpoint` collects each cleanup closure in an array and runs them all in\n271:   `destroy()`.\n272: \n273: ## Stores may depend on other stores\n274: \n275: A store may read another store or the translation table when its logic needs\n276: them:\n277: \n278: - `QuickAdd` reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()` for its error\n279:   messages, and `getAuth()` for the API client.\n280: - `Translation` reads `getAuth()` to pick the user's language.\n281: \n282: Resolve these dependencies once in the constructor (or as defaults), not on\n283: every method call, and never create a cycle. Keep the dependency in the\n284: constructor's parameter list where practical so tests can inject it\n285: (`docs/TESTING.md` §4 gives `QuickAdd` as the `ts`/`notifications` example).\n286: \n287: ## Read-only view state via getters\n288: \n289: When a store owns computed state that consumers must not write, expose it\n290: through getters. `Viewpoint` keeps its data in a `private _state` and returns\n291: `get state()`, `get width()`, `get isDesktop()`, etc.:\n292: \n293: ```ts\n294: private _state = $state<ViewPointState>({ width: 0, height: 0, isDesktop: false, isMobile: true, isTablet: false });\n295: \n296: get isDesktop() {\n297: \treturn this._state.isDesktop;\n298: }\n299: ```\n300: \n301: Use this for genuinely read-only derivations (screen class, computed URL\n302: flags). For normal domain data, keep the public `$state` field — getters for\n303: everything add noise.\n304: \n305: ## What not to do\n306: \n307: - **No markup, DOM, or UI strings** in a store. That is the component layer's\n308:   job.\n309: - **No hardcoded API URLs.** Every endpoint comes from\n310:   `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`; never build a URL string by hand.\n311: - **No inline `fetch`.** `ApiService` is the single network seam; a store calls\n312:   it and nothing else. (The only exceptions are the few legacy direct-`fetch`\n313:   methods in `Calendars` — do not copy them.)\n314: - **No giant methods.** Split by named steps (`loadCategories`, `useFilters`).\n315: - **No new global singletons.** Use the context pattern; do not export a\n316:   module-level `new Todos()`.\n317: - **No `$derived` dumping ground.** Derived values that belong in a method or a\n318:   service stay there; see [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline).\n319: - Do not add an abstraction a store does not already use.\n320: \n321: ## Related docs\n322: \n323: - [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n324: - [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — `ApiService`, `apiRoutes`, services,\n325:   helpers, types, i18n.\n326: - [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components read these stores.\n327: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §3–4 — the store test recipe and the\n328:   constructor-injection refactor.\n\n(End of file - total 328 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ntalk to the API. Read [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n\n## One class per domain, one file per domain\n\n- One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n  in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n- `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n  compile.\n- The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n  the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n  `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n- No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n  components and `i18n/`).\n\n## The context-singleton pattern","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md","text":"# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ntalk to the API. Read [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n\n## One class per domain, one file per domain\n\n- One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n  in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n- `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n  compile.\n- The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n  the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n  `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n- No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n  components and `i18n/`).\n\n## The context-singleton pattern\n\nEvery store is a Svelte context singleton. The file exports a private `Symbol`\nkey plus a `setX()` / `getX()` pair — the only sanctioned shape:\n\n```ts\nconst CLIPBOARD_KEY = Symbol('SOLYTO_CLIPBOARD');\n\nexport function setClipboard(): Clipboard {\n\treturn setContext(CLIPBOARD_KEY, new Clipboard());\n}\n\nexport function getClipboard(): Clipboard {\n\treturn getContext<Clipboard>(CLIPBOARD_KEY);\n}\n```\n\n- `setX()` is called **once**, during component initialisation, and returns the\n  new instance.\n- `getX()` is called by any component below that needs the store. It never\n  constructs — a missing provider is a programming error, not a case to handle.\n- App-wide stores (`Auth`, `Translation`, `Viewpoint`, `KeyManager`,\n  `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `Navigation`, `CookieConsent`,\n  `PwaInstall`, `WelcomeTour`, `QuickAdd`) are created in\n  `src/routes/+layout.svelte`.\n- Feature stores are created in the feature's route layout — e.g.\n  `setTodos()`/`setTags()` in `src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n  `setClipboard()` in `src/routes/clipboard/+layout.svelte`,\n  `setBookLibrary()` in `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`. This keeps\n  a feature's store alive only while its routes are mounted.\n\n## Reactive state as `$state` class fields\n\n- Declare each piece of reactive state as a public `$state` field with an\n  explicit type:\n\n  ```ts\n  loaded = $state<boolean>(false);\n  todos = $state<Todo[]>([]);\n  activeWorkspace = $state<TodoWorkspace | null>(null);\n  view = $state<'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' | 'card'>('list');\n  ```\n\n- Initialise to the empty/neutral value so the store is valid before `load()`\n  runs.\n- Mutate the field directly (`this.todos = res.data as Todo[]`); do not wrap it\n  in setters, stores or extra indirection. Svelte's runes propagate the change.\n- Internal-only state may be `private` (see `Viewpoint._state`), but reach for\n  that only when you also want to expose a stable read-only surface (next\n  section).\n\n## Member ordering\n\nKeep the same order in every store, top to bottom. `Todos` is the reference:\n\n1. `static readonly` constants (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`).\n2. `$state` fields.\n3. Collaborators/dependencies declared as typed fields (`auth`, `apiService`,\n   `localStorage`, injected services) and any private helpers.\n4. The constructor.\n5. Public methods.\n6. `private` methods last.\n\nThe `Symbol` key and `setX()`/`getX()` functions live **below** the class, at\nthe bottom of the file.\n\n## Constructor dependency injection (preferred)\n\nThe preferred shape injects collaborators through constructor parameters whose\ndefaults preserve zero-argument construction. `Todos` and `Finances` are the\nreference:\n\n```ts\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n\n\tconstructor(\n\t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n\t\tapiService: ApiService = auth.apiService,\n\t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n\t) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nexport class Finances {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\n\tconstructor(auth: Auth = getAuth(), apiService: ApiService = auth.apiService) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nWhy it matters:\n\n- `new Todos()` still works everywhere (the defaults do the context lookup), so\n  the change is invisible to callers.\n- Tests can pass mocks (`new Todos(mockAuth, mockApi, mockStorage)`) without\n  module-level `vi.mock` gymnastics — this is the refactor `docs/TESTING.md` §4\n  describes, and it is what made the store tests possible.\n- The defaults are the single place that knows how to build the real\n  collaborators.\n\nThe **older style** some stores still use declares dependencies as\nfield initialisers, which run before the constructor body:\n\n```ts\n// older — not the target style\nexport class Clipboard {\n\tauth = getAuth();\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tthis.apiService = this.auth.apiService;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis works, but it cannot be overridden by a constructor argument and forces\ntests to mock the `Auth` module. When you touch a store, prefer migrating it to\nthe injectable shape; do not do it as a bulk rewrite.\n\nThe shared API client is `auth.apiService` — `Auth` owns one `ApiService`\ninstance and keeps its token current (`updateAuthToken`). Stores default to it;\ndo not construct a second `ApiService` with a hand-copied token.\n\n## The `load()` + `loaded` convention\n\nEvery domain store exposes an async `load(): Promise<void>` that fetches its\ndata and populates the `$state` fields, and a boolean `loaded` field set to\n`true` on the first successful load. Components/layouts call `load()` in\n`onMount` and use `loaded` to avoid rendering empty state.\n\n```ts\nasync load(): Promise<void> {\n\tconst res = await this.apiService.list(apiRoutes.todos.list);\n\n\tif (res) {\n\t\tthis.loaded = true;\n\t\tthis.todos = res.data as Todo[];\n\t\tthis.filteredTodos = this.todos;\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n\n\t// … derived steps, then parallel sub-loads\n}\n```\n\n- One `if (res)` block does the assignment; failure simply leaves the previous\n  state in place (see error semantics in [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)).\n- Sub-loads use their own `loadX()` methods and may run in parallel via\n  `Promise.all`.\n- `load()` re-derives everything that depends on the freshly-loaded data, so a\n  store is never left half-updated.\n\n## The CRUD method pattern\n\nEvery create/update/delete method follows the same shape: call `ApiService`\nwith a route from `apiRoutes`, reload on success, return a boolean.\n\n```ts\nasync delete(todo: Todo): Promise<boolean> {\n\tconst ok = await this.apiService.delete(apiRoutes.todos.delete, todo.id);\n\tif (ok) await this.load();\n\treturn ok;\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nasync addTag(todo: Todo, tagId: number): Promise<boolean> {\n\tconst tagIds = todo.tags.map((t) => t.id);\n\tconst request: UpdateTodoRequest = { tags: tagIds.concat([tagId]) };\n\tconst res = await this.apiService.update(apiRoutes.todos.update, todo.id, request);\n\tif (res) await this.load();\n\treturn res;\n}\n```\n\n- Build a typed request object first (`const request: UpdateTodoRequest = {…}`),\n  then pass it to `ApiService`.\n- Return `true`/`false` (or the raw `res`/`ok`) so the calling component can\n  react. Mutating methods that need a created entity return it (or `null`).\n- **This repetitiveness is intentional.** It is not something to \"DRY up\" behind\n  a generic `crud(endpoint, method, id)` helper — each method is a greppable,\n  independently-readable contract with its own request type, and the\n  boilerplate CRUD wrappers are explicitly excluded from test coverage\n  (`docs/TESTING.md` §8). Copy the nearest method; do not abstract it.\n\n## Delegate pure logic to `services/`\n\nA store is glue: it holds state and sequences API/pure calls. Filtering,\nsorting, grouping and scoring are pure and live in `src/lib/services/`:\n\n- `Todos` delegates to `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`,\n  `TodoGroupingService` and `TodoRelevanceService` — e.g.\n  `this.filteredTodos = this.filterService.filter(filter, this.filteredTodos)`.\n- The service instances are held as fields (`filterService = new TodoFilterService()`)\n  and called from the store's methods.\n- Library stores hold a `LibraryFilterService`; `Finances` uses\n  `WealthStatisticsService`.\n\nIf you are about to write a non-trivial `filter`/`map`/`reduce` chain inside a\nstore method, stop: it probably belongs in a `*Service.ts` where it can be unit\ntested without any Svelte context. See [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md).\n\n## Persistence\n\nThe only client-side persistence is `LocalStorageService`, injected into the\nstore. Storage keys are class constants named `LS_*`:\n\n```ts\nexport class Todos {\n\tstatic readonly LS_HIDE_IT_KEY: string = 'todos_hideit';\n\t// …\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nthis.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n```\n\n- Always go through `LocalStorageService` — it guards `browser` internally, so\n  callers do not have to.\n- Keys are `snake_case` strings (`'todos_hideit'`, `'custom_api_url'`).\n- Restore persisted state in the constructor, and re-read it in `load()` when a\n  value could have changed while the initial load was in flight (see\n  `Todos.loadHideIt()`). Auth tokens are the one exception handled by `Auth`\n  itself.\n\n## Browser and route imports — guard them\n\n- `browser` from `$app/environment` guards anything that touches `window`,\n  `document` or `localStorage`. `LocalStorageService` does this internally; a\n  store that touches the DOM directly must do the same. `Viewpoint` guards its\n  entire initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n- `page` from `$app/state` is read for route information (e.g.\n  `page.url.searchParams` in `Todos.checkUrlForFilter()`). Read it; do not\n  subscribe to navigation inside the store.\n- If a store registers listeners or timers, clean them up in an explicit\n  `destroy()` method and call it from the owner component's `onDestroy`.\n  `Viewpoint` collects each cleanup closure in an array and runs them all in\n  `destroy()`.\n\n## Stores may depend on other stores\n\nA store may read another store or the translation table when its logic needs\nthem:\n\n- `QuickAdd` reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()` for its error\n  messages, and `getAuth()` for the API client.\n- `Translation` reads `getAuth()` to pick the user's language.\n\nResolve these dependencies once in the constructor (or as defaults), not on\nevery method call, and never create a cycle. Keep the dependency in the\nconstructor's parameter list where practical so tests can inject it\n(`docs/TESTING.md` §4 gives `QuickAdd` as the `ts`/`notifications` example).\n\n## Read-only view state via getters\n\nWhen a store owns computed state that consumers must not write, expose it\nthrough getters. `Viewpoint` keeps its data in a `private _state` and returns\n`get state()`, `get width()`, `get isDesktop()`, etc.:\n\n```ts\nprivate _state = $state<ViewPointState>({ width: 0, height: 0, isDesktop: false, isMobile: true, isTablet: false });\n\nget isDesktop() {\n\treturn this._state.isDesktop;\n}\n```\n\nUse this for genuinely read-only derivations (screen class, computed URL\nflags). For normal domain data, keep the public `$state` field — getters for\neverything add noise.\n\n## What not to do\n\n- **No markup, DOM, or UI strings** in a store. That is the component layer's\n  job.\n- **No hardcoded API URLs.** Every endpoint comes from\n  `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`; never build a URL string by hand.\n- **No inline `fetch`.** `ApiService` is the single network seam; a store calls\n  it and nothing else. (The only exceptions are the few legacy direct-`fetch`\n  methods in `Calendars` — do not copy them.)\n- **No giant methods.** Split by named steps (`loadCategories`, `useFilters`).\n- **No new global singletons.** Use the context pattern; do not export a\n  module-level `new Todos()`.\n- **No `$derived` dumping ground.** Derived values that belong in a method or a\n  service stay there; see [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline).\n- Do not add an abstraction a store does not already use.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n- [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — `ApiService`, `apiRoutes`, services,\n  helpers, types, i18n.\n- [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components read these stores.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §3–4 — the store test recipe and the\n  constructor-injection refactor.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":328,"totalLines":328,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/STATE_SERVICES.md","time":{"start":1791640064674,"end":1791640064708}},"id":"prt_12611d224001JrcrX0TOBv8CBN","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","messageID":"msg_12611c8c8001ghp5nc6Pw5mSug"}}
