{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640157374,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_a7211c84f3a94b1c94ccfae8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && git diff AGENTS.md && echo \"=== sed STATE_SERVICES head ===\" && sed -n '1,7p' docs/STATE_SERVICES.md && echo \"=== DATA_LAYER nav + i18n fix ===\" && sed -n '160,166p' docs/DATA_LAYER.md && sed -n '191,196p' docs/DATA_LAYER.md"},"output":"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex 63d299c..52b4cb4 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -49,6 +49,14 @@ The client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one per\n - `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n - Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n \n+## Coding policies\n+When writing or reviewing code, follow the policy set in `docs/` — the rules are grounded in this repo's actual idioms, and AI agents should treat them as binding:\n+- `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` — general in-file principles (readability, DRY, early returns, naming, comments, `$derived`, tooling)\n+- `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — the `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer\n+- `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` UI layer\n+- `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/` and the data flow\n+- `docs/TESTING.md` — the test coverage plan (\"test logic and contracts, not markup, not third-party internals\")\n+\n ## Commands\n - `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n - `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n=== sed STATE_SERVICES head ===\n# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ncommunication with the API. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n=== DATA_LAYER nav + i18n fix ===\n  computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n  ad-hoc flags to components.\n- **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n  `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n  `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n- **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n  `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n## i18n — four locales, typed keys\n\n`src/lib/i18n/` has exactly four translation tables — `en.ts`, `de.ts`,\n`es.ts`, `fr.ts` — typed by `src/lib/types/translation.ts` (`LanguageFile`) so\na key missing from any locale (or a stray key) is a compile error.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex 63d299c..52b4cb4 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -49,6 +49,14 @@ The client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one per\n - `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n - Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n \n+## Coding policies\n+When writing or reviewing code, follow the policy set in `docs/` — the rules are grounded in this repo's actual idioms, and AI agents should treat them as binding:\n+- `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` — general in-file principles (readability, DRY, early returns, naming, comments, `$derived`, tooling)\n+- `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — the `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer\n+- `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` UI layer\n+- `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/` and the data flow\n+- `docs/TESTING.md` — the test coverage plan (\"test logic and contracts, not markup, not third-party internals\")\n+\n ## Commands\n - `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n - `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n=== sed STATE_SERVICES head ===\n# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ncommunication with the API. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n=== DATA_LAYER nav + i18n fix ===\n  computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n  ad-hoc flags to components.\n- **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n  `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n  `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n- **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n  `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n## i18n — four locales, typed keys\n\n`src/lib/i18n/` has exactly four translation tables — `en.ts`, `de.ts`,\n`es.ts`, `fr.ts` — typed by `src/lib/types/translation.ts` (`LanguageFile`) so\na key missing from any locale (or a stray key) is a compile error.\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && git diff AGENTS.md && echo \"=== sed STATE_SERVICES head ===\" && sed -n '1,7p' docs/STATE_SERVICES.md && echo \"=== DATA_LAYER nav + i18n fix ===\" && sed -n '160,166p' docs/DATA_LAYER.md && sed -n '191,196p' docs/DATA_LAYER.md","time":{"start":1791640157280,"end":1791640157328}},"id":"prt_126133813001um4LYsLbcOLOOO","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4bacaffe2fU0aQS8EF17gR","messageID":"msg_126130e0b001LL4oD39RGMLWwJ"}}
