{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640265071,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_Z9IC2E57pZx8rtFRfpko1366","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/brief.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief: svelte best practices\n2: \n3: type: feature\n4: id: cut\n5: branch: feature/cut_svelte-best-practices\n6: date: 2026-10-10\n7: author: Leander Muskalla\n8: \n9: ## What\n10: \n11: Can you analyze our app repository and try to gather a policy set HOW we build stuff? Most of the app I've developed myself in a way that makes sense and adheres to best practices, is easy to read and easy to work with. When I let AI do stuff, it's sometimes okay, but sometimes meh. So I'd like to build a policy set of how to do things inside of solyto app, e.g. easy-to-read, specific state services, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested short-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on $derived, etc. Write it to docs/*.md.\n12: \n13: ## Why\n14: \n15: <!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n16: \n17: ## Out of scope\n18: \n19: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n20: \n21: ## Notes\n22: \n23: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Coding policies\nWhen writing or reviewing code, follow the policy set in `docs/` — the rules are grounded in this repo's actual idioms, and AI agents should treat them as binding:\n- `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` — general in-file principles (readability, DRY, early returns, naming, comments, `$derived`, tooling)\n- `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — the `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer\n- `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` UI layer\n- `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/` and the data flow\n- `docs/TESTING.md` — the test coverage plan (\"test logic and contracts, not markup, not third-party internals\")\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief: svelte best practices\n\ntype: feature\nid: cut\nbranch: feature/cut_svelte-best-practices\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nCan you analyze our app repository and try to gather a policy set HOW we build stuff? Most of the app I've developed myself in a way that makes sense and adheres to best practices, is easy to read and easy to work with. When I let AI do stuff, it's sometimes okay, but sometimes meh. So I'd like to build a policy set of how to do things inside of solyto app, e.g. easy-to-read, specific state services, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested short-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on $derived, etc. Write it to docs/*.md.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/brief.md","text":"# Brief: svelte best practices\n\ntype: feature\nid: cut\nbranch: feature/cut_svelte-best-practices\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nCan you analyze our app repository and try to gather a policy set HOW we build stuff? Most of the app I've developed myself in a way that makes sense and adheres to best practices, is easy to read and easy to work with. When I let AI do stuff, it's sometimes okay, but sometimes meh. So I'd like to build a policy set of how to do things inside of solyto app, e.g. easy-to-read, specific state services, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested short-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on $derived, etc. Write it to docs/*.md.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n\n## Notes\n\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":23,"totalLines":23,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/brief.md","time":{"start":1791640264883,"end":1791640265033}},"id":"prt_12614e060001lAbVFJHShqm73E","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12614d9c3001wptqhN03qawfLK"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640265163,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_F1HEWzgkD8bJRdlGOh5Q8587","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: svelte best practices\n2: \n3: id: cut\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: deepseek-v4-flash\n6: date: 2026-10-10\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Context\n11: \n12: The brief asks for a **policy set of how we build things in solyto** — a\n13: conventions/standards guide that a human (and, importantly, an AI agent) can\n14: follow so new code matches the existing style: \"easy-to-read, specific state\n15: services, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested\n16: short-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on `$derived`, etc.\" The deliverable is\n17: **documentation written to `docs/*.md`**. This is a **docs-only job: no files\n18: under `src/` are changed.**\n19: \n20: This is a frontend-only repo. The conventions must be **grounded in the actual\n21: code**, not generic Svelte advice — the value is capturing the author's real\n22: idioms: the `setX()`/`getX()` context-singleton stores, `auth.apiService`,\n23: endpoints only via `config/apiRoutes.ts`, `ts.get.*` i18n, `$state` class\n24: fields, constructor DI with defaults, `import type`, Tailwind `c-*` theme\n25: tokens, desktop/mobile view variants, early returns, and \"comments explain why\".\n26: \n27: ### What already exists (do not duplicate)\n28: \n29: - `docs/AGENTS.md` — the project context/architecture summary loaded every\n30:   session. The policy docs should be **consistent with it** and are the natural\n31:   detail behind its \"Architecture\" and \"Hard rules\" sections.\n32: - `docs/TESTING.md` — an existing, single-topic testing policy. The policy set\n33:   must **reference/summarise** it, not rewrite it.\n34: \n35: ### Deliverable layout (analyst decision)\n36: \n37: Produce a **small, focused set of top-level docs in `docs/`** rather than one\n38: monolith. The brief says \"policy set\" and \"`docs/*.md`\", each area is a\n39: different concern, and smaller docs are easier to read and to point agents at\n40: (the repo already uses one topical doc per concern — `TESTING.md`). The set:\n41: \n42: | Doc                     | Owns                                                                 |\n43: | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n44: | `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`| Entry point + general in-file code principles (applies everywhere)   |\n45: | `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`| The `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer                                |\n46: | `docs/COMPONENTS.md`    | The `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` UI layer             |\n47: | `docs/DATA_LAYER.md`    | `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/`, data flow     |\n48: \n49: If the author would rather have a **single** `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` containing\n50: all of it, that is a trivial merge of the four files — see Notes; do not\n51: silently pick the other option.\n52: \n53: ## Task breakdown\n54: \n55: TASK-1: Write `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` — the entry point and the general, cross-cutting engineering principles that every other doc assumes.\n56:      content: purpose and how to use the policy set (for humans and for AI contributors); \"readability first\" as the top rule; DRY *without* premature abstraction (tie to the AGENTS.md hard rule \"do not add abstractions not already present\"); small, single-purpose functions; explicit **early returns** and **no nested short-ifs / no `else` after a `return`** (show the preferred shape); naming (booleans, handlers, stores); comments that explain **why**/non-obvious constraints (cite the explanatory comments in `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` `load()` and `src/lib/state/Viewpoint.svelte.ts`), not \"what\"; `$derived` discipline — use it only for genuine derivations read in the template, not as a dumping ground for transforms that belong in a function/service or a `$state` set by a method (cite `src/routes/+layout.svelte`'s `canAccessRoute` as the legitimate use); TypeScript strict + `import type`; formatting/tooling (4-space tabs, single quotes, `printWidth: 100`, prettier + `prettier-plugin-svelte`/`tailwindcss`, eslint, `npm run check`); the **testing stance** — one short section that points at `docs/TESTING.md` and states the rule \"test logic and contracts, not markup, not third-party internals\"; a short \"related docs\" index linking the three sibling docs. Establish a consistent heading/tone convention the sibling docs follow.\n57:      files: docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md\n58:      depends: none\n59:      risk: low — documentation only; sets the shared tone for the other docs, so it should land first.\n60: \n61: TASK-2: Write `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — the policy for the state-service layer (`src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`), grounded in real examples.\n62:      content: one runes class per domain, one file per domain; the context-singleton pattern (private `Symbol` key + `setX()`/`getX()` pair, instances created once in `src/routes/+layout.svelte`); reactive state as `$state` class fields; **member ordering** (state fields → collaborators/deps → constructor → methods); **constructor dependency injection with defaults that preserve zero-arg construction** (`auth = getAuth()`, `apiService = auth.apiService`, `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()`) — contrast the preferred injectable style (`Todos`, `Clipboard` after the TESTING.md refactor) with the older field-initializer style and codify the preferred one; the `load()` + `loaded` flag convention; the **CRUD method pattern** (call `ApiService`, `if (res) await this.load()`, return boolean) and an explicit note that its repetitiveness is intentional, not something to \"DRY up\" with a generic helper; delegate pure logic to `services/` (e.g. `Todos` → `TodoFilterService`/`TodoSortingService`/`TodoGroupingService`/`TodoRelevanceService`); persistence via `LocalStorageService` with a `static readonly LS_*_KEY` (cite `Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`); use of `page` from `$app/state` and `browser` from `$app/environment` (guards!), plus lifecycle/`destroy()` cleanup (cite `Viewpoint`); stores may read other stores/translation (cite `QuickAdd`); read-only view state via getters (cite `Viewpoint`); what **not** to do (no markup/UI, no hardcoded API URLs, no inline `fetch` where `ApiService` exists, keep methods small). Cross-link `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` and `docs/DATA_LAYER.md`.\n63:      files: docs/STATE_SERVICES.md\n64:      depends: TASK-1\n65:      risk: low — documentation only; source is well understood from TASK files and the codebase.\n66: \n67: TASK-3: Write `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the policy for Svelte components (`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` `.svelte` files), grounded in real examples.\n68:      content: components are **lean** — read context stores once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">` (`const todos = getTodos();`) and delegate logic to the store/service; type props with `$props<{...}>()`; Svelte 5 syntax (event attributes like `onclick`, snippets, `{@render children?.()}`) — no Svelte 4 `on:click`/`createEventDispatcher`/`export let`; keep markup declarative and **extract non-trivial conditions into functions or booleans** rather than nesting short-ifs/ternaries in markup (cite the long ternary class in `src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte` as an anti-pattern to flag); prefer the shared `ui/` and `forms/` primitives over hand-rolled controls; the desktop/mobile split convention (`views/`, `*Mobile.svelte`, `Viewpoint`); Tailwind conventions (`c-*` theme tokens, `dark:` variants, class ordering via `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`, `size-*`, `class:` directives); icons from `@lucide/svelte/icons/*`; i18n via `ts.get.*` (all four locale files stay in sync); local UI state via `$state`; loading feedback via `getLoadingIndicator()`; keyboard handling via `getKeyManager()` register/unregister in `onDestroy` (cite `Title.svelte`); accessibility caveats (the two intentionally-ignored `svelte-check` warnings mean a click handler must still get keyboard/tabindex handling); testability (props-driven leaves are the cleanest targets — cite `docs/TESTING.md` §8). Cross-link `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`.\n69:      files: docs/COMPONENTS.md\n70:      depends: TASK-1\n71:      risk: low — documentation only.\n72: \n73: TASK-4: Write `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — the policy for the non-UI layers (`services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/`) and the app's data flow.\n74:      content: the one-directional data flow (route/component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API at `/api/v1`) and the fact that **all routes are client-rendered** (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts`/`load` functions anywhere) so data is fetched by stores, not by routes; `ApiService` is the **single network seam** (`list/get/create/update/delete/post/put/postFormData`, Bearer token from `Auth`, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, JSON/FormData bodies, null/boolean error semantics) — never call `fetch` directly for app data; endpoints live **only** in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`; pure domain `services/*Service.ts` (no constructor side-effects, one responsibility, unit-tested) with the naming convention; pure `helpers/*Helper.ts`; `config/` responsibilities (`platform.ts` web/desktop/mobile + API URL resolution order, `features.ts` flags, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `themes.ts`); `types/` one file per domain mirroring the API, always `import type` (note the two files with runtime values, `check_in.ts`/`quick_add.ts`); `i18n/` — `en/de/es/fr` kept in sync and typed via `types/translation.ts`, read through `getTranslation().get`; `LocalStorageService` is the only persistence. Cross-link `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` and `docs/AGENTS.md`.\n75:      files: docs/DATA_LAYER.md\n76:      depends: TASK-1\n77:      risk: low — documentation only.\n78: \n79: TASK-5: Add a short \"Coding policies\" pointer to `docs/AGENTS.md` so the policy set is discoverable and loaded into future agent sessions.\n80:      content: append a concise section (or a few bullets under an existing heading) linking to `BEST_PRACTICES.md`, `STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` and pointing at `TESTING.md`. Keep it to a handful of lines; do **not** restructure or rewrite AGENTS.md. This is a **judgment call** (an extension beyond the strict \"write docs/*.md\"): if the author prefers AGENTS.md untouched, this task is dropped and nothing else changes — flag that in the implementation notes rather than deciding silently.\n81:      files: docs/AGENTS.md\n82:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n83:      risk: low — small doc edit; but it touches the shared project-context file, so the author/reviewer should confirm the pointer is wanted.\n84: \n85: TASK-6: Consistency, cross-reference, and accuracy pass over the whole policy set.\n86:      content: re-read all four docs (plus the AGENTS.md pointer) together; remove contradictions and duplication; make headings/tone/cross-links uniform; verify **every** cited file path exists and every claim matches the code (spot-check each referenced idiom against the file it names); ensure the sibling docs actually follow the principles stated in `BEST_PRACTICES.md`; confirm the markdown renders (tables, code fences); and confirm no `src/**` or other source file was modified. Fix as needed.\n87:      files: docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md; docs/STATE_SERVICES.md; docs/COMPONENTS.md; docs/DATA_LAYER.md; docs/AGENTS.md\n88:      depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n89:      risk: low — documentation-only review pass.\n90: \n91: ## Notes / open questions\n92: \n93: - **Doc layout is an analyst decision, not settled by the brief.** The brief says\n94:   \"policy set … `docs/*.md`\". I split it into four top-level docs (see Context).\n95:   Merging them into one `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` instead is a trivial\n96:   reorganization — if the author prefers one file, do that; if they prefer a\n97:   `docs/policies/` subfolder, adjust the paths. Flag the chosen layout in the\n98:   implementation notes.\n99: - **No source changes.** This job only adds policy documents (and optionally the\n100:   AGENTS.md pointer). Implementing any rule, or retro-fitting existing code to it,\n101:   is out of scope and should become separate jobs.\n102: - **Do not duplicate `docs/TESTING.md`.** The policy set references it and states\n103:   the testing philosophy in one short section; the detailed coverage plan stays\n104:   where it is.\n105: - **Grounding requirement.** Every rule should cite a real file/idiom from this\n106:   repo (state stores, components, services, config) — a generic Svelte style guide\n107:   would not achieve the brief's goal of making AI output match the author's style.\n108: - **Branch:** `brief.md` specifies `feature/cut_svelte-best-practices`. This\n109:   analyst session had no shell, so `git branch --show-current` could not be run;\n110:   the mounted worktree is assumed to be on the job branch (per the pipeline's\n111:   worktree guarantee). No `git checkout` is needed.\n112: - **No render report / screenshots exist for this job** (it produces docs, not UI),\n113:   so no rendered ground truth is relevant.\n\n(End of file - total 113 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: svelte best practices\n\nid: cut\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe brief asks for a **policy set of how we build things in solyto** — a\nconventions/standards guide that a human (and, importantly, an AI agent) can\nfollow so new code matches the existing style: \"easy-to-read, specific state\nservices, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested\nshort-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on `$derived`, etc.\" The deliverable is\n**documentation written to `docs/*.md`**. This is a **docs-only job: no files\nunder `src/` are changed.**\n\nThis is a frontend-only repo. The conventions must be **grounded in the actual","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: svelte best practices\n\nid: cut\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\nThe brief asks for a **policy set of how we build things in solyto** — a\nconventions/standards guide that a human (and, importantly, an AI agent) can\nfollow so new code matches the existing style: \"easy-to-read, specific state\nservices, dry, functions don't do too much, components are lean, no nested\nshort-ifs, no unnecessary reliance on `$derived`, etc.\" The deliverable is\n**documentation written to `docs/*.md`**. This is a **docs-only job: no files\nunder `src/` are changed.**\n\nThis is a frontend-only repo. The conventions must be **grounded in the actual\ncode**, not generic Svelte advice — the value is capturing the author's real\nidioms: the `setX()`/`getX()` context-singleton stores, `auth.apiService`,\nendpoints only via `config/apiRoutes.ts`, `ts.get.*` i18n, `$state` class\nfields, constructor DI with defaults, `import type`, Tailwind `c-*` theme\ntokens, desktop/mobile view variants, early returns, and \"comments explain why\".\n\n### What already exists (do not duplicate)\n\n- `docs/AGENTS.md` — the project context/architecture summary loaded every\n  session. The policy docs should be **consistent with it** and are the natural\n  detail behind its \"Architecture\" and \"Hard rules\" sections.\n- `docs/TESTING.md` — an existing, single-topic testing policy. The policy set\n  must **reference/summarise** it, not rewrite it.\n\n### Deliverable layout (analyst decision)\n\nProduce a **small, focused set of top-level docs in `docs/`** rather than one\nmonolith. The brief says \"policy set\" and \"`docs/*.md`\", each area is a\ndifferent concern, and smaller docs are easier to read and to point agents at\n(the repo already uses one topical doc per concern — `TESTING.md`). The set:\n\n| Doc                     | Owns                                                                 |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`| Entry point + general in-file code principles (applies everywhere)   |\n| `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`| The `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer                                |\n| `docs/COMPONENTS.md`    | The `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` UI layer             |\n| `docs/DATA_LAYER.md`    | `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/`, data flow     |\n\nIf the author would rather have a **single** `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` containing\nall of it, that is a trivial merge of the four files — see Notes; do not\nsilently pick the other option.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Write `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` — the entry point and the general, cross-cutting engineering principles that every other doc assumes.\n     content: purpose and how to use the policy set (for humans and for AI contributors); \"readability first\" as the top rule; DRY *without* premature abstraction (tie to the AGENTS.md hard rule \"do not add abstractions not already present\"); small, single-purpose functions; explicit **early returns** and **no nested short-ifs / no `else` after a `return`** (show the preferred shape); naming (booleans, handlers, stores); comments that explain **why**/non-obvious constraints (cite the explanatory comments in `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` `load()` and `src/lib/state/Viewpoint.svelte.ts`), not \"what\"; `$derived` discipline — use it only for genuine derivations read in the template, not as a dumping ground for transforms that belong in a function/service or a `$state` set by a method (cite `src/routes/+layout.svelte`'s `canAccessRoute` as the legitimate use); TypeScript strict + `import type`; formatting/tooling (4-space tabs, single quotes, `printWidth: 100`, prettier + `prettier-plugin-svelte`/`tailwindcss`, eslint, `npm run check`); the **testing stance** — one short section that points at `docs/TESTING.md` and states the rule \"test logic and contracts, not markup, not third-party internals\"; a short \"related docs\" index linking the three sibling docs. Establish a consistent heading/tone convention the sibling docs follow.\n     files: docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — documentation only; sets the shared tone for the other docs, so it should land first.\n\nTASK-2: Write `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` — the policy for the state-service layer (`src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`), grounded in real examples.\n     content: one runes class per domain, one file per domain; the context-singleton pattern (private `Symbol` key + `setX()`/`getX()` pair, instances created once in `src/routes/+layout.svelte`); reactive state as `$state` class fields; **member ordering** (state fields → collaborators/deps → constructor → methods); **constructor dependency injection with defaults that preserve zero-arg construction** (`auth = getAuth()`, `apiService = auth.apiService`, `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()`) — contrast the preferred injectable style (`Todos`, `Clipboard` after the TESTING.md refactor) with the older field-initializer style and codify the preferred one; the `load()` + `loaded` flag convention; the **CRUD method pattern** (call `ApiService`, `if (res) await this.load()`, return boolean) and an explicit note that its repetitiveness is intentional, not something to \"DRY up\" with a generic helper; delegate pure logic to `services/` (e.g. `Todos` → `TodoFilterService`/`TodoSortingService`/`TodoGroupingService`/`TodoRelevanceService`); persistence via `LocalStorageService` with a `static readonly LS_*_KEY` (cite `Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`); use of `page` from `$app/state` and `browser` from `$app/environment` (guards!), plus lifecycle/`destroy()` cleanup (cite `Viewpoint`); stores may read other stores/translation (cite `QuickAdd`); read-only view state via getters (cite `Viewpoint`); what **not** to do (no markup/UI, no hardcoded API URLs, no inline `fetch` where `ApiService` exists, keep methods small). Cross-link `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` and `docs/DATA_LAYER.md`.\n     files: docs/STATE_SERVICES.md\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — documentation only; source is well understood from TASK files and the codebase.\n\nTASK-3: Write `docs/COMPONENTS.md` — the policy for Svelte components (`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` `.svelte` files), grounded in real examples.\n     content: components are **lean** — read context stores once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">` (`const todos = getTodos();`) and delegate logic to the store/service; type props with `$props<{...}>()`; Svelte 5 syntax (event attributes like `onclick`, snippets, `{@render children?.()}`) — no Svelte 4 `on:click`/`createEventDispatcher`/`export let`; keep markup declarative and **extract non-trivial conditions into functions or booleans** rather than nesting short-ifs/ternaries in markup (cite the long ternary class in `src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte` as an anti-pattern to flag); prefer the shared `ui/` and `forms/` primitives over hand-rolled controls; the desktop/mobile split convention (`views/`, `*Mobile.svelte`, `Viewpoint`); Tailwind conventions (`c-*` theme tokens, `dark:` variants, class ordering via `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`, `size-*`, `class:` directives); icons from `@lucide/svelte/icons/*`; i18n via `ts.get.*` (all four locale files stay in sync); local UI state via `$state`; loading feedback via `getLoadingIndicator()`; keyboard handling via `getKeyManager()` register/unregister in `onDestroy` (cite `Title.svelte`); accessibility caveats (the two intentionally-ignored `svelte-check` warnings mean a click handler must still get keyboard/tabindex handling); testability (props-driven leaves are the cleanest targets — cite `docs/TESTING.md` §8). Cross-link `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`.\n     files: docs/COMPONENTS.md\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — documentation only.\n\nTASK-4: Write `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` — the policy for the non-UI layers (`services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/`) and the app's data flow.\n     content: the one-directional data flow (route/component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API at `/api/v1`) and the fact that **all routes are client-rendered** (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts`/`load` functions anywhere) so data is fetched by stores, not by routes; `ApiService` is the **single network seam** (`list/get/create/update/delete/post/put/postFormData`, Bearer token from `Auth`, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, JSON/FormData bodies, null/boolean error semantics) — never call `fetch` directly for app data; endpoints live **only** in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`; pure domain `services/*Service.ts` (no constructor side-effects, one responsibility, unit-tested) with the naming convention; pure `helpers/*Helper.ts`; `config/` responsibilities (`platform.ts` web/desktop/mobile + API URL resolution order, `features.ts` flags, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `themes.ts`); `types/` one file per domain mirroring the API, always `import type` (note the two files with runtime values, `check_in.ts`/`quick_add.ts`); `i18n/` — `en/de/es/fr` kept in sync and typed via `types/translation.ts`, read through `getTranslation().get`; `LocalStorageService` is the only persistence. Cross-link `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` and `docs/AGENTS.md`.\n     files: docs/DATA_LAYER.md\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — documentation only.\n\nTASK-5: Add a short \"Coding policies\" pointer to `docs/AGENTS.md` so the policy set is discoverable and loaded into future agent sessions.\n     content: append a concise section (or a few bullets under an existing heading) linking to `BEST_PRACTICES.md`, `STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` and pointing at `TESTING.md`. Keep it to a handful of lines; do **not** restructure or rewrite AGENTS.md. This is a **judgment call** (an extension beyond the strict \"write docs/*.md\"): if the author prefers AGENTS.md untouched, this task is dropped and nothing else changes — flag that in the implementation notes rather than deciding silently.\n     files: docs/AGENTS.md\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n     risk: low — small doc edit; but it touches the shared project-context file, so the author/reviewer should confirm the pointer is wanted.\n\nTASK-6: Consistency, cross-reference, and accuracy pass over the whole policy set.\n     content: re-read all four docs (plus the AGENTS.md pointer) together; remove contradictions and duplication; make headings/tone/cross-links uniform; verify **every** cited file path exists and every claim matches the code (spot-check each referenced idiom against the file it names); ensure the sibling docs actually follow the principles stated in `BEST_PRACTICES.md`; confirm the markdown renders (tables, code fences); and confirm no `src/**` or other source file was modified. Fix as needed.\n     files: docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md; docs/STATE_SERVICES.md; docs/COMPONENTS.md; docs/DATA_LAYER.md; docs/AGENTS.md\n     depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n     risk: low — documentation-only review pass.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- **Doc layout is an analyst decision, not settled by the brief.** The brief says\n  \"policy set … `docs/*.md`\". I split it into four top-level docs (see Context).\n  Merging them into one `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` instead is a trivial\n  reorganization — if the author prefers one file, do that; if they prefer a\n  `docs/policies/` subfolder, adjust the paths. Flag the chosen layout in the\n  implementation notes.\n- **No source changes.** This job only adds policy documents (and optionally the\n  AGENTS.md pointer). Implementing any rule, or retro-fitting existing code to it,\n  is out of scope and should become separate jobs.\n- **Do not duplicate `docs/TESTING.md`.** The policy set references it and states\n  the testing philosophy in one short section; the detailed coverage plan stays\n  where it is.\n- **Grounding requirement.** Every rule should cite a real file/idiom from this\n  repo (state stores, components, services, config) — a generic Svelte style guide\n  would not achieve the brief's goal of making AI output match the author's style.\n- **Branch:** `brief.md` specifies `feature/cut_svelte-best-practices`. This\n  analyst session had no shell, so `git branch --show-current` could not be run;\n  the mounted worktree is assumed to be on the job branch (per the pipeline's\n  worktree guarantee). No `git checkout` is needed.\n- **No render report / screenshots exist for this job** (it produces docs, not UI),\n  so no rendered ground truth is relevant.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":113,"totalLines":113,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791640265050,"end":1791640265158}},"id":"prt_12614e0cc001W0yMrVjz1Ize6W","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12614d9c3001wptqhN03qawfLK"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640265172,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_luOpOe4muEtvtTfOok5Z9339","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: svelte best practices\n2: \n3: id: cut\n4: developer: deepseek-v4-flash\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Summary\n10: \n11: Wrote a policy set — four top-level, cross-linked docs in `docs/` — capturing\n12: how the solyto frontend is actually built, so humans and AI contributors write\n13: code that matches the author's style. Every rule is grounded in a real file in\n14: this repo (state stores, components, services, config, types, i18n). This was a\n15: docs-only job: **no files under `src/` were touched.**\n16: \n17: Layout decision (analyst's recommended option, confirmed as-is): a small set of\n18: top-level docs — `BEST_PRACTICES.md` (entry point + general in-file rules),\n19: `STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` — rather than one\n20: monolith or a `docs/policies/` subfolder. `docs/TESTING.md` is referenced, not\n21: rewritten. A short \"Coding policies\" pointer was added to `docs/AGENTS.md` (and\n22: its mounted root copy `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, per the repo's tracked-mount\n23: pattern) so the set is discoverable in future agent sessions.\n24: \n25: ## Changes\n26: \n27: TASK-1 `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` (new) — entry point. Purpose/how-to-use for the\n28: set, readability-first, DRY without premature abstraction (quoting the AGENTS.md\n29: hard rule), small single-purpose functions, early returns / no nested short-ifs\n30: (with before/after example), naming conventions, why-comments (cited the\n31: explanatory comments in `Todos.svelte.ts` `load()` and the `Viewpoint` `if\n32: (browser)` guard), `$derived` discipline (cited `canAccessRoute` in\n33: `src/routes/+layout.svelte`), TypeScript strict + `import type`, exact\n34: formatting/tooling from `.prettierrc`/`eslint.config.js`/`package.json`, the\n35: one-paragraph testing stance pointing at `docs/TESTING.md`, and a related-docs\n36: index.\n37: \n38: TASK-2 `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` (new) — the `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer:\n39: one class per domain/file, context-singleton pattern (`Symbol` key + `setX()`/\n40: `getX()`, created in root or feature route layouts), `$state` fields, member\n41: ordering, preferred constructor DI with zero-arg-preserving defaults (cited\n42: `Todos`/`Finances`) vs. the older field-initializer style (cited `Clipboard`),\n43: `load()`+`loaded` convention, the intentional CRUD pattern (\"if (res) await\n44: this.load(); return ok\" — explicitly not to be DRYed up), delegation to\n45: `services/`, `LS_*` persistence keys, guarded `browser`/`page` imports and\n46: `destroy()` cleanup (cited `Viewpoint`), cross-store dependencies (cited\n47: `QuickAdd`), read-only getters, and a \"what not to do\" list.\n48: \n49: TASK-3 `docs/COMPONENTS.md` (new) — the UI layer: lean components that read\n50: stores once at the top of the script and delegate; `$props<{...}>()` typing;\n51: Svelte 5-only syntax (no `on:click`/`createEventDispatcher`/`export let` —\n52: verified zero across `src/`); extracting non-trivial conditions out of markup\n53: (flagged the `todos/props/Title.svelte` inline ternary as an anti-pattern);\n54: preferring shared `ui/`/`forms/` primitives; the desktop/mobile `views`/\n55: `*Mobile.svelte` convention driven by `Viewpoint`; Tailwind `c-*` tokens, `dark:`\n56: variants, `size-*`, `class:` directives and prettier-plugin-tailwindcss\n57: ordering; lucide icons; `ts.get.*` i18n with all four locales in sync; local\n58: `$state`; loading feedback via `getLoadingIndicator()`; `KeyManager`\n59: register/unregister in `onDestroy`; the two intentionally-ignored svelte-check\n60: a11y warnings and the keyboard/tabindex responsibility they waive; and\n61: testability (props-driven leaves, `docs/TESTING.md` §4/§8).\n62: \n63: TASK-4 `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` (new) — the non-UI layers and data flow:\n64: one-directional flow (route/component → store → `ApiService` → `/api/v1`), the\n65: client-rendered-only guarantee (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts`/`load`\n66: anywhere — verified), `ApiService` as the single network seam (full method\n67: table with URL placeholders, Bearer auth, null/false error semantics, one-shot\n68: 401 recovery), endpoints only in `config/apiRoutes.ts`, pure `*Service.ts` and\n69: `*Helper.ts` rules, per-file `config/` responsibilities (platform URL resolution\n70: order, features, navigation, urls, themes), `types/` mirroring the API (with\n71: the two runtime-value exceptions `check_in.ts`/`quick_add.ts`), the four-locale\n72: typed i18n, and `LocalStorageService` as the only persistence.\n73: \n74: TASK-5 `docs/AGENTS.md` (+ root `/workspace/AGENTS.md`) — added a concise\n75: \"## Coding policies\" section under Architecture pointing to the four new docs\n76: and `TESTING.md`. Deliberately minimal; the rest of AGENTS.md is untouched.\n77: Judgment call (flagging per the task): the pointer extends beyond the strict\n78: \"write docs/*.md\" brief; it is 8 lines and reversible if the author prefers\n79: AGENTS.md pristine.\n80: \n81: TASK-6 Consistency/accuracy pass — re-read all four docs together; verified\n82: every cited file path exists and every named idiom matches the code; fixed\n83: two inaccuracies found (`postFormData` success semantics in the ApiService\n84: table, and `navigation.ts`'s `mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount` — the\n85: task text's \"Clipboard after the TESTING.md refactor\" was also corrected:\n86: the refactor only covered `Todos`/`Finances`, `Clipboard` still uses the older\n87: style, which the doc now shows as the \"older\" example); balanced code fences,\n88: checked table rendering and heading-anchor links; confirmed no `src/**` files\n89: were modified.\n90: \n91: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n92: \n93: - **`docs/AGENTS.md` line 40** says the root `+layout.svelte` \"bootstraps every\n94:   state store via setContext\". In reality the root layout creates the app-wide\n95:   stores and each feature's stores are created in its own route layout\n96:   (`todos/+layout.svelte`, `libraries/books/+layout.svelte`, …). The new policy\n97:   docs describe the accurate picture; the AGENTS.md summary line was left as-is\n98:   because TASK-5 forbade restructuring it. Worth a one-line future fix.\n99: - **Task text vs. code** for the DI example: the analyst's `STATE_SERVICES.md`\n100:   task text listed \"```Todos```, ```Clipboard``` after the TESTING.md refactor\"\n101:   as the preferred style, but only `Todos`/`Finances` received the refactor.\n102:   The doc was grounded in the real code instead (preferred: `Todos`/`Finances`;\n103:   older: `Clipboard`/`QuickAdd`).\n104: - **`docs/TESTING.md` §0** describes `new Todos()` as capturing\n105:   `auth.getToken()` into its own `ApiService`; the current code defaults\n106:   `Todos`/`Finances` to the shared `auth.apiService` instance. Not changed (out\n107:   of scope) — if TESTING.md is next touched, that sentence could be aligned.\n108: - Nothing else outstanding; the docs-only scope was respected (`git status`\n109:   shows no `src/**` changes).\n\n(End of file - total 109 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: svelte best practices\n\nid: cut\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nWrote a policy set — four top-level, cross-linked docs in `docs/` — capturing\nhow the solyto frontend is actually built, so humans and AI contributors write\ncode that matches the author's style. Every rule is grounded in a real file in\nthis repo (state stores, components, services, config, types, i18n). This was a\ndocs-only job: **no files under `src/` were touched.**\n\nLayout decision (analyst's recommended option, confirmed as-is): a small set of\ntop-level docs — `BEST_PRACTICES.md` (entry point + general in-file rules),\n`STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` — rather than one\nmonolith or a `docs/policies/` subfolder. `docs/TESTING.md` is referenced, not","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: svelte best practices\n\nid: cut\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nWrote a policy set — four top-level, cross-linked docs in `docs/` — capturing\nhow the solyto frontend is actually built, so humans and AI contributors write\ncode that matches the author's style. Every rule is grounded in a real file in\nthis repo (state stores, components, services, config, types, i18n). This was a\ndocs-only job: **no files under `src/` were touched.**\n\nLayout decision (analyst's recommended option, confirmed as-is): a small set of\ntop-level docs — `BEST_PRACTICES.md` (entry point + general in-file rules),\n`STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` — rather than one\nmonolith or a `docs/policies/` subfolder. `docs/TESTING.md` is referenced, not\nrewritten. A short \"Coding policies\" pointer was added to `docs/AGENTS.md` (and\nits mounted root copy `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, per the repo's tracked-mount\npattern) so the set is discoverable in future agent sessions.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1 `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` (new) — entry point. Purpose/how-to-use for the\nset, readability-first, DRY without premature abstraction (quoting the AGENTS.md\nhard rule), small single-purpose functions, early returns / no nested short-ifs\n(with before/after example), naming conventions, why-comments (cited the\nexplanatory comments in `Todos.svelte.ts` `load()` and the `Viewpoint` `if\n(browser)` guard), `$derived` discipline (cited `canAccessRoute` in\n`src/routes/+layout.svelte`), TypeScript strict + `import type`, exact\nformatting/tooling from `.prettierrc`/`eslint.config.js`/`package.json`, the\none-paragraph testing stance pointing at `docs/TESTING.md`, and a related-docs\nindex.\n\nTASK-2 `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` (new) — the `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` layer:\none class per domain/file, context-singleton pattern (`Symbol` key + `setX()`/\n`getX()`, created in root or feature route layouts), `$state` fields, member\nordering, preferred constructor DI with zero-arg-preserving defaults (cited\n`Todos`/`Finances`) vs. the older field-initializer style (cited `Clipboard`),\n`load()`+`loaded` convention, the intentional CRUD pattern (\"if (res) await\nthis.load(); return ok\" — explicitly not to be DRYed up), delegation to\n`services/`, `LS_*` persistence keys, guarded `browser`/`page` imports and\n`destroy()` cleanup (cited `Viewpoint`), cross-store dependencies (cited\n`QuickAdd`), read-only getters, and a \"what not to do\" list.\n\nTASK-3 `docs/COMPONENTS.md` (new) — the UI layer: lean components that read\nstores once at the top of the script and delegate; `$props<{...}>()` typing;\nSvelte 5-only syntax (no `on:click`/`createEventDispatcher`/`export let` —\nverified zero across `src/`); extracting non-trivial conditions out of markup\n(flagged the `todos/props/Title.svelte` inline ternary as an anti-pattern);\npreferring shared `ui/`/`forms/` primitives; the desktop/mobile `views`/\n`*Mobile.svelte` convention driven by `Viewpoint`; Tailwind `c-*` tokens, `dark:`\nvariants, `size-*`, `class:` directives and prettier-plugin-tailwindcss\nordering; lucide icons; `ts.get.*` i18n with all four locales in sync; local\n`$state`; loading feedback via `getLoadingIndicator()`; `KeyManager`\nregister/unregister in `onDestroy`; the two intentionally-ignored svelte-check\na11y warnings and the keyboard/tabindex responsibility they waive; and\ntestability (props-driven leaves, `docs/TESTING.md` §4/§8).\n\nTASK-4 `docs/DATA_LAYER.md` (new) — the non-UI layers and data flow:\none-directional flow (route/component → store → `ApiService` → `/api/v1`), the\nclient-rendered-only guarantee (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts`/`load`\nanywhere — verified), `ApiService` as the single network seam (full method\ntable with URL placeholders, Bearer auth, null/false error semantics, one-shot\n401 recovery), endpoints only in `config/apiRoutes.ts`, pure `*Service.ts` and\n`*Helper.ts` rules, per-file `config/` responsibilities (platform URL resolution\norder, features, navigation, urls, themes), `types/` mirroring the API (with\nthe two runtime-value exceptions `check_in.ts`/`quick_add.ts`), the four-locale\ntyped i18n, and `LocalStorageService` as the only persistence.\n\nTASK-5 `docs/AGENTS.md` (+ root `/workspace/AGENTS.md`) — added a concise\n\"## Coding policies\" section under Architecture pointing to the four new docs\nand `TESTING.md`. Deliberately minimal; the rest of AGENTS.md is untouched.\nJudgment call (flagging per the task): the pointer extends beyond the strict\n\"write docs/*.md\" brief; it is 8 lines and reversible if the author prefers\nAGENTS.md pristine.\n\nTASK-6 Consistency/accuracy pass — re-read all four docs together; verified\nevery cited file path exists and every named idiom matches the code; fixed\ntwo inaccuracies found (`postFormData` success semantics in the ApiService\ntable, and `navigation.ts`'s `mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount` — the\ntask text's \"Clipboard after the TESTING.md refactor\" was also corrected:\nthe refactor only covered `Todos`/`Finances`, `Clipboard` still uses the older\nstyle, which the doc now shows as the \"older\" example); balanced code fences,\nchecked table rendering and heading-anchor links; confirmed no `src/**` files\nwere modified.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **`docs/AGENTS.md` line 40** says the root `+layout.svelte` \"bootstraps every\n  state store via setContext\". In reality the root layout creates the app-wide\n  stores and each feature's stores are created in its own route layout\n  (`todos/+layout.svelte`, `libraries/books/+layout.svelte`, …). The new policy\n  docs describe the accurate picture; the AGENTS.md summary line was left as-is\n  because TASK-5 forbade restructuring it. Worth a one-line future fix.\n- **Task text vs. code** for the DI example: the analyst's `STATE_SERVICES.md`\n  task text listed \"```Todos```, ```Clipboard``` after the TESTING.md refactor\"\n  as the preferred style, but only `Todos`/`Finances` received the refactor.\n  The doc was grounded in the real code instead (preferred: `Todos`/`Finances`;\n  older: `Clipboard`/`QuickAdd`).\n- **`docs/TESTING.md` §0** describes `new Todos()` as capturing\n  `auth.getToken()` into its own `ApiService`; the current code defaults\n  `Todos`/`Finances` to the shared `auth.apiService` instance. Not changed (out\n  of scope) — if TESTING.md is next touched, that sentence could be aligned.\n- Nothing else outstanding; the docs-only scope was respected (`git status`\n  shows no `src/**` changes).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":109,"totalLines":109,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/cut_svelte-best-practices/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791640265128,"end":1791640265167}},"id":"prt_12614e15e001ZwJzlwrVuGJclQ","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12614d9c3001wptqhN03qawfLK"}}
