{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640283073,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_F8tZF3SJ1iz7INdlnpFF5400","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # solyto coding policies\n2: \n3: General, cross-cutting rules for writing code in the solyto frontend. Every\n4: other policy document assumes these rules; this file is the entry point to the\n5: set.\n6: \n7: ## Purpose and how to use this set\n8: \n9: The solyto frontend is one SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 app maintained by a small\n10: number of people, most of it written by hand in a consistent style. These\n11: documents capture that style so new code — whether written by a person or by an\n12: AI assistant — reads like the rest of the codebase instead of like a generic\n13: Svelte tutorial.\n14: \n15: There are four policy documents, each owning one layer:\n16: \n17: | Document                                       | Owns                                                                        |\n18: | ---------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n19: | **`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`** (this file)       | General in-file rules that apply everywhere                                 |\n20: | [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md)  | The state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`                                 |\n21: | [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md)          | The UI layer: `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` `.svelte` files    |\n22: | [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)          | `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/` and the data flow      |\n23: \n24: `docs/TESTING.md` is the companion testing policy and is referenced from the\n25: \"Testing\" section below rather than duplicated here. `docs/AGENTS.md` remains\n26: the top-level architecture summary.\n27: \n28: **How to use it:** read this file first, then jump to the document for the\n29: layer you are touching. Every rule is grounded in a real file in this repo —\n30: when in doubt, open the cited file and copy its shape. If a rule and the\n31: existing code disagree, the rule is wrong; fix the rule.\n32: \n33: ## Readability first\n34: \n35: The top rule, and the reason the others exist: code is read far more often than\n36: it is written. Optimise for the next person reading it, not for the fewest\n37: lines or the cleverest expression.\n38: \n39: - Prefer an obvious implementation over a compact one. A five-line function\n40:   with clear names beats a one-line chain of `reduce`/ternaries.\n41: - Match the surrounding file. The codebase has an established shape for stores,\n42:   components, services and config — imitate the nearest example instead of\n43:   inventing a new pattern.\n44: - A reader should be able to follow a function top to bottom without jumping\n45:   around to understand control flow.\n46: \n47: This trade-off is deliberate: the repo accepts some repetition (see\n48: [`STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md#the-crud-method-pattern)) in exchange\n49: for predictable, greppable, obvious code.\n50: \n51: ## DRY — but not prematurely\n52: \n53: Duplication is a smell, but a premature abstraction is worse: it hides two\n54: slightly-different things behind one helper and makes both harder to change.\n55: `docs/AGENTS.md` states the hard rule directly:\n56: \n57: > Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase.\n58: \n59: - Extract a helper when the same logic appears **three or more times** and the\n60:   cases genuinely do the same thing. Two similar-looking blocks are allowed to\n61:   stay separate.\n62: - Do not introduce base classes, generics, factories, or \"flexible\" options\n63:   objects the codebase does not already use.\n64: - When logic is shared, put it in a named, single-purpose module\n65:   (`src/lib/helpers/*Helper.ts` for pure utilities, `src/lib/services/*Service.ts`\n66:   for domain logic) — not in a god-object or inline in a component.\n67: - Repetition that mirrors an external contract (e.g. the CRUD methods in the\n68:   state layer) is intentional and should be left alone.\n69: \n70: If you cannot point at an existing pattern for the abstraction you are about to\n71: add, do not add it.\n72: \n73: ## Small, single-purpose functions\n74: \n75: A function should do one thing and its name should say what that is.\n76: \n77: - Keep functions short enough to read without scrolling. If a function has\n78:   several distinct phases, each phase is usually its own function.\n79: - No side effects hidden behind an innocuous name. A function called\n80:   `getScoredTodos` returns scored todos; it does not also mutate storage.\n81: - Split a long method by extracting named steps. In `Todos.svelte.ts`, `load()`\n82:   reads as a sequence of named operations — `loadCategories()`,\n83:   `loadWorkspaces()`, `loadHideIt()`, `groupByStatus()` — rather than one long\n84:   body.\n85: - Pure logic belongs in `services/`/`helpers/`, not mixed into UI or state\n86:   glue. `Todos` delegates filtering, sorting and grouping to\n87:   `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService` and `TodoGroupingService`.\n88: \n89: ## Early returns — no nested short-ifs\n90: \n91: Guard clauses are the default. Handle the exceptional or terminal cases first\n92: and return, so the rest of the function stays at one level of nesting.\n93: \n94: **Do not** wrap a whole function body in an `if` when the inverted condition\n95: lets you return early, and **do not** write `else` after a branch that already\n96: returns.\n97: \n98: ```ts\n99: // preferred — flat, each guard on its own line\n100: function label(todo: Todo): string {\n101: \tif (todo.is_completed) return 'done';\n102: \tif (todo.status === 'backlog') return 'backlog';\n103: \treturn 'open';\n104: }\n105: \n106: // avoid — inverted condition nested over the whole body\n107: function label(todo: Todo): string {\n108: \tif (!todo.is_completed) {\n109: \t\tif (todo.status !== 'backlog') {\n110: \t\t\treturn 'open';\n111: \t\t}\n112: \t\treturn 'backlog';\n113: \t}\n114: \treturn 'done';\n115: }\n116: ```\n117: \n118: Real examples: `Todos.loadHideIt()`, `QuickAdd.detect()`/`confirm()`, and\n119: `Viewpoint`'s `if (browser)` guard all bail out early instead of nesting the\n120: main path. One-line guards with a bare `return` (`if (!res) return;`) are\n121: preferred over a nested `else`.\n122: \n123: This is a readability rule, not an anti-`if` rule: a single, shallow `if/else`\n124: with balanced branches is fine. The thing to avoid is a ladder of nested\n125: `if/else` and short ternaries that force the reader to hold several conditions\n126: in their head at once.\n127: \n128: ## Naming\n129: \n130: Names carry the structure of the code; be consistent with the existing ones.\n131: \n132: - **Booleans** read as assertions: `loaded`, `isDesktop`, `isMobile`,\n133:   `hideItActive`, `sortByScore`, `todosScored`, `needsConfirmation`. Prefix\n134:   with `is`/`has`/`should` when the bare noun is ambiguous.\n135: - **Handlers** in components: `onclick`-style attributes reference a function\n136:   whose name describes the action — `toggleChangeTitle`, `setExplanationBoxPosition`,\n137:   or the conventional `handleEnter`/`handleEscape`. Form callbacks use the\n138:   short `onsubmit`/`onblur`/`oninput` when they mirror the DOM event.\n139: - **State classes** are nouns (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`); their context\n140:   accessors are `setX()` / `getX()` (see\n141:   [`STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md#the-context-singleton-pattern)).\n142: - **Methods** are verbs: `load`, `useFilters`, `groupByStatus`, `toggleHideIt`.\n143:   Getters that expose derived read-only values are named after the value\n144:   (`isUrl`, `isDesktop`).\n145: - **Constants** are `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` and scoped to the class that owns them:\n146:   `Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`, `TODOS_KEY`. Storage keys always start with `LS_`.\n147: - Files map to the class: `Todos.svelte.ts`, `ApiService.ts`, `TodoFilterService.ts`.\n148: \n149: ## Comments explain why, not what\n150: \n151: The code says what it does; a comment earns its place by explaining **why** —\n152: the non-obvious constraint, the reason for the awkward-looking order, the bug\n153: being avoided.\n154: \n155: `Todos.svelte.ts` is the reference:\n156: \n157: ```ts\n158: // Restore synchronously so every filter pass (including the ones run by\n159: // load() before the workspaces request resolves) already sees the\n160: // persisted value instead of the default false.\n161: this.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n162: ```\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165: // Always re-apply hide-it once the parallel loads settled: a failed\n166: // or rejected workspaces/categories request must not skip this.\n167: ```\n168: \n169: `Viewpoint.svelte.ts` shows the complementary case: the non-obvious constraint\n170: is that browser APIs only exist in the browser, so the constructor guards the\n171: whole initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n172: \n173: - Do **not** narrate the obvious (`// increment i`).\n174: - Do **not** leave commented-out code; git remembers it.\n175: - Prefer a short block comment above a tricky block over line-by-line comments\n176:   inside it.\n177: \n178: ## `$derived` discipline\n179: \n180: Use `$derived` only for a genuine derivation of other reactive state that is\n181: read while rendering. It is not a place to stash transformations that belong in\n182: a function, a service, or a `$state` field set by a method.\n183: \n184: The legitimate use is `src/routes/+layout.svelte`:\n185: \n186: ```ts\n187: const canAccessRoute = $derived(auth.loggedIn || isAuthRoute() || isSetupRoute());\n188: ```\n189: \n190: `canAccessRoute` is a pure function of existing state and is consumed in the\n191: template, so it stays correct automatically.\n192: \n193: - Deriving from one or two reactive reads with no side effects: fine.\n194: - Hiding a chain of `.filter().map().sort()` behind `$derived`: move it into a\n195:   method or service (`Todos.useFilters` is a method, not a `$derived`).\n196: - A value that is recomputed by an explicit method (e.g. `filteredTodos` after\n197:   a filter change or a reload): keep it as `$state` and assign it in the\n198:   method, so writes go through one place and stay debuggable.\n199: - Do not use `$derived` to avoid thinking about when a value changes.\n200: \n201: ## TypeScript\n202: \n203: The project is TypeScript strict (`tsconfig.json` sets `\"strict\": true`).\n204: \n205: - Type everything real. Prefer explicit types on public method parameters and\n206:   return values in the state and service layers.\n207: - Use `import type { ... }` for types — it keeps the import out of the runtime\n208:   graph and is enforced by tooling. Types-only files under `src/lib/types/` are\n209:   erased at compile time; the only two with runtime values are\n210:   `src/lib/types/check_in.ts` and `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts`.\n211: - Avoid `any`. If an API payload genuinely has no shape yet, cast through the\n212:   domain type at the boundary (`res.data as Todo[]`) rather than leaking `any`\n213:   through the codebase.\n214: - Model unions as string-literal unions (`'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' |\n215:   'card'`) instead of loose `string`, and keep them next to the state they\n216:   describe.\n217: - Run `npm run check` (svelte-check) before considering a change done.\n218: \n219: ## Formatting and tooling\n220: \n221: Formatting is not a matter of taste here — it is fixed by `.prettierrc` and\n222: enforced by `npm run lint`.\n223: \n224: - **Indentation:** tabs (`useTabs: true`), 4-wide.\n225: - **Quotes:** single quotes.\n226: - **Line width:** 100 characters.\n227: - **Trailing commas:** none.\n228: - **Plugins:** `prettier-plugin-svelte` (Svelte markup) and\n229:   `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` (stable ordering of Tailwind classes).\n230: - `npm run format` rewrites files; do not hand-fight the formatter. Never\n231:   hand-edit generated output (`build/`, `.svelte-kit/`).\n232: - ESLint (`eslint.config.js`) layers `typescript-eslint` and\n233:   `eslint-plugin-svelte` on top of Prettier. `npm run lint` runs both\n234:   `prettier --check .` and `eslint .`.\n235: - `npm run check` is the type gate; treat it as part of \"done\", not optional.\n236: \n237: ## Testing\n238: \n239: Keep this short and defer to the full plan in [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md).\n240: The one rule to remember:\n241: \n242: > Test logic and contracts, not markup, and not third-party internals.\n243: \n244: - Pure helpers, services and config get unit tests in node (`npm test`).\n245: - State stores are tested through their public methods with `ApiService`,\n246:   `Auth` and `LocalStorageService` mocked or injected — never by reaching into\n247:   private fields.\n248: - Presentational components are tested only when they carry logic (keyboard\n249:   handling, selection, props-driven data). Render-only icons, logos and\n250:   dividers are not worth a test.\n251: - Do not assert on ECharts/TipTap/DnD internals; assert our props and logic.\n252: - Follow the existing store-mock recipe and context harness described in\n253:   `docs/TESTING.md` §4.\n254: \n255: ## Related docs\n256: \n257: - [`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — what the app is and how it is structured.\n258: - [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the state-service layer.\n259: - [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — the component and route layer.\n260: - [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — services, helpers, config, types, i18n.\n261: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) — the full test coverage plan.\n\n(End of file - total 261 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# solyto coding policies\n\nGeneral, cross-cutting rules for writing code in the solyto frontend. Every\nother policy document assumes these rules; this file is the entry point to the\nset.\n\n## Purpose and how to use this set\n\nThe solyto frontend is one SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 app maintained by a small\nnumber of people, most of it written by hand in a consistent style. These\ndocuments capture that style so new code — whether written by a person or by an\nAI assistant — reads like the rest of the codebase instead of like a generic\nSvelte tutorial.\n\nThere are four policy documents, each owning one layer:\n\n| Document                                       | Owns                                                                        |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`** (this file)       | General in-file rules that apply everywhere                                 |\n| [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md)  | The state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`                                 |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md","text":"# solyto coding policies\n\nGeneral, cross-cutting rules for writing code in the solyto frontend. Every\nother policy document assumes these rules; this file is the entry point to the\nset.\n\n## Purpose and how to use this set\n\nThe solyto frontend is one SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 app maintained by a small\nnumber of people, most of it written by hand in a consistent style. These\ndocuments capture that style so new code — whether written by a person or by an\nAI assistant — reads like the rest of the codebase instead of like a generic\nSvelte tutorial.\n\nThere are four policy documents, each owning one layer:\n\n| Document                                       | Owns                                                                        |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`** (this file)       | General in-file rules that apply everywhere                                 |\n| [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md)  | The state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`                                 |\n| [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md)          | The UI layer: `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**` `.svelte` files    |\n| [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)          | `services/`, `helpers/`, `config/`, `types/`, `i18n/` and the data flow      |\n\n`docs/TESTING.md` is the companion testing policy and is referenced from the\n\"Testing\" section below rather than duplicated here. `docs/AGENTS.md` remains\nthe top-level architecture summary.\n\n**How to use it:** read this file first, then jump to the document for the\nlayer you are touching. Every rule is grounded in a real file in this repo —\nwhen in doubt, open the cited file and copy its shape. If a rule and the\nexisting code disagree, the rule is wrong; fix the rule.\n\n## Readability first\n\nThe top rule, and the reason the others exist: code is read far more often than\nit is written. Optimise for the next person reading it, not for the fewest\nlines or the cleverest expression.\n\n- Prefer an obvious implementation over a compact one. A five-line function\n  with clear names beats a one-line chain of `reduce`/ternaries.\n- Match the surrounding file. The codebase has an established shape for stores,\n  components, services and config — imitate the nearest example instead of\n  inventing a new pattern.\n- A reader should be able to follow a function top to bottom without jumping\n  around to understand control flow.\n\nThis trade-off is deliberate: the repo accepts some repetition (see\n[`STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md#the-crud-method-pattern)) in exchange\nfor predictable, greppable, obvious code.\n\n## DRY — but not prematurely\n\nDuplication is a smell, but a premature abstraction is worse: it hides two\nslightly-different things behind one helper and makes both harder to change.\n`docs/AGENTS.md` states the hard rule directly:\n\n> Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase.\n\n- Extract a helper when the same logic appears **three or more times** and the\n  cases genuinely do the same thing. Two similar-looking blocks are allowed to\n  stay separate.\n- Do not introduce base classes, generics, factories, or \"flexible\" options\n  objects the codebase does not already use.\n- When logic is shared, put it in a named, single-purpose module\n  (`src/lib/helpers/*Helper.ts` for pure utilities, `src/lib/services/*Service.ts`\n  for domain logic) — not in a god-object or inline in a component.\n- Repetition that mirrors an external contract (e.g. the CRUD methods in the\n  state layer) is intentional and should be left alone.\n\nIf you cannot point at an existing pattern for the abstraction you are about to\nadd, do not add it.\n\n## Small, single-purpose functions\n\nA function should do one thing and its name should say what that is.\n\n- Keep functions short enough to read without scrolling. If a function has\n  several distinct phases, each phase is usually its own function.\n- No side effects hidden behind an innocuous name. A function called\n  `getScoredTodos` returns scored todos; it does not also mutate storage.\n- Split a long method by extracting named steps. In `Todos.svelte.ts`, `load()`\n  reads as a sequence of named operations — `loadCategories()`,\n  `loadWorkspaces()`, `loadHideIt()`, `groupByStatus()` — rather than one long\n  body.\n- Pure logic belongs in `services/`/`helpers/`, not mixed into UI or state\n  glue. `Todos` delegates filtering, sorting and grouping to\n  `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService` and `TodoGroupingService`.\n\n## Early returns — no nested short-ifs\n\nGuard clauses are the default. Handle the exceptional or terminal cases first\nand return, so the rest of the function stays at one level of nesting.\n\n**Do not** wrap a whole function body in an `if` when the inverted condition\nlets you return early, and **do not** write `else` after a branch that already\nreturns.\n\n```ts\n// preferred — flat, each guard on its own line\nfunction label(todo: Todo): string {\n\tif (todo.is_completed) return 'done';\n\tif (todo.status === 'backlog') return 'backlog';\n\treturn 'open';\n}\n\n// avoid — inverted condition nested over the whole body\nfunction label(todo: Todo): string {\n\tif (!todo.is_completed) {\n\t\tif (todo.status !== 'backlog') {\n\t\t\treturn 'open';\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn 'backlog';\n\t}\n\treturn 'done';\n}\n```\n\nReal examples: `Todos.loadHideIt()`, `QuickAdd.detect()`/`confirm()`, and\n`Viewpoint`'s `if (browser)` guard all bail out early instead of nesting the\nmain path. One-line guards with a bare `return` (`if (!res) return;`) are\npreferred over a nested `else`.\n\nThis is a readability rule, not an anti-`if` rule: a single, shallow `if/else`\nwith balanced branches is fine. The thing to avoid is a ladder of nested\n`if/else` and short ternaries that force the reader to hold several conditions\nin their head at once.\n\n## Naming\n\nNames carry the structure of the code; be consistent with the existing ones.\n\n- **Booleans** read as assertions: `loaded`, `isDesktop`, `isMobile`,\n  `hideItActive`, `sortByScore`, `todosScored`, `needsConfirmation`. Prefix\n  with `is`/`has`/`should` when the bare noun is ambiguous.\n- **Handlers** in components: `onclick`-style attributes reference a function\n  whose name describes the action — `toggleChangeTitle`, `setExplanationBoxPosition`,\n  or the conventional `handleEnter`/`handleEscape`. Form callbacks use the\n  short `onsubmit`/`onblur`/`oninput` when they mirror the DOM event.\n- **State classes** are nouns (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`); their context\n  accessors are `setX()` / `getX()` (see\n  [`STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md#the-context-singleton-pattern)).\n- **Methods** are verbs: `load`, `useFilters`, `groupByStatus`, `toggleHideIt`.\n  Getters that expose derived read-only values are named after the value\n  (`isUrl`, `isDesktop`).\n- **Constants** are `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` and scoped to the class that owns them:\n  `Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`, `TODOS_KEY`. Storage keys always start with `LS_`.\n- Files map to the class: `Todos.svelte.ts`, `ApiService.ts`, `TodoFilterService.ts`.\n\n## Comments explain why, not what\n\nThe code says what it does; a comment earns its place by explaining **why** —\nthe non-obvious constraint, the reason for the awkward-looking order, the bug\nbeing avoided.\n\n`Todos.svelte.ts` is the reference:\n\n```ts\n// Restore synchronously so every filter pass (including the ones run by\n// load() before the workspaces request resolves) already sees the\n// persisted value instead of the default false.\nthis.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n```\n\n```ts\n// Always re-apply hide-it once the parallel loads settled: a failed\n// or rejected workspaces/categories request must not skip this.\n```\n\n`Viewpoint.svelte.ts` shows the complementary case: the non-obvious constraint\nis that browser APIs only exist in the browser, so the constructor guards the\nwhole initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n\n- Do **not** narrate the obvious (`// increment i`).\n- Do **not** leave commented-out code; git remembers it.\n- Prefer a short block comment above a tricky block over line-by-line comments\n  inside it.\n\n## `$derived` discipline\n\nUse `$derived` only for a genuine derivation of other reactive state that is\nread while rendering. It is not a place to stash transformations that belong in\na function, a service, or a `$state` field set by a method.\n\nThe legitimate use is `src/routes/+layout.svelte`:\n\n```ts\nconst canAccessRoute = $derived(auth.loggedIn || isAuthRoute() || isSetupRoute());\n```\n\n`canAccessRoute` is a pure function of existing state and is consumed in the\ntemplate, so it stays correct automatically.\n\n- Deriving from one or two reactive reads with no side effects: fine.\n- Hiding a chain of `.filter().map().sort()` behind `$derived`: move it into a\n  method or service (`Todos.useFilters` is a method, not a `$derived`).\n- A value that is recomputed by an explicit method (e.g. `filteredTodos` after\n  a filter change or a reload): keep it as `$state` and assign it in the\n  method, so writes go through one place and stay debuggable.\n- Do not use `$derived` to avoid thinking about when a value changes.\n\n## TypeScript\n\nThe project is TypeScript strict (`tsconfig.json` sets `\"strict\": true`).\n\n- Type everything real. Prefer explicit types on public method parameters and\n  return values in the state and service layers.\n- Use `import type { ... }` for types — it keeps the import out of the runtime\n  graph and is enforced by tooling. Types-only files under `src/lib/types/` are\n  erased at compile time; the only two with runtime values are\n  `src/lib/types/check_in.ts` and `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts`.\n- Avoid `any`. If an API payload genuinely has no shape yet, cast through the\n  domain type at the boundary (`res.data as Todo[]`) rather than leaking `any`\n  through the codebase.\n- Model unions as string-literal unions (`'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' |\n  'card'`) instead of loose `string`, and keep them next to the state they\n  describe.\n- Run `npm run check` (svelte-check) before considering a change done.\n\n## Formatting and tooling\n\nFormatting is not a matter of taste here — it is fixed by `.prettierrc` and\nenforced by `npm run lint`.\n\n- **Indentation:** tabs (`useTabs: true`), 4-wide.\n- **Quotes:** single quotes.\n- **Line width:** 100 characters.\n- **Trailing commas:** none.\n- **Plugins:** `prettier-plugin-svelte` (Svelte markup) and\n  `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` (stable ordering of Tailwind classes).\n- `npm run format` rewrites files; do not hand-fight the formatter. Never\n  hand-edit generated output (`build/`, `.svelte-kit/`).\n- ESLint (`eslint.config.js`) layers `typescript-eslint` and\n  `eslint-plugin-svelte` on top of Prettier. `npm run lint` runs both\n  `prettier --check .` and `eslint .`.\n- `npm run check` is the type gate; treat it as part of \"done\", not optional.\n\n## Testing\n\nKeep this short and defer to the full plan in [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md).\nThe one rule to remember:\n\n> Test logic and contracts, not markup, and not third-party internals.\n\n- Pure helpers, services and config get unit tests in node (`npm test`).\n- State stores are tested through their public methods with `ApiService`,\n  `Auth` and `LocalStorageService` mocked or injected — never by reaching into\n  private fields.\n- Presentational components are tested only when they carry logic (keyboard\n  handling, selection, props-driven data). Render-only icons, logos and\n  dividers are not worth a test.\n- Do not assert on ECharts/TipTap/DnD internals; assert our props and logic.\n- Follow the existing store-mock recipe and context harness described in\n  `docs/TESTING.md` §4.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — what the app is and how it is structured.\n- [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the state-service layer.\n- [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — the component and route layer.\n- [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — services, helpers, config, types, i18n.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) — the full test coverage plan.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":261,"totalLines":261,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md","time":{"start":1791640282994,"end":1791640283051}},"id":"prt_126152760001h9NPopyYQtjVQR","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12614f76c001J0FlDtISSnXX4d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640283074,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_YkVIvZf404aW5oGBJnvX5107","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # State services\n2: \n3: Policy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\n4: Svelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\n5: communication with the API. Read\n6: [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\n7: document applies those general rules to this layer.\n8: \n9: ## One class per domain, one file per domain\n10: \n11: - One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n12:   in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n13: - `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n14:   compile.\n15: - The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n16:   the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n17:   `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n18: - No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n19:   components and `i18n/`).\n20: \n21: ## The context-singleton pattern\n22: \n23: Every store is a Svelte context singleton. The file exports a private `Symbol`\n24: key plus a `setX()` / `getX()` pair — the only sanctioned shape:\n25: \n26: ```ts\n27: const CLIPBOARD_KEY = Symbol('SOLYTO_CLIPBOARD');\n28: \n29: export function setClipboard(): Clipboard {\n30: \treturn setContext(CLIPBOARD_KEY, new Clipboard());\n31: }\n32: \n33: export function getClipboard(): Clipboard {\n34: \treturn getContext<Clipboard>(CLIPBOARD_KEY);\n35: }\n36: ```\n37: \n38: - `setX()` is called **once**, during component initialisation, and returns the\n39:   new instance.\n40: - `getX()` is called by any component below that needs the store. It never\n41:   constructs — a missing provider is a programming error, not a case to handle.\n42: - App-wide stores (`Auth`, `Translation`, `Viewpoint`, `KeyManager`,\n43:   `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `Navigation`, `CookieConsent`,\n44:   `PwaInstall`, `WelcomeTour`, `QuickAdd`) are created in\n45:   `src/routes/+layout.svelte`.\n46: - Feature stores are created in the feature's route layout — e.g.\n47:   `setTodos()`/`setTags()` in `src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n48:   `setClipboard()` in `src/routes/clipboard/+layout.svelte`,\n49:   `setBookLibrary()` in `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`. This keeps\n50:   a feature's store alive only while its routes are mounted.\n51: \n52: ## Reactive state as `$state` class fields\n53: \n54: - Declare each piece of reactive state as a public `$state` field with an\n55:   explicit type:\n56: \n57:   ```ts\n58:   loaded = $state<boolean>(false);\n59:   todos = $state<Todo[]>([]);\n60:   activeWorkspace = $state<TodoWorkspace | null>(null);\n61:   view = $state<'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' | 'card'>('list');\n62:   ```\n63: \n64: - Initialise to the empty/neutral value so the store is valid before `load()`\n65:   runs.\n66: - Mutate the field directly (`this.todos = res.data as Todo[]`); do not wrap it\n67:   in setters, stores or extra indirection. Svelte's runes propagate the change.\n68: - Internal-only state may be `private` (see `Viewpoint._state`), but reach for\n69:   that only when you also want to expose a stable read-only surface (next\n70:   section).\n71: \n72: ## Member ordering\n73: \n74: Keep the same order in every store, top to bottom. `Todos` is the reference:\n75: \n76: 1. `static readonly` constants (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`).\n77: 2. `$state` fields.\n78: 3. Collaborators/dependencies declared as typed fields (`auth`, `apiService`,\n79:    `localStorage`, injected services) and any private helpers.\n80: 4. The constructor.\n81: 5. Public methods.\n82: 6. `private` methods last.\n83: \n84: The `Symbol` key and `setX()`/`getX()` functions live **below** the class, at\n85: the bottom of the file.\n86: \n87: ## Constructor dependency injection (preferred)\n88: \n89: The preferred shape injects collaborators through constructor parameters whose\n90: defaults preserve zero-argument construction. `Todos` and `Finances` are the\n91: reference:\n92: \n93: ```ts\n94: export class Todos {\n95: \tauth: Auth;\n96: \tapiService: ApiService;\n97: \tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n98: \n99: \tconstructor(\n100: \t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n101: \t\tapiService: ApiService = auth.apiService,\n102: \t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n103: \t) {\n104: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n105: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n106: \t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n107: \t}\n108: }\n109: ```\n110: \n111: ```ts\n112: export class Finances {\n113: \tauth: Auth;\n114: \tapiService: ApiService;\n115: \n116: \tconstructor(auth: Auth = getAuth(), apiService: ApiService = auth.apiService) {\n117: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n118: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n119: \t\t// …\n120: \t}\n121: }\n122: ```\n123: \n124: Why it matters:\n125: \n126: - `new Todos()` still works everywhere (the defaults do the context lookup), so\n127:   the change is invisible to callers.\n128: - Tests can pass mocks (`new Todos(mockAuth, mockApi, mockStorage)`) without\n129:   module-level `vi.mock` gymnastics — this is the refactor `docs/TESTING.md` §4\n130:   describes, and it is what made the store tests possible.\n131: - The defaults are the single place that knows how to build the real\n132:   collaborators.\n133: \n134: The **older style** some stores still use declares dependencies as\n135: field initialisers, which run before the constructor body:\n136: \n137: ```ts\n138: // older — not the target style\n139: export class Clipboard {\n140: \tauth = getAuth();\n141: \tapiService: ApiService;\n142: \n143: \tconstructor() {\n144: \t\tthis.apiService = this.auth.apiService;\n145: \t}\n146: }\n147: ```\n148: \n149: This works, but it cannot be overridden by a constructor argument and forces\n150: tests to mock the `Auth` module. When you touch a store, prefer migrating it to\n151: the injectable shape; do not do it as a bulk rewrite.\n152: \n153: The shared API client is `auth.apiService` — `Auth` owns one `ApiService`\n154: instance and keeps its token current (`updateAuthToken`). Stores default to it;\n155: do not construct a second `ApiService` with a hand-copied token.\n156: \n157: ## The `load()` + `loaded` convention\n158: \n159: Every domain store exposes an async `load(): Promise<void>` that fetches its\n160: data and populates the `$state` fields, and a boolean `loaded` field set to\n161: `true` on the first successful load. Components/layouts call `load()` in\n162: `onMount` and use `loaded` to avoid rendering empty state.\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165: async load(): Promise<void> {\n166: \tconst res = await this.apiService.list(apiRoutes.todos.list);\n167: \n168: \tif (res) {\n169: \t\tthis.loaded = true;\n170: \t\tthis.todos = res.data as Todo[];\n171: \t\tthis.filteredTodos = this.todos;\n172: \t\t// …\n173: \t}\n174: \n175: \t// … derived steps, then parallel sub-loads\n176: }\n177: ```\n178: \n179: - One `if (res)` block does the assignment; failure simply leaves the previous\n180:   state in place (see error semantics in [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)).\n181: - Sub-loads use their own `loadX()` methods and may run in parallel via\n182:   `Promise.all`.\n183: - `load()` re-derives everything that depends on the freshly-loaded data, so a\n184:   store is never left half-updated.\n185: \n186: ## The CRUD method pattern\n187: \n188: Every create/update/delete method follows the same shape: call `ApiService`\n189: with a route from `apiRoutes`, reload on success, return a boolean.\n190: \n191: ```ts\n192: async delete(todo: Todo): Promise<boolean> {\n193: \tconst ok = await this.apiService.delete(apiRoutes.todos.delete, todo.id);\n194: \tif (ok) await this.load();\n195: \treturn ok;\n196: }\n197: ```\n198: \n199: ```ts\n200: async addTag(todo: Todo, tagId: number): Promise<boolean> {\n201: \tconst tagIds = todo.tags.map((t) => t.id);\n202: \tconst request: UpdateTodoRequest = { tags: tagIds.concat([tagId]) };\n203: \tconst res = await this.apiService.update(apiRoutes.todos.update, todo.id, request);\n204: \tif (res) await this.load();\n205: \treturn res;\n206: }\n207: ```\n208: \n209: - Build a typed request object first (`const request: UpdateTodoRequest = {…}`),\n210:   then pass it to `ApiService`.\n211: - Return `true`/`false` (or the raw `res`/`ok`) so the calling component can\n212:   react. Mutating methods that need a created entity return it (or `null`).\n213: - **This repetitiveness is intentional.** It is not something to \"DRY up\" behind\n214:   a generic `crud(endpoint, method, id)` helper — each method is a greppable,\n215:   independently-readable contract with its own request type, and the\n216:   boilerplate CRUD wrappers are explicitly excluded from test coverage\n217:   (`docs/TESTING.md` §8). Copy the nearest method; do not abstract it.\n218: \n219: ## Delegate pure logic to `services/`\n220: \n221: A store is glue: it holds state and sequences API/pure calls. Filtering,\n222: sorting, grouping and scoring are pure and live in `src/lib/services/`:\n223: \n224: - `Todos` delegates to `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`,\n225:   `TodoGroupingService` and `TodoRelevanceService` — e.g.\n226:   `this.filteredTodos = this.filterService.filter(filter, this.filteredTodos)`.\n227: - The service instances are held as fields (`filterService = new TodoFilterService()`)\n228:   and called from the store's methods.\n229: - Library stores hold a `LibraryFilterService`; `Finances` uses\n230:   `WealthStatisticsService`.\n231: \n232: If you are about to write a non-trivial `filter`/`map`/`reduce` chain inside a\n233: store method, stop: it probably belongs in a `*Service.ts` where it can be unit\n234: tested without any Svelte context. See [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md).\n235: \n236: ## Persistence\n237: \n238: The only client-side persistence is `LocalStorageService`, injected into the\n239: store. Storage keys are class constants named `LS_*`:\n240: \n241: ```ts\n242: export class Todos {\n243: \tstatic readonly LS_HIDE_IT_KEY: string = 'todos_hideit';\n244: \t// …\n245: }\n246: ```\n247: \n248: ```ts\n249: this.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n250: ```\n251: \n252: - Always go through `LocalStorageService` — it guards `browser` internally, so\n253:   callers do not have to.\n254: - Keys are `snake_case` strings (`'todos_hideit'`, `'custom_api_url'`).\n255: - Restore persisted state in the constructor, and re-read it in `load()` when a\n256:   value could have changed while the initial load was in flight (see\n257:   `Todos.loadHideIt()`). Auth tokens are the one exception handled by `Auth`\n258:   itself.\n259: \n260: ## Browser and route imports — guard them\n261: \n262: - `browser` from `$app/environment` guards anything that touches `window`,\n263:   `document` or `localStorage`. `LocalStorageService` does this internally; a\n264:   store that touches the DOM directly must do the same. `Viewpoint` guards its\n265:   entire initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n266: - `page` from `$app/state` is read for route information (e.g.\n267:   `page.url.searchParams` in `Todos.checkUrlForFilter()`). Read it; do not\n268:   subscribe to navigation inside the store.\n269: - If a store registers listeners or timers, clean them up in an explicit\n270:   `destroy()` method and call it from the owner component's `onDestroy`.\n271:   `Viewpoint` collects each cleanup closure in an array and runs them all in\n272:   `destroy()`.\n273: \n274: ## Stores may depend on other stores\n275: \n276: A store may read another store or the translation table when its logic needs\n277: them:\n278: \n279: - `QuickAdd` reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()` for its error\n280:   messages, and `getAuth()` for the API client.\n281: - `Translation` reads `getAuth()` to pick the user's language.\n282: \n283: Resolve these dependencies once in the constructor (or as defaults), not on\n284: every method call, and never create a cycle. Keep the dependency in the\n285: constructor's parameter list where practical so tests can inject it\n286: (`docs/TESTING.md` §4 gives `QuickAdd` as the `ts`/`notifications` example).\n287: \n288: ## Read-only view state via getters\n289: \n290: When a store owns computed state that consumers must not write, expose it\n291: through getters. `Viewpoint` keeps its data in a `private _state` and returns\n292: `get state()`, `get width()`, `get isDesktop()`, etc.:\n293: \n294: ```ts\n295: private _state = $state<ViewPointState>({ width: 0, height: 0, isDesktop: false, isMobile: true, isTablet: false });\n296: \n297: get isDesktop() {\n298: \treturn this._state.isDesktop;\n299: }\n300: ```\n301: \n302: Use this for genuinely read-only derivations (screen class, computed URL\n303: flags). For normal domain data, keep the public `$state` field — getters for\n304: everything add noise.\n305: \n306: ## What not to do\n307: \n308: - **No markup, DOM, or UI strings** in a store. That is the component layer's\n309:   job.\n310: - **No hardcoded API URLs.** Every endpoint comes from\n311:   `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`; never build a URL string by hand.\n312: - **No inline `fetch`.** `ApiService` is the single network seam; a store calls\n313:   it and nothing else. (The only exceptions are the few legacy direct-`fetch`\n314:   methods in `Calendars` — do not copy them.)\n315: - **No giant methods.** Split by named steps (`loadCategories`, `useFilters`).\n316: - **No new global singletons.** Use the context pattern; do not export a\n317:   module-level `new Todos()`.\n318: - **No `$derived` dumping ground.** Derived values that belong in a method or a\n319:   service stay there; see [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline).\n320: - Do not add an abstraction a store does not already use.\n321: \n322: ## Related docs\n323: \n324: - [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n325: - [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — `ApiService`, `apiRoutes`, services,\n326:   helpers, types, i18n.\n327: - [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components read these stores.\n328: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §3–4 — the store test recipe and the\n329:   constructor-injection refactor.\n\n(End of file - total 329 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ncommunication with the API. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n\n## One class per domain, one file per domain\n\n- One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n  in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n- `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n  compile.\n- The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n  the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n  `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n- No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n  components and `i18n/`).\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md","text":"# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ncommunication with the API. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n\n## One class per domain, one file per domain\n\n- One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n  in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n- `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n  compile.\n- The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n  the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n  `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n- No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n  components and `i18n/`).\n\n## The context-singleton pattern\n\nEvery store is a Svelte context singleton. The file exports a private `Symbol`\nkey plus a `setX()` / `getX()` pair — the only sanctioned shape:\n\n```ts\nconst CLIPBOARD_KEY = Symbol('SOLYTO_CLIPBOARD');\n\nexport function setClipboard(): Clipboard {\n\treturn setContext(CLIPBOARD_KEY, new Clipboard());\n}\n\nexport function getClipboard(): Clipboard {\n\treturn getContext<Clipboard>(CLIPBOARD_KEY);\n}\n```\n\n- `setX()` is called **once**, during component initialisation, and returns the\n  new instance.\n- `getX()` is called by any component below that needs the store. It never\n  constructs — a missing provider is a programming error, not a case to handle.\n- App-wide stores (`Auth`, `Translation`, `Viewpoint`, `KeyManager`,\n  `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `Navigation`, `CookieConsent`,\n  `PwaInstall`, `WelcomeTour`, `QuickAdd`) are created in\n  `src/routes/+layout.svelte`.\n- Feature stores are created in the feature's route layout — e.g.\n  `setTodos()`/`setTags()` in `src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n  `setClipboard()` in `src/routes/clipboard/+layout.svelte`,\n  `setBookLibrary()` in `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`. This keeps\n  a feature's store alive only while its routes are mounted.\n\n## Reactive state as `$state` class fields\n\n- Declare each piece of reactive state as a public `$state` field with an\n  explicit type:\n\n  ```ts\n  loaded = $state<boolean>(false);\n  todos = $state<Todo[]>([]);\n  activeWorkspace = $state<TodoWorkspace | null>(null);\n  view = $state<'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' | 'card'>('list');\n  ```\n\n- Initialise to the empty/neutral value so the store is valid before `load()`\n  runs.\n- Mutate the field directly (`this.todos = res.data as Todo[]`); do not wrap it\n  in setters, stores or extra indirection. Svelte's runes propagate the change.\n- Internal-only state may be `private` (see `Viewpoint._state`), but reach for\n  that only when you also want to expose a stable read-only surface (next\n  section).\n\n## Member ordering\n\nKeep the same order in every store, top to bottom. `Todos` is the reference:\n\n1. `static readonly` constants (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`).\n2. `$state` fields.\n3. Collaborators/dependencies declared as typed fields (`auth`, `apiService`,\n   `localStorage`, injected services) and any private helpers.\n4. The constructor.\n5. Public methods.\n6. `private` methods last.\n\nThe `Symbol` key and `setX()`/`getX()` functions live **below** the class, at\nthe bottom of the file.\n\n## Constructor dependency injection (preferred)\n\nThe preferred shape injects collaborators through constructor parameters whose\ndefaults preserve zero-argument construction. `Todos` and `Finances` are the\nreference:\n\n```ts\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n\n\tconstructor(\n\t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n\t\tapiService: ApiService = auth.apiService,\n\t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n\t) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nexport class Finances {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\n\tconstructor(auth: Auth = getAuth(), apiService: ApiService = auth.apiService) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nWhy it matters:\n\n- `new Todos()` still works everywhere (the defaults do the context lookup), so\n  the change is invisible to callers.\n- Tests can pass mocks (`new Todos(mockAuth, mockApi, mockStorage)`) without\n  module-level `vi.mock` gymnastics — this is the refactor `docs/TESTING.md` §4\n  describes, and it is what made the store tests possible.\n- The defaults are the single place that knows how to build the real\n  collaborators.\n\nThe **older style** some stores still use declares dependencies as\nfield initialisers, which run before the constructor body:\n\n```ts\n// older — not the target style\nexport class Clipboard {\n\tauth = getAuth();\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tthis.apiService = this.auth.apiService;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis works, but it cannot be overridden by a constructor argument and forces\ntests to mock the `Auth` module. When you touch a store, prefer migrating it to\nthe injectable shape; do not do it as a bulk rewrite.\n\nThe shared API client is `auth.apiService` — `Auth` owns one `ApiService`\ninstance and keeps its token current (`updateAuthToken`). Stores default to it;\ndo not construct a second `ApiService` with a hand-copied token.\n\n## The `load()` + `loaded` convention\n\nEvery domain store exposes an async `load(): Promise<void>` that fetches its\ndata and populates the `$state` fields, and a boolean `loaded` field set to\n`true` on the first successful load. Components/layouts call `load()` in\n`onMount` and use `loaded` to avoid rendering empty state.\n\n```ts\nasync load(): Promise<void> {\n\tconst res = await this.apiService.list(apiRoutes.todos.list);\n\n\tif (res) {\n\t\tthis.loaded = true;\n\t\tthis.todos = res.data as Todo[];\n\t\tthis.filteredTodos = this.todos;\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n\n\t// … derived steps, then parallel sub-loads\n}\n```\n\n- One `if (res)` block does the assignment; failure simply leaves the previous\n  state in place (see error semantics in [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)).\n- Sub-loads use their own `loadX()` methods and may run in parallel via\n  `Promise.all`.\n- `load()` re-derives everything that depends on the freshly-loaded data, so a\n  store is never left half-updated.\n\n## The CRUD method pattern\n\nEvery create/update/delete method follows the same shape: call `ApiService`\nwith a route from `apiRoutes`, reload on success, return a boolean.\n\n```ts\nasync delete(todo: Todo): Promise<boolean> {\n\tconst ok = await this.apiService.delete(apiRoutes.todos.delete, todo.id);\n\tif (ok) await this.load();\n\treturn ok;\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nasync addTag(todo: Todo, tagId: number): Promise<boolean> {\n\tconst tagIds = todo.tags.map((t) => t.id);\n\tconst request: UpdateTodoRequest = { tags: tagIds.concat([tagId]) };\n\tconst res = await this.apiService.update(apiRoutes.todos.update, todo.id, request);\n\tif (res) await this.load();\n\treturn res;\n}\n```\n\n- Build a typed request object first (`const request: UpdateTodoRequest = {…}`),\n  then pass it to `ApiService`.\n- Return `true`/`false` (or the raw `res`/`ok`) so the calling component can\n  react. Mutating methods that need a created entity return it (or `null`).\n- **This repetitiveness is intentional.** It is not something to \"DRY up\" behind\n  a generic `crud(endpoint, method, id)` helper — each method is a greppable,\n  independently-readable contract with its own request type, and the\n  boilerplate CRUD wrappers are explicitly excluded from test coverage\n  (`docs/TESTING.md` §8). Copy the nearest method; do not abstract it.\n\n## Delegate pure logic to `services/`\n\nA store is glue: it holds state and sequences API/pure calls. Filtering,\nsorting, grouping and scoring are pure and live in `src/lib/services/`:\n\n- `Todos` delegates to `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`,\n  `TodoGroupingService` and `TodoRelevanceService` — e.g.\n  `this.filteredTodos = this.filterService.filter(filter, this.filteredTodos)`.\n- The service instances are held as fields (`filterService = new TodoFilterService()`)\n  and called from the store's methods.\n- Library stores hold a `LibraryFilterService`; `Finances` uses\n  `WealthStatisticsService`.\n\nIf you are about to write a non-trivial `filter`/`map`/`reduce` chain inside a\nstore method, stop: it probably belongs in a `*Service.ts` where it can be unit\ntested without any Svelte context. See [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md).\n\n## Persistence\n\nThe only client-side persistence is `LocalStorageService`, injected into the\nstore. Storage keys are class constants named `LS_*`:\n\n```ts\nexport class Todos {\n\tstatic readonly LS_HIDE_IT_KEY: string = 'todos_hideit';\n\t// …\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nthis.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n```\n\n- Always go through `LocalStorageService` — it guards `browser` internally, so\n  callers do not have to.\n- Keys are `snake_case` strings (`'todos_hideit'`, `'custom_api_url'`).\n- Restore persisted state in the constructor, and re-read it in `load()` when a\n  value could have changed while the initial load was in flight (see\n  `Todos.loadHideIt()`). Auth tokens are the one exception handled by `Auth`\n  itself.\n\n## Browser and route imports — guard them\n\n- `browser` from `$app/environment` guards anything that touches `window`,\n  `document` or `localStorage`. `LocalStorageService` does this internally; a\n  store that touches the DOM directly must do the same. `Viewpoint` guards its\n  entire initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n- `page` from `$app/state` is read for route information (e.g.\n  `page.url.searchParams` in `Todos.checkUrlForFilter()`). Read it; do not\n  subscribe to navigation inside the store.\n- If a store registers listeners or timers, clean them up in an explicit\n  `destroy()` method and call it from the owner component's `onDestroy`.\n  `Viewpoint` collects each cleanup closure in an array and runs them all in\n  `destroy()`.\n\n## Stores may depend on other stores\n\nA store may read another store or the translation table when its logic needs\nthem:\n\n- `QuickAdd` reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()` for its error\n  messages, and `getAuth()` for the API client.\n- `Translation` reads `getAuth()` to pick the user's language.\n\nResolve these dependencies once in the constructor (or as defaults), not on\nevery method call, and never create a cycle. Keep the dependency in the\nconstructor's parameter list where practical so tests can inject it\n(`docs/TESTING.md` §4 gives `QuickAdd` as the `ts`/`notifications` example).\n\n## Read-only view state via getters\n\nWhen a store owns computed state that consumers must not write, expose it\nthrough getters. `Viewpoint` keeps its data in a `private _state` and returns\n`get state()`, `get width()`, `get isDesktop()`, etc.:\n\n```ts\nprivate _state = $state<ViewPointState>({ width: 0, height: 0, isDesktop: false, isMobile: true, isTablet: false });\n\nget isDesktop() {\n\treturn this._state.isDesktop;\n}\n```\n\nUse this for genuinely read-only derivations (screen class, computed URL\nflags). For normal domain data, keep the public `$state` field — getters for\neverything add noise.\n\n## What not to do\n\n- **No markup, DOM, or UI strings** in a store. That is the component layer's\n  job.\n- **No hardcoded API URLs.** Every endpoint comes from\n  `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`; never build a URL string by hand.\n- **No inline `fetch`.** `ApiService` is the single network seam; a store calls\n  it and nothing else. (The only exceptions are the few legacy direct-`fetch`\n  methods in `Calendars` — do not copy them.)\n- **No giant methods.** Split by named steps (`loadCategories`, `useFilters`).\n- **No new global singletons.** Use the context pattern; do not export a\n  module-level `new Todos()`.\n- **No `$derived` dumping ground.** Derived values that belong in a method or a\n  service stay there; see [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline).\n- Do not add an abstraction a store does not already use.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n- [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — `ApiService`, `apiRoutes`, services,\n  helpers, types, i18n.\n- [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components read these stores.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §3–4 — the store test recipe and the\n  constructor-injection refactor.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":329,"totalLines":329,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/STATE_SERVICES.md","time":{"start":1791640283016,"end":1791640283058}},"id":"prt_126152775001MJdGnx2ttEUuqT","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12614f76c001J0FlDtISSnXX4d"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791640283155,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"id":"prt_126152801001j7ZZ6gX336WNbh","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"","messageID":"msg_12614f76c001J0FlDtISSnXX4d","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":27643,"input":1201,"output":84,"reasoning":1910,"cache":{"write":0,"read":24448}},"cost":0.001449894}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791640284476,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"id":"prt_126152d390011gHTiHwbaVL0iq","messageID":"msg_12615280e0015SRXWCaLo85o3j","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640285228,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_hvsSy8BMJUIAXTmaTjvv9855","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Components\n2: \n3: Policy for the UI layer: every `.svelte` component under\n4: `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**`. Read\n5: [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document applies the\n6: general rules to markup and components.\n7: \n8: ## Components are lean\n9: \n10: A component's job is to render state and forward user intent. All logic lives\n11: below it — in the state store or a pure service.\n12: \n13: - Read the stores a component needs **once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">`**,\n14:   never inside the markup or per-method:\n15: \n16:   ```ts\n17:   const todos = getTodos();\n18:   const loadingIndicator = getLoadingIndicator();\n19:   const keyManager = getKeyManager();\n20:   const ts = getTranslation();\n21:   ```\n22: \n23: - A component that grows a long list of `if`s and helper functions around data\n24:   has probably swallowed store logic: move it into a method on the store or a\n25:   service, then call it here. Components delegate; see\n26:   [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md).\n27: - Keep the `<script>` readable: store reads, `$props`, a few `$state` fields,\n28:   event handlers, `onDestroy`. If it stops being scannable, split components.\n29: \n30: ## Type props with `$props<{...}>()`\n31: \n32: Props are typed via the runes API. There is no `export let` anywhere in this\n33: codebase; do not introduce it.\n34: \n35: ```ts\n36: let { todo } = $props<{ todo: Todo }>();\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ```ts\n40: let {\n41: \tinput = $bindable(),\n42: \tvalue = $bindable(),\n43: \tplaceholder,\n44: \tonblur,\n45: \tmultiLine = false,\n46: \theight = null,\n47: \ttabindex = null\n48: } = $props<{\n49: \tinput?: HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement | null;\n50: \tvalue: string;\n51: \tplaceholder?: string;\n52: \tonblur?: () => void;\n53: \toninput?: () => void;\n54: \tmultiLine?: boolean;\n55: \theight?: number | null;\n56: \ttabindex?: number | null;\n57: }>();\n58: ```\n59: \n60: - Use `$bindable()` only for props that the parent binds (`bind:value`); plain\n61:   props otherwise.\n62: - Event callbacks are props typed as `() => void` / `(e: Event) => void` — pass\n63:   them through with the `{onblur}` shorthand.\n64: - `let { children } = $props();` accepts the default slot fragment.\n65: \n66: ## Svelte 5 syntax only\n67: \n68: No Svelte 4 idioms. The repo has zero `on:click`, zero `createEventDispatcher`\n69: and zero `export let` — keep it that way.\n70: \n71: - Event attributes, not directives: `onclick`, `onkeydown`, `onblur`,\n72:   `onmouseover` — not `on:click`.\n73: - `{@render children?.()}` for the default slot, `{@render name()}` /\n74:   `{#snippet name()}` for named snippets.\n75: - Lifecycle: `onMount`, `onDestroy`, `$effect` imported from `svelte`.\n76: - No `createEventDispatcher`: either call a store method directly or accept an\n77:   event callback as a prop.\n78: \n79: ## Keep markup declarative — extract conditions\n80: \n81: Markup should read top-to-bottom: `{#if}` blocks for branching, `{#each}` for\n82: lists, `{value}` for output. Non-trivial conditions belong in a function or a\n83: named boolean at the top of the script, not nested inline.\n84: \n85: **Avoid** long or nested ternaries inside class attributes or other markup\n86: expressions. Example of what not to write (found in\n87: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`):\n88: \n89: ```svelte\n90: class=\"{todos.view === 'list'\n91: \t? 'w-9/10'\n92: \t: 'w-3/4'} rounded-lg border-1 border-c-neutral-2 text-sm …\"\n93: ```\n94: \n95: When a class or expression depends on more than a trivially-invertible fact,\n96: compute it in the script and reference the name:\n97: \n98: ```ts\n99: let inputWidth = $state('w-3/4');\n100: // derived from todos.view in a method, or:\n101: function inputClass(): string {\n102: \treturn todos.view === 'list' ? 'w-9/10' : 'w-3/4';\n103: }\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Same rule for `{#if}`: a `{#if}` whose condition spans several `&&`/`||` or\n107: requires a nest of conditions should become a named boolean or an extracted\n108: render-block function. Prefer the guard-clause style from\n109: [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#early-returns--no-nested-short-ifs)\n110: where possible.\n111: \n112: ## Prefer the shared primitives\n113: \n114: Check `src/lib/components/ui/` (buttons, modals, badges, cards, navbars) and\n115: `src/lib/components/forms/` (`TextInput`, `Checkbox`, `Toggle`, `Select`,\n116: `Slider`, `DateInput`, …) before hand-rolling a control.\n117: \n118: - Reuse the existing primitives for inputs, modals, buttons and confirmation\n119:   dialogs. A hand-rolled text input with different classes than `TextInput` is\n120:   a smell.\n121: - Modal/confirm flows use the shared `Modal` primitives —\n122:   `ui/ConfirmationModal`, `ui/ContentModal`, `BottomSheetModal` for mobile.\n123: - When a primitive genuinely misses a feature, extend the shared one rather\n124:   than forking it per-feature.\n125: \n126: ## The desktop/mobile split\n127: \n128: Several features keep separate view variants driven by `Viewpoint`:\n129: \n130: - `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n131:   `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n132: - `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n133: - Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n134:   `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n135:   `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n136: - Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n137:   living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n138: \n139: ## Tailwind conventions\n140: \n141: Styling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\n142: CSS, and dark-mode variants.\n143: \n144: - Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n145:   `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n146:   tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n147:   components.\n148: - Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n149:   mode.\n150: - Class order is managed by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — write classes and\n151:   let `npm run format`/the formatter sort them.\n152: - Use `size-*` utilities for component sizing (`size-6`, `size-4`) instead of\n153:   mixing `w-`/`h-` where a square is meant.\n154: - Conditional classes via the `class:` directive\n155:   (`class:pt-6={IS_DESKTOP}`) — it composes with plain `class=\"…\"`.\n156: - Utility values that repeat across the app (like the input styling on\n157:   `TextInput`) stay in the shared component, not re-pasted.\n158: \n159: ## Icons\n160: \n161: Icons come from `@lucide/svelte`, imported per-icon from\n162: `@lucide/svelte/icons/<kebab-case-name>`:\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165: import IconLoaderCircle from '@lucide/svelte/icons/loader-circle';\n166: ```\n167: \n168: ```svelte\n169: <IconLoaderCircle class=\"size-6 animate-spin text-c-btn\" />\n170: ```\n171: \n172: No hand-drawn SVGs inline, no icon-font classes; the lucide set is the icon\n173: library.\n174: \n175: ## i18n — `ts.get.*`\n176: \n177: Every user-facing string comes from the translation store:\n178: `const ts = getTranslation();` then `ts.get.layout.save`, or\n179: `ts.get.quick_add.commit_success.replace('%s', destination)`.\n180: \n181: - Never hardcode a UI string in a component. `{ts.get.layout.double_click_to_edit}`\n182:   is the pattern (`Title.svelte`).\n183: - All four locale files (`src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`) must stay in sync —\n184:   `npm run check` enforces it (`docs/AGENTS.md` hard rule).\n185: - Use `%s`/`%d` placeholders in a translation string and `.replace(...)` at the\n186:   call site when a value is interpolated.\n187: - Translation keys are typed via `src/lib/types/translation.ts`; an invalid key\n188:   is a compile error.\n189: \n190: ## Local UI state via `$state`\n191: \n192: Component-local, ephemeral state (an open modal, an edit flag, a hover box\n193: position) is a `$state` field — not a store, not a `$derived`-spam:\n194: \n195: ```ts\n196: let changeTitle = $state<boolean>(false);\n197: let titleInput = $state<HTMLInputElement | null>(null);\n198: let explanationBoxX = $state<number>(0);\n199: ```\n200: \n201: - UI-only state stays in the component; anything the route, another component\n202:   or the backend cares about belongs on a store.\n203: - `$derived` only for genuine template-read derivations\n204:   ([`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline)).\n205: \n206: ## Loading feedback\n207: \n208: Wrap store operations in the shared indicator:\n209: \n210: ```ts\n211: loadingIndicator.start();\n212: await todos.changeTitle(todo, todoTitle);\n213: loadingIndicator.stop();\n214: ```\n215: \n216: - `getLoadingIndicator()` returns the shared `LoadingIndicator` store; its\n217:   `start()`/`stop()` power the global `ui/LoadingIndicator` overlay.\n218: - Always `start()` before the await and `stop()` on every exit path. Prefer\n219:   `if (!res) return;`-style early returns with a `stop()` before them, or a\n220:   `try/finally`, so the spinner can never stay up.\n221: \n222: ## Keyboard handling via `KeyManager`\n223: \n224: Global keyboard shortcuts use the `KeyManager` store, registered per component\n225: and cleaned up in `onDestroy`. The pattern from\n226: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`:\n227: \n228: ```ts\n229: keyHandlers.Enter = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Enter', handleEnter);\n230: keyHandlers.Escape = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Escape', handleEscape);\n231: \n232: onDestroy(() => keyManager.unregisterAll(keyHandlers));\n233: ```\n234: \n235: - `registerKeyDown(key, handler)` returns an id; keep it in a local object so\n236:   `unregisterAll(handlers)` can release everything at once, including on blur.\n237: - Never register a handler without registering its inverse for the component's\n238:   lifetime — an orphaned global handler leaks across routes.\n239: - Plain DOM-level keys (an input's own `onkeydown`) do not need `KeyManager`;\n240:   it exists for app-wide/global shortcuts and per-edit-mode hijacks.\n241: \n242: ## Accessibility\n243: \n244: `svelte-check` is configured to ignore two a11y warnings:\n245: `a11y_click_events_have_key_events` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions`\n246: (see the `check` script in `package.json`). That ignore is intentional, but the\n247: responsibility it waives is not: **any clickable non-native element must still\n248: be made reachable by keyboard.**\n249: \n250: - A clickable `<span>`/`<div>` needs `role=\"button\"` and `tabindex=\"0\"`, and\n251:   either an `onkeydown` doppelgänger or a `KeyManager` registration for Enter.\n252:   (`Title.svelte` uses `role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"` for its double-click\n253:   target; double-click itself has no keyboard equivalent, which is why the\n254:   accompanying hover box is not the only affordance.)\n255: - Prefer native elements (`<button>`, `<a href>`) whenever the interaction is a\n256:   real click — they get focus, keyboard and semantics for free.\n257: - Keep focus styles visible (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-d-lightblue` on inputs,\n258:   and `focus:outline-none` only where a ring replaces the outline).\n259: \n260: ## Testability\n261: \n262: The cleanest test targets are props-driven leaves: components that take data\n263: and callbacks as props and render them (dashboard widgets, `forms/Slider`,\n264: badges/counters). They need no context seeding and are covered by\n265: `docs/TESTING.md` §4a/§8's \"Priority 2\". Components that pull stores via\n266: `getX()` but carry real logic (keyboard handling, selection, filtering UI) are\n267: testable through the context harness described in `docs/TESTING.md` §4.3.\n268: \n269: When writing a new component, favour making it easy to test: accept data via\n270: props and delegate mutations to the store either way. Render-only markup\n271: (simple icons, dividers, static labels) does not need tests and should not get\n272: them.\n273: \n274: ## Related docs\n275: \n276: - [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general rules (readability,\n277:   naming, comments, `$derived`).\n278: - [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the stores components read.\n279: - [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — types and i18n used in props/markup.\n280: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §4, §8 — component test strategy.\n\n(End of file - total 280 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Components\n\nPolicy for the UI layer: every `.svelte` component under\n`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**`. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document applies the\ngeneral rules to markup and components.\n\n## Components are lean\n\nA component's job is to render state and forward user intent. All logic lives\nbelow it — in the state store or a pure service.\n\n- Read the stores a component needs **once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">`**,\n  never inside the markup or per-method:\n\n  ```ts\n  const todos = getTodos();\n  const loadingIndicator = getLoadingIndicator();\n  const keyManager = getKeyManager();\n  const ts = getTranslation();","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md","text":"# Components\n\nPolicy for the UI layer: every `.svelte` component under\n`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**`. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document applies the\ngeneral rules to markup and components.\n\n## Components are lean\n\nA component's job is to render state and forward user intent. All logic lives\nbelow it — in the state store or a pure service.\n\n- Read the stores a component needs **once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">`**,\n  never inside the markup or per-method:\n\n  ```ts\n  const todos = getTodos();\n  const loadingIndicator = getLoadingIndicator();\n  const keyManager = getKeyManager();\n  const ts = getTranslation();\n  ```\n\n- A component that grows a long list of `if`s and helper functions around data\n  has probably swallowed store logic: move it into a method on the store or a\n  service, then call it here. Components delegate; see\n  [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md).\n- Keep the `<script>` readable: store reads, `$props`, a few `$state` fields,\n  event handlers, `onDestroy`. If it stops being scannable, split components.\n\n## Type props with `$props<{...}>()`\n\nProps are typed via the runes API. There is no `export let` anywhere in this\ncodebase; do not introduce it.\n\n```ts\nlet { todo } = $props<{ todo: Todo }>();\n```\n\n```ts\nlet {\n\tinput = $bindable(),\n\tvalue = $bindable(),\n\tplaceholder,\n\tonblur,\n\tmultiLine = false,\n\theight = null,\n\ttabindex = null\n} = $props<{\n\tinput?: HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement | null;\n\tvalue: string;\n\tplaceholder?: string;\n\tonblur?: () => void;\n\toninput?: () => void;\n\tmultiLine?: boolean;\n\theight?: number | null;\n\ttabindex?: number | null;\n}>();\n```\n\n- Use `$bindable()` only for props that the parent binds (`bind:value`); plain\n  props otherwise.\n- Event callbacks are props typed as `() => void` / `(e: Event) => void` — pass\n  them through with the `{onblur}` shorthand.\n- `let { children } = $props();` accepts the default slot fragment.\n\n## Svelte 5 syntax only\n\nNo Svelte 4 idioms. The repo has zero `on:click`, zero `createEventDispatcher`\nand zero `export let` — keep it that way.\n\n- Event attributes, not directives: `onclick`, `onkeydown`, `onblur`,\n  `onmouseover` — not `on:click`.\n- `{@render children?.()}` for the default slot, `{@render name()}` /\n  `{#snippet name()}` for named snippets.\n- Lifecycle: `onMount`, `onDestroy`, `$effect` imported from `svelte`.\n- No `createEventDispatcher`: either call a store method directly or accept an\n  event callback as a prop.\n\n## Keep markup declarative — extract conditions\n\nMarkup should read top-to-bottom: `{#if}` blocks for branching, `{#each}` for\nlists, `{value}` for output. Non-trivial conditions belong in a function or a\nnamed boolean at the top of the script, not nested inline.\n\n**Avoid** long or nested ternaries inside class attributes or other markup\nexpressions. Example of what not to write (found in\n`src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`):\n\n```svelte\nclass=\"{todos.view === 'list'\n\t? 'w-9/10'\n\t: 'w-3/4'} rounded-lg border-1 border-c-neutral-2 text-sm …\"\n```\n\nWhen a class or expression depends on more than a trivially-invertible fact,\ncompute it in the script and reference the name:\n\n```ts\nlet inputWidth = $state('w-3/4');\n// derived from todos.view in a method, or:\nfunction inputClass(): string {\n\treturn todos.view === 'list' ? 'w-9/10' : 'w-3/4';\n}\n```\n\nSame rule for `{#if}`: a `{#if}` whose condition spans several `&&`/`||` or\nrequires a nest of conditions should become a named boolean or an extracted\nrender-block function. Prefer the guard-clause style from\n[`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#early-returns--no-nested-short-ifs)\nwhere possible.\n\n## Prefer the shared primitives\n\nCheck `src/lib/components/ui/` (buttons, modals, badges, cards, navbars) and\n`src/lib/components/forms/` (`TextInput`, `Checkbox`, `Toggle`, `Select`,\n`Slider`, `DateInput`, …) before hand-rolling a control.\n\n- Reuse the existing primitives for inputs, modals, buttons and confirmation\n  dialogs. A hand-rolled text input with different classes than `TextInput` is\n  a smell.\n- Modal/confirm flows use the shared `Modal` primitives —\n  `ui/ConfirmationModal`, `ui/ContentModal`, `BottomSheetModal` for mobile.\n- When a primitive genuinely misses a feature, extend the shared one rather\n  than forking it per-feature.\n\n## The desktop/mobile split\n\nSeveral features keep separate view variants driven by `Viewpoint`:\n\n- `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n  `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n- `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n- Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n  `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n  `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n- Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n  living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n\n## Tailwind conventions\n\nStyling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\nCSS, and dark-mode variants.\n\n- Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n  `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n  tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n  components.\n- Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n  mode.\n- Class order is managed by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — write classes and\n  let `npm run format`/the formatter sort them.\n- Use `size-*` utilities for component sizing (`size-6`, `size-4`) instead of\n  mixing `w-`/`h-` where a square is meant.\n- Conditional classes via the `class:` directive\n  (`class:pt-6={IS_DESKTOP}`) — it composes with plain `class=\"…\"`.\n- Utility values that repeat across the app (like the input styling on\n  `TextInput`) stay in the shared component, not re-pasted.\n\n## Icons\n\nIcons come from `@lucide/svelte`, imported per-icon from\n`@lucide/svelte/icons/<kebab-case-name>`:\n\n```ts\nimport IconLoaderCircle from '@lucide/svelte/icons/loader-circle';\n```\n\n```svelte\n<IconLoaderCircle class=\"size-6 animate-spin text-c-btn\" />\n```\n\nNo hand-drawn SVGs inline, no icon-font classes; the lucide set is the icon\nlibrary.\n\n## i18n — `ts.get.*`\n\nEvery user-facing string comes from the translation store:\n`const ts = getTranslation();` then `ts.get.layout.save`, or\n`ts.get.quick_add.commit_success.replace('%s', destination)`.\n\n- Never hardcode a UI string in a component. `{ts.get.layout.double_click_to_edit}`\n  is the pattern (`Title.svelte`).\n- All four locale files (`src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`) must stay in sync —\n  `npm run check` enforces it (`docs/AGENTS.md` hard rule).\n- Use `%s`/`%d` placeholders in a translation string and `.replace(...)` at the\n  call site when a value is interpolated.\n- Translation keys are typed via `src/lib/types/translation.ts`; an invalid key\n  is a compile error.\n\n## Local UI state via `$state`\n\nComponent-local, ephemeral state (an open modal, an edit flag, a hover box\nposition) is a `$state` field — not a store, not a `$derived`-spam:\n\n```ts\nlet changeTitle = $state<boolean>(false);\nlet titleInput = $state<HTMLInputElement | null>(null);\nlet explanationBoxX = $state<number>(0);\n```\n\n- UI-only state stays in the component; anything the route, another component\n  or the backend cares about belongs on a store.\n- `$derived` only for genuine template-read derivations\n  ([`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline)).\n\n## Loading feedback\n\nWrap store operations in the shared indicator:\n\n```ts\nloadingIndicator.start();\nawait todos.changeTitle(todo, todoTitle);\nloadingIndicator.stop();\n```\n\n- `getLoadingIndicator()` returns the shared `LoadingIndicator` store; its\n  `start()`/`stop()` power the global `ui/LoadingIndicator` overlay.\n- Always `start()` before the await and `stop()` on every exit path. Prefer\n  `if (!res) return;`-style early returns with a `stop()` before them, or a\n  `try/finally`, so the spinner can never stay up.\n\n## Keyboard handling via `KeyManager`\n\nGlobal keyboard shortcuts use the `KeyManager` store, registered per component\nand cleaned up in `onDestroy`. The pattern from\n`src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`:\n\n```ts\nkeyHandlers.Enter = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Enter', handleEnter);\nkeyHandlers.Escape = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Escape', handleEscape);\n\nonDestroy(() => keyManager.unregisterAll(keyHandlers));\n```\n\n- `registerKeyDown(key, handler)` returns an id; keep it in a local object so\n  `unregisterAll(handlers)` can release everything at once, including on blur.\n- Never register a handler without registering its inverse for the component's\n  lifetime — an orphaned global handler leaks across routes.\n- Plain DOM-level keys (an input's own `onkeydown`) do not need `KeyManager`;\n  it exists for app-wide/global shortcuts and per-edit-mode hijacks.\n\n## Accessibility\n\n`svelte-check` is configured to ignore two a11y warnings:\n`a11y_click_events_have_key_events` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions`\n(see the `check` script in `package.json`). That ignore is intentional, but the\nresponsibility it waives is not: **any clickable non-native element must still\nbe made reachable by keyboard.**\n\n- A clickable `<span>`/`<div>` needs `role=\"button\"` and `tabindex=\"0\"`, and\n  either an `onkeydown` doppelgänger or a `KeyManager` registration for Enter.\n  (`Title.svelte` uses `role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"` for its double-click\n  target; double-click itself has no keyboard equivalent, which is why the\n  accompanying hover box is not the only affordance.)\n- Prefer native elements (`<button>`, `<a href>`) whenever the interaction is a\n  real click — they get focus, keyboard and semantics for free.\n- Keep focus styles visible (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-d-lightblue` on inputs,\n  and `focus:outline-none` only where a ring replaces the outline).\n\n## Testability\n\nThe cleanest test targets are props-driven leaves: components that take data\nand callbacks as props and render them (dashboard widgets, `forms/Slider`,\nbadges/counters). They need no context seeding and are covered by\n`docs/TESTING.md` §4a/§8's \"Priority 2\". Components that pull stores via\n`getX()` but carry real logic (keyboard handling, selection, filtering UI) are\ntestable through the context harness described in `docs/TESTING.md` §4.3.\n\nWhen writing a new component, favour making it easy to test: accept data via\nprops and delegate mutations to the store either way. Render-only markup\n(simple icons, dividers, static labels) does not need tests and should not get\nthem.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general rules (readability,\n  naming, comments, `$derived`).\n- [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the stores components read.\n- [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — types and i18n used in props/markup.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §4, §8 — component test strategy.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":280,"totalLines":280,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/COMPONENTS.md","time":{"start":1791640285134,"end":1791640285218}},"id":"prt_126152f9a001He9tkxUFtfWQF1","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12615280e0015SRXWCaLo85o3j"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791640285276,"sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_9bGMpt2kesKcdYjmFyUF3219","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/DATA_LAYER.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/DATA_LAYER.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Data layer\n2: \n3: Policy for the non-UI layers: `src/lib/services/`, `src/lib/helpers/`,\n4: `src/lib/config/`, `src/lib/types/`, `src/lib/i18n/` and the app's data flow.\n5: Read [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document is the\n6: detail behind the \"Architecture\" and \"Data flow\" sections of\n7: [`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).\n8: \n9: ## Data flow\n10: \n11: The app has exactly one data flow, and it is one-directional:\n12: \n13: ```\n14: route/component  →  state store (src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts)\n15:                  →  ApiService (src/lib/services/ApiService.ts)\n16:                  →  REST API at {getApiUrl()}/api/v1\n17: ```\n18: \n19: - **All routes are client-rendered.** There are no `+page.server.ts`,\n20:   `+server.ts`, `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts` or `load` functions anywhere in\n21:   `src/routes`. Routes must never fetch data; a route's layout (or component)\n22:   calls `store.load()` in `onMount` and the store does the fetching.\n23: - The root `src/routes/+layout.svelte` bootstraps the app-wide stores; each\n24:   feature layout (`src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n25:   `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`, …) creates its feature stores and\n26:   calls `load()` on them — see [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md).\n27: - Nothing writes to the API from a component. Components call store methods\n28:   (`todos.changeCompleted(todo, checked)`); the store calls `ApiService`.\n29: \n30: ## `ApiService` is the single network seam\n31: \n32: `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` is the only place that calls `fetch` for app\n33: data. It owns Bearer auth, headers, JSON/FormData bodies and URL placeholder\n34: replacement.\n35: \n36: **Never call `fetch` directly for app data.** If you need a new HTTP operation,\n37: use one of the existing methods:\n38: \n39: | Method                 | Verb/route        | Returns on success            | On error      |\n40: | ---------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------- |\n41: | `list(endpoint)`       | GET               | `ListResponse`                | `null`        |\n42: | `get(endpoint, id)`    | GET + `%s`/`%d`   | `GetResponse`                 | `null`        |\n43: | `create(endpoint, body)` | POST + JSON body | `CreateResponse`              | `null`        |\n44: | `createWithStatus(...)`  | POST             | `{ ok, status }`              | `{ ok: false, status }` |\n45: | `delete(endpoint, id)` | DELETE + `%s`/`%d`| `true`                        | `false`       |\n46: | `update(endpoint, id, body)` | PUT + JSON body | `true`                    | `false`       |\n47: | `post(endpoint, body)` | POST + JSON/FormData | `PostResponse`            | `null`        |\n48: | `postWithStatus(...)`  | POST              | `{ ok, status, data }`        | `{ ok: false, status, data: null }` |\n49: | `postRaw<T>(...)`      | POST              | raw typed body                | throws on non-ok JSON |\n50: | `put(endpoint, body)`  | PUT + JSON/FormData | `true`                      | `false`       |\n51: | `postFormData(endpoint, body)` | POST multipart | parsed JSON body (truthy success) | `false`      |\n52: | `uploadFile(endpoint, id, body)` | POST multipart | `CreateResponse`       | `null`        |\n53: | `image(endpoint)`      | GET               | `Blob`                        | `null`        |\n54: \n55: How it works and what callers rely on:\n56: \n57: - **Bearer token** is held on the instance (`authToken`) and refreshed via\n58:   `Auth.updateAuthToken`; headers are built by `getApiHeader*`. Stores use the\n59:   shared `auth.apiService` instance ([`STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md)).\n60: - **URL placeholders:** endpoints containing `%s` (string id) or `%d` (number\n61:   id) are substituted by the method. Callers pass the bare endpoint from\n62:   `apiRoutes` plus the id.\n63: - **Semantics:** `null`/`false` on any non-`ok` response — stores pattern-match\n64:   with `if (res)`/`if (ok)`. A rejected network fetch is a different signal: it\n65:   propagates (or is caught) and never triggers the 401-recovery path.\n66: - **401 recovery** is handled once, inside `ApiService` (`fetchWithRecovery` +\n67:   `setUnauthorizedHandler`), for the app as a whole — never per-store. Auth\n68:   endpoints (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS`) are exempt so a failed login cannot trigger a\n69:   refresh loop.\n70: \n71: Tests pin this seam (`docs/TESTING.md` §3/Phase 2): stubbing `globalThis.fetch`\n72: lets every store test verify the exact method/URL/headers/body.\n73: \n74: ## Endpoints live only in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`\n75: \n76: Every endpoint is a named route in `apiRoutes`, composed once from\n77: `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`:\n78: \n79: ```ts\n80: const BASE_URL = getApiUrl();\n81: const API_URL = `${BASE_URL}/api/v1`;\n82: \n83: export const apiRoutes = {\n84: \ttodos: {\n85: \t\tlist: API_URL + '/todos',\n86: \t\tupdate: API_URL + '/todos/%s',\n87: \t\tupdateCategory: API_URL + '/todos/categories/%d',\n88: \t\t// …\n89: \t}\n90: \t// …\n91: } as const;\n92: ```\n93: \n94: - Store/service code references `apiRoutes.<domain>.<action>` — never builds a\n95:   URL string, never hardcodes a host or path.\n96: - `%s`/`%d` mark the id slots; the `ApiService` methods substitute them.\n97: - The file is `as const` so route names are exact literal types.\n98: - Storage URLs (`API_STORAGE_URL`, `API_USER_STORAGE_URL`) are exported from\n99:   the same file.\n100: \n101: ## Pure domain services — `*Service.ts`\n102: \n103: `src/lib/services/` splits into the **network seam** (`ApiService`) and **pure\n104: domain services** with no I/O:\n105: \n106: - `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`,\n107:   `TodoRelevanceService` — the todos pipeline.\n108: - `LibraryFilterService` — search/filter for all eight library stores.\n109: - `WealthStatisticsService` — finances graph/statistics math.\n110: - `CalendarDragService`, `ImageService` — feature helpers (ImageService uses\n111:   canvas; treat as environment-bound).\n112: - `LocalStorageService` — the persistence seam (below).\n113: \n114: Rules for a domain service:\n115: \n116: - **One responsibility.** A service implements one family of pure\n117:   transformations (filtering, sorting, grouping, scoring). If the name needs\n118:   \"and\", split it.\n119: - **No constructor side effects and no context reads.** Services are\n120:   `new`-able anywhere (stores even default them as fields:\n121:   `filterService = new TodoFilterService()`); they never call `getAuth()` or\n122:   read `$app/*`.\n123: - **Pure functions over plain data in, plain data out** — unit-testable in node\n124:   with no mocks (`npm test`, see `docs/TESTING.md`). Keep types-only imports.\n125: - Naming: `<Domain><Verb>Service.ts`. Methods read as verbs over the domain\n126:   (`filter`, `sort`, `groupByStatus`, `getScoredTodos`).\n127: - If you find non-trivial logic in a store or component, extract it here.\n128: \n129: ## Pure helpers — `*Helper.ts`\n130: \n131: `src/lib/helpers/` holds small, pure, framework-free utilities, named\n132: `*Helper.ts` and exporting plain functions:\n133: \n134: - `DateHelper` (~34 functions: `formatDate`, `getUrlFormat`, `getCalendarMonth`, …),\n135:   `NumberHelper`, `FormatHelper`, `ColorHelper`, `NameHelper`, `CheckInHelper`,\n136:   `CheckInSummaryHelper`, `NavHelper`, `ClickHelper`, `ImageHelper`,\n137:   `MusicTheoryHelper` (+ the `MusicTheory/` directory of pure modules).\n138: \n139: Rules:\n140: \n141: - No Svelte imports, no DOM, no `$app/*`. Pure `(input) → output` functions so\n142:   they run in node tests.\n143: - One concern per file. Shared helpers are imported by services, stores and\n144:   components alike (`TodoFilterService` uses `isDateInThePast` etc. from\n145:   `DateHelper`).\n146: - A helper stops being a helper the moment it touches state, storage or the\n147:   network — that belongs in a service or store.\n148: \n149: ## `src/lib/config/` — one responsibility per file\n150: \n151: - **`platform.ts`** — the platform triplet. `PLATFORM` is `'web' | 'desktop' |\n152:   'mobile'` from `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`; `IS_WEB`/`IS_DESKTOP`/\n153:   `IS_MOBILE`/`IS_NATIVE` derive from it. `getApiUrl()` resolves the API base:\n154:   desktop/mobile → `getCustomApiUrl()` (from LocalStorage via\n155:   `setCustomApiUrl`/`dropCustomApiUrl`), web → `getPwaApiUrl()` which tries,\n156:   in order: `dev` → `http://localhost:8000`, `PUBLIC_API_URL`, then a\n157:   hostname→API map (`app.solyto.de` → `api.solyto.de`, …) with\n158:   `https://api.solyto.app` as the fallback.\n159: - **`features.ts`** — feature flags (`setCustomApiUrl`, `firstStartupOptions`)\n160:   computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n161:   ad-hoc flags to components.\n162: - **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n163:   `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n164:   `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n165: - **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n166:   `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n167:   `<a>` come from here.\n168: - **`themes.ts`** — the theme registry (pure data consumed by the runtime theme\n169:   loading).\n170: \n171: Config files are evaluated at module load; keep them import-light (they are\n172: covered by tests mocking `$env/dynamic/public` + `$app/*`).\n173: \n174: ## `src/lib/types/` — mirror the API, one file per domain\n175: \n176: - One file per domain mirroring the API model: `todo.ts`, `note.ts`,\n177:   `calendar.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `clipboard.ts`, `check_in.ts`, plus auxiliary\n178:   files (`translation.ts`, `api.ts`, `feature.ts`, `platform.ts`, …).\n179: - Type-only imports — `import type { Todo } from '$lib/types/todo'` — keep type\n180:   files out of the runtime graph.\n181: - Two files carry runtime values and are the sanctioned exceptions:\n182:   `src/lib/types/check_in.ts` (tracker/sport constants) and\n183:   `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts` (`CONTENT_TYPE_LABELS`). Everything else in\n184:   `types/` is erased at compile time — if you need a runtime constant, keep it\n185:   in `config/` or in those two files, not scattered.\n186: - Types match the API snake_case fields exactly (`due_at`, `is_completed`,\n187:   `recurrence_frequency`).\n188: - Domain types are used by the store, the components and the `i18n` types; do\n189:   not duplicate a shape elsewhere.\n190: \n191: ## i18n — four locales, typed keys\n192: \n193: `src/lib/i18n/` has exactly four translation tables — `en.ts`, `de.ts`,\n194: `es.ts`, `fr.ts` — typed by `src/lib/types/translation.ts` (`LanguageFile`) so\n195: a key missing from any locale (or a stray key) is a compile error.\n196: \n197: - **All UI strings live in these files; components read them via\n198:   `getTranslation().get` (`ts.get.<group>.<key>`)** — see the \"i18n — `ts.get.*`\"\n199:   section in [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md).\n200: - Every key must exist in all four locales — `npm run check` enforces it.\n201:   When you add a string, add it to `en` first, then translate/sync the other\n202:   three.\n203: - `Translation.svelte.ts` owns the loaded language; `ts.loadLanguage()` is\n204:   called at startup and `changeLanguage()` swaps the active table.\n205: - Keys are grouped per area (`layout`, `todos`, `quick_add`, …) matching the\n206:   interface sections in `types/translation.ts`.\n207: \n208: ## Persistence — `LocalStorageService` only\n209: \n210: The client stores nothing but auth tokens, theme and preferences, all through\n211: `src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts` (typed get/set helpers:\n212: `getJson`, `setBool`, `getNumber`, `destroy`, …; each method guards `browser`\n213: internally).\n214: \n215: - No `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`/cookie access from components or stores\n216:   directly — always via `LocalStorageService` (or `CookieConsent` state for\n217:   cookies).\n218: - Keys are constants next to their owner (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`,\n219:   `custom_api_url` in `platform.ts`), not inline strings.\n220: - Everything else is backend-owned; the API is the database.\n221: \n222: ## Related docs\n223: \n224: - [`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — top-level architecture summary.\n225: - [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the stores that consume these\n226:   seams.\n227: - [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n228: - [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components use types and i18n.\n229: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) — the coverage plan for this layer (Phase 1–2).\n\n(End of file - total 229 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Data layer\n\nPolicy for the non-UI layers: `src/lib/services/`, `src/lib/helpers/`,\n`src/lib/config/`, `src/lib/types/`, `src/lib/i18n/` and the app's data flow.\nRead [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document is the\ndetail behind the \"Architecture\" and \"Data flow\" sections of\n[`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).\n\n## Data flow\n\nThe app has exactly one data flow, and it is one-directional:\n\n```\nroute/component  →  state store (src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts)\n                 →  ApiService (src/lib/services/ApiService.ts)\n                 →  REST API at {getApiUrl()}/api/v1\n```\n\n- **All routes are client-rendered.** There are no `+page.server.ts`,\n  `+server.ts`, `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts` or `load` functions anywhere in","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/DATA_LAYER.md","text":"# Data layer\n\nPolicy for the non-UI layers: `src/lib/services/`, `src/lib/helpers/`,\n`src/lib/config/`, `src/lib/types/`, `src/lib/i18n/` and the app's data flow.\nRead [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document is the\ndetail behind the \"Architecture\" and \"Data flow\" sections of\n[`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).\n\n## Data flow\n\nThe app has exactly one data flow, and it is one-directional:\n\n```\nroute/component  →  state store (src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts)\n                 →  ApiService (src/lib/services/ApiService.ts)\n                 →  REST API at {getApiUrl()}/api/v1\n```\n\n- **All routes are client-rendered.** There are no `+page.server.ts`,\n  `+server.ts`, `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts` or `load` functions anywhere in\n  `src/routes`. Routes must never fetch data; a route's layout (or component)\n  calls `store.load()` in `onMount` and the store does the fetching.\n- The root `src/routes/+layout.svelte` bootstraps the app-wide stores; each\n  feature layout (`src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n  `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`, …) creates its feature stores and\n  calls `load()` on them — see [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md).\n- Nothing writes to the API from a component. Components call store methods\n  (`todos.changeCompleted(todo, checked)`); the store calls `ApiService`.\n\n## `ApiService` is the single network seam\n\n`src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` is the only place that calls `fetch` for app\ndata. It owns Bearer auth, headers, JSON/FormData bodies and URL placeholder\nreplacement.\n\n**Never call `fetch` directly for app data.** If you need a new HTTP operation,\nuse one of the existing methods:\n\n| Method                 | Verb/route        | Returns on success            | On error      |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `list(endpoint)`       | GET               | `ListResponse`                | `null`        |\n| `get(endpoint, id)`    | GET + `%s`/`%d`   | `GetResponse`                 | `null`        |\n| `create(endpoint, body)` | POST + JSON body | `CreateResponse`              | `null`        |\n| `createWithStatus(...)`  | POST             | `{ ok, status }`              | `{ ok: false, status }` |\n| `delete(endpoint, id)` | DELETE + `%s`/`%d`| `true`                        | `false`       |\n| `update(endpoint, id, body)` | PUT + JSON body | `true`                    | `false`       |\n| `post(endpoint, body)` | POST + JSON/FormData | `PostResponse`            | `null`        |\n| `postWithStatus(...)`  | POST              | `{ ok, status, data }`        | `{ ok: false, status, data: null }` |\n| `postRaw<T>(...)`      | POST              | raw typed body                | throws on non-ok JSON |\n| `put(endpoint, body)`  | PUT + JSON/FormData | `true`                      | `false`       |\n| `postFormData(endpoint, body)` | POST multipart | parsed JSON body (truthy success) | `false`      |\n| `uploadFile(endpoint, id, body)` | POST multipart | `CreateResponse`       | `null`        |\n| `image(endpoint)`      | GET               | `Blob`                        | `null`        |\n\nHow it works and what callers rely on:\n\n- **Bearer token** is held on the instance (`authToken`) and refreshed via\n  `Auth.updateAuthToken`; headers are built by `getApiHeader*`. Stores use the\n  shared `auth.apiService` instance ([`STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md)).\n- **URL placeholders:** endpoints containing `%s` (string id) or `%d` (number\n  id) are substituted by the method. Callers pass the bare endpoint from\n  `apiRoutes` plus the id.\n- **Semantics:** `null`/`false` on any non-`ok` response — stores pattern-match\n  with `if (res)`/`if (ok)`. A rejected network fetch is a different signal: it\n  propagates (or is caught) and never triggers the 401-recovery path.\n- **401 recovery** is handled once, inside `ApiService` (`fetchWithRecovery` +\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler`), for the app as a whole — never per-store. Auth\n  endpoints (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS`) are exempt so a failed login cannot trigger a\n  refresh loop.\n\nTests pin this seam (`docs/TESTING.md` §3/Phase 2): stubbing `globalThis.fetch`\nlets every store test verify the exact method/URL/headers/body.\n\n## Endpoints live only in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`\n\nEvery endpoint is a named route in `apiRoutes`, composed once from\n`getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`:\n\n```ts\nconst BASE_URL = getApiUrl();\nconst API_URL = `${BASE_URL}/api/v1`;\n\nexport const apiRoutes = {\n\ttodos: {\n\t\tlist: API_URL + '/todos',\n\t\tupdate: API_URL + '/todos/%s',\n\t\tupdateCategory: API_URL + '/todos/categories/%d',\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n\t// …\n} as const;\n```\n\n- Store/service code references `apiRoutes.<domain>.<action>` — never builds a\n  URL string, never hardcodes a host or path.\n- `%s`/`%d` mark the id slots; the `ApiService` methods substitute them.\n- The file is `as const` so route names are exact literal types.\n- Storage URLs (`API_STORAGE_URL`, `API_USER_STORAGE_URL`) are exported from\n  the same file.\n\n## Pure domain services — `*Service.ts`\n\n`src/lib/services/` splits into the **network seam** (`ApiService`) and **pure\ndomain services** with no I/O:\n\n- `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`,\n  `TodoRelevanceService` — the todos pipeline.\n- `LibraryFilterService` — search/filter for all eight library stores.\n- `WealthStatisticsService` — finances graph/statistics math.\n- `CalendarDragService`, `ImageService` — feature helpers (ImageService uses\n  canvas; treat as environment-bound).\n- `LocalStorageService` — the persistence seam (below).\n\nRules for a domain service:\n\n- **One responsibility.** A service implements one family of pure\n  transformations (filtering, sorting, grouping, scoring). If the name needs\n  \"and\", split it.\n- **No constructor side effects and no context reads.** Services are\n  `new`-able anywhere (stores even default them as fields:\n  `filterService = new TodoFilterService()`); they never call `getAuth()` or\n  read `$app/*`.\n- **Pure functions over plain data in, plain data out** — unit-testable in node\n  with no mocks (`npm test`, see `docs/TESTING.md`). Keep types-only imports.\n- Naming: `<Domain><Verb>Service.ts`. Methods read as verbs over the domain\n  (`filter`, `sort`, `groupByStatus`, `getScoredTodos`).\n- If you find non-trivial logic in a store or component, extract it here.\n\n## Pure helpers — `*Helper.ts`\n\n`src/lib/helpers/` holds small, pure, framework-free utilities, named\n`*Helper.ts` and exporting plain functions:\n\n- `DateHelper` (~34 functions: `formatDate`, `getUrlFormat`, `getCalendarMonth`, …),\n  `NumberHelper`, `FormatHelper`, `ColorHelper`, `NameHelper`, `CheckInHelper`,\n  `CheckInSummaryHelper`, `NavHelper`, `ClickHelper`, `ImageHelper`,\n  `MusicTheoryHelper` (+ the `MusicTheory/` directory of pure modules).\n\nRules:\n\n- No Svelte imports, no DOM, no `$app/*`. Pure `(input) → output` functions so\n  they run in node tests.\n- One concern per file. Shared helpers are imported by services, stores and\n  components alike (`TodoFilterService` uses `isDateInThePast` etc. from\n  `DateHelper`).\n- A helper stops being a helper the moment it touches state, storage or the\n  network — that belongs in a service or store.\n\n## `src/lib/config/` — one responsibility per file\n\n- **`platform.ts`** — the platform triplet. `PLATFORM` is `'web' | 'desktop' |\n  'mobile'` from `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`; `IS_WEB`/`IS_DESKTOP`/\n  `IS_MOBILE`/`IS_NATIVE` derive from it. `getApiUrl()` resolves the API base:\n  desktop/mobile → `getCustomApiUrl()` (from LocalStorage via\n  `setCustomApiUrl`/`dropCustomApiUrl`), web → `getPwaApiUrl()` which tries,\n  in order: `dev` → `http://localhost:8000`, `PUBLIC_API_URL`, then a\n  hostname→API map (`app.solyto.de` → `api.solyto.de`, …) with\n  `https://api.solyto.app` as the fallback.\n- **`features.ts`** — feature flags (`setCustomApiUrl`, `firstStartupOptions`)\n  computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n  ad-hoc flags to components.\n- **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n  `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n  `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n- **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n  `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n  `<a>` come from here.\n- **`themes.ts`** — the theme registry (pure data consumed by the runtime theme\n  loading).\n\nConfig files are evaluated at module load; keep them import-light (they are\ncovered by tests mocking `$env/dynamic/public` + `$app/*`).\n\n## `src/lib/types/` — mirror the API, one file per domain\n\n- One file per domain mirroring the API model: `todo.ts`, `note.ts`,\n  `calendar.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `clipboard.ts`, `check_in.ts`, plus auxiliary\n  files (`translation.ts`, `api.ts`, `feature.ts`, `platform.ts`, …).\n- Type-only imports — `import type { Todo } from '$lib/types/todo'` — keep type\n  files out of the runtime graph.\n- Two files carry runtime values and are the sanctioned exceptions:\n  `src/lib/types/check_in.ts` (tracker/sport constants) and\n  `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts` (`CONTENT_TYPE_LABELS`). Everything else in\n  `types/` is erased at compile time — if you need a runtime constant, keep it\n  in `config/` or in those two files, not scattered.\n- Types match the API snake_case fields exactly (`due_at`, `is_completed`,\n  `recurrence_frequency`).\n- Domain types are used by the store, the components and the `i18n` types; do\n  not duplicate a shape elsewhere.\n\n## i18n — four locales, typed keys\n\n`src/lib/i18n/` has exactly four translation tables — `en.ts`, `de.ts`,\n`es.ts`, `fr.ts` — typed by `src/lib/types/translation.ts` (`LanguageFile`) so\na key missing from any locale (or a stray key) is a compile error.\n\n- **All UI strings live in these files; components read them via\n  `getTranslation().get` (`ts.get.<group>.<key>`)** — see the \"i18n — `ts.get.*`\"\n  section in [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md).\n- Every key must exist in all four locales — `npm run check` enforces it.\n  When you add a string, add it to `en` first, then translate/sync the other\n  three.\n- `Translation.svelte.ts` owns the loaded language; `ts.loadLanguage()` is\n  called at startup and `changeLanguage()` swaps the active table.\n- Keys are grouped per area (`layout`, `todos`, `quick_add`, …) matching the\n  interface sections in `types/translation.ts`.\n\n## Persistence — `LocalStorageService` only\n\nThe client stores nothing but auth tokens, theme and preferences, all through\n`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts` (typed get/set helpers:\n`getJson`, `setBool`, `getNumber`, `destroy`, …; each method guards `browser`\ninternally).\n\n- No `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`/cookie access from components or stores\n  directly — always via `LocalStorageService` (or `CookieConsent` state for\n  cookies).\n- Keys are constants next to their owner (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`,\n  `custom_api_url` in `platform.ts`), not inline strings.\n- Everything else is backend-owned; the API is the database.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — top-level architecture summary.\n- [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the stores that consume these\n  seams.\n- [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n- [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components use types and i18n.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) — the coverage plan for this layer (Phase 1–2).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":229,"totalLines":229,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/DATA_LAYER.md","time":{"start":1791640285213,"end":1791640285268}},"id":"prt_126152fe2001wlrAr8Nnlm0anV","sessionID":"ses_ed9eb3c85ffeyA3hMagC4n6Gru","messageID":"msg_12615280e0015SRXWCaLo85o3j"}}
